{"jobs":[{"id":"1defbc0d-71f7-4c08-919c-4eb49992727d","title":"Sr. Manager, Success Operations","department":"Commercial Operations","team":"Commercial Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T22:15:25.510+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/1defbc0d-71f7-4c08-919c-4eb49992727d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/1defbc0d-71f7-4c08-919c-4eb49992727d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2>About the Success Operations Team</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success Operations shapes how Thumbtack’s Success organization runs. We design the strategies, programs, and processes that help pros and customers realize value quickly and predictably. Our team partners across Sales, Success, Service, Partnerships, Product, Data Science, and Finance to create clarity, alignment, and an operating rhythm that keeps the marketplace healthy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We focus on building reliable processes, defining clear success metrics, generating insights that guide decisions, and driving the cross functional execution needed to improve marketplace outcomes. Our work ensures the Success organization operates consistently, scales effectively, and delivers meaningful impact for both sides of the marketplace.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Sr. Manager of Success Operations to own the strategy, tooling, and process that support our frontline teams across Manual Ops, Partnership Experiments, and the broader Experiments function that serves all of Success, plus the supply health model and levers that keep pro supply ready as more partners come online. You’ll lead a team of senior operations analysts and report to the Director of Success Operations. This role is about bringing structure to chaos: you're comfortable working in a highly entrepreneurial, highly ambiguous, highly versatile environment and building new processes from the ground up, rather than optimizing an already steady-state program. You'll decide where AI genuinely reduces manual load and where a human needs to stay in the loop. You will also shape team capabilities, leadership effectiveness, and talent decisions required to scale this work across Success.</p><div><div style=\"left:0;width:100%;height:0;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%\"><iframe src=\"https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/277e5bc5-1178-4709-9501-c349724e3043/9ebfc4c4-ba71-413c-887c-c09b2f51fcb9\" style=\"top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0\" allowfullscreen scrolling=\"no\" allow=\"encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation\"></iframe></div></div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the strategy, tooling, and outcome goals for the operations behind our biggest growth areas: launching and scaling new partner motions, keeping the supply of qualified pros ready, running the hands-on fulfillment that ensures jobs get matched and completed, and driving the test-and-learn engine that improves programs across Success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the single Commercial Ops liaison to Partnerships, translating new partner commitments and growth spikes into staffed, tooled, supply-ready frontline execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead execution across Success, Partnerships, Product, Data Science, and Finance, resolving dependencies and adapting priorities as partner volume and supply needs change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee the supply health model, dashboard, and levers, directing where to acquire, reactivate, or adjust pricing and job-fit while giving leaders a clear view of coverage, gaps, and required actions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own headcount and capacity forecasting, business reviews, and executive narratives that translate fulfillment and supply signals into staffing plans and actionable directives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the test-and-learn strategy for fulfillment approaches, go-to-market motions, AI-enabled workflows, and automation, determining when to pilot manually and when to invest in scalable solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and evolve a high-performing team of senior individual contributors, and/or operations analysts through strategic hiring, coaching, performance management, role clarity, and team-composition decisions.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years in Customer Success Operations, Marketplace Operations, Revenue Operations, Business Operations, or similar roles, including experience managing senior individual contributors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A background that blends strategic thinking with hands-on operations (for example strategy and operations, management consulting, or a GM or founder role), with a track record of breaking down ambiguous, high-complexity problems and turning them into clear, executable plans.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a two-sided marketplace, gig economy platform, or fast-moving consumer/SMB ecosystem, ideally one that was supply-constrained or required balancing supply and demand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of standing up a new operational motion under time pressure, shipping an imperfect version fast and iterating rather than waiting for a fully built system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quantitative fluency: comfortable enough with coverage ratios, propensity or probability-based models, or similar frameworks to direct someone building one and sanity-check their output yourself.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience shipping an AI-enabled workflow or automation in an operations context, including the judgment to know when automation isn't the right call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and a track record of changing senior stakeholders' minds with data rather than title or authority.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $190,400 - $246,400.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $171,700 - $222,200</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $161,500 - $209,000</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE SUCCESS OPERATIONS TEAM\n\nSuccess Operations shapes how Thumbtack’s Success organization runs. We design the strategies, programs, and processes that help pros and customers realize value quickly and predictably. Our team partners across Sales, Success, Service, Partnerships, Product, Data Science, and Finance to create clarity, alignment, and an operating rhythm that keeps the marketplace healthy.\n\nWe focus on building reliable processes, defining clear success metrics, generating insights that guide decisions, and driving the cross functional execution needed to improve marketplace outcomes. Our work ensures the Success organization operates consistently, scales effectively, and delivers meaningful impact for both sides of the marketplace.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for a Sr. Manager of Success Operations to own the strategy, tooling, and process that support our frontline teams across Manual Ops, Partnership Experiments, and the broader Experiments function that serves all of Success, plus the supply health model and levers that keep pro supply ready as more partners come online. You’ll lead a team of senior operations analysts and report to the Director of Success Operations. This role is about bringing structure to chaos: you're comfortable working in a highly entrepreneurial, highly ambiguous, highly versatile environment and building new processes from the ground up, rather than optimizing an already steady-state program. You'll decide where AI genuinely reduces manual load and where a human needs to stay in the loop. You will also shape team capabilities, leadership effectiveness, and talent decisions required to scale this work across Success.\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Set the strategy, tooling, and outcome goals for the operations behind our biggest growth areas: launching and scaling new partner motions, keeping the supply of qualified pros ready, running the hands-on fulfillment that ensures jobs get matched and completed, and driving the test-and-learn engine that improves programs across Success.\n\n - Serve as the single Commercial Ops liaison to Partnerships, translating new partner commitments and growth spikes into staffed, tooled, supply-ready frontline execution.\n\n - Lead execution across Success, Partnerships, Product, Data Science, and Finance, resolving dependencies and adapting priorities as partner volume and supply needs change.\n\n - Oversee the supply health model, dashboard, and levers, directing where to acquire, reactivate, or adjust pricing and job-fit while giving leaders a clear view of coverage, gaps, and required actions.\n\n - Own headcount and capacity forecasting, business reviews, and executive narratives that translate fulfillment and supply signals into staffing plans and actionable directives.\n\n - Set the test-and-learn strategy for fulfillment approaches, go-to-market motions, AI-enabled workflows, and automation, determining when to pilot manually and when to invest in scalable solutions.\n\n - Lead and evolve a high-performing team of senior individual contributors, and/or operations analysts through strategic hiring, coaching, performance management, role clarity, and team-composition decisions.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 7+ years in Customer Success Operations, Marketplace Operations, Revenue Operations, Business Operations, or similar roles, including experience managing senior individual contributors.\n\n - A background that blends strategic thinking with hands-on operations (for example strategy and operations, management consulting, or a GM or founder role), with a track record of breaking down ambiguous, high-complexity problems and turning them into clear, executable plans.\n\n - Experience in a two-sided marketplace, gig economy platform, or fast-moving consumer/SMB ecosystem, ideally one that was supply-constrained or required balancing supply and demand.\n\n - Track record of standing up a new operational motion under time pressure, shipping an imperfect version fast and iterating rather than waiting for a fully built system.\n\n - Quantitative fluency: comfortable enough with coverage ratios, propensity or probability-based models, or similar frameworks to direct someone building one and sanity-check their output yourself.\n\n - Hands-on experience shipping an AI-enabled workflow or automation in an operations context, including the judgment to know when automation isn't the right call.\n\n - Strong executive presence and a track record of changing senior stakeholders' minds with data rather than title or authority.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $190,400 - $246,400.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $171,700 - $222,200\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $161,500 - $209,000\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6af64bc2-c409-442a-9a61-30b9758d5f34","title":"Customer Service Advocate (Multi-Channel Support)","department":"Service","team":"Service","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T00:19:29.714+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6af64bc2-c409-442a-9a61-30b9758d5f34","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6af64bc2-c409-442a-9a61-30b9758d5f34/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Service Operations Team </strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Thumbtack Service Operations Team brings the Thumbtack mission to life! We focus on providing a great experience to our users by building customer loyalty and helping professionals grow their business. Service Advocates are responsible for managing the user journey by providing the best solution for each individual- both pro and customer. We focus on providing a great experience to our users through consistent, quality, and efficient Email, Refund, Chat, SMS, and Voice support. To be successful, it’s important that our advocates prioritize the most important work first in order to navigate our fast-paced service environment. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role </strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Service Advocate creates user experiences that are simple, valuable, and inspired. They are responsible for making sure that all professionals get best-in-class support whenever they contact Thumbtack Support Operations by addressing their concerns correctly and accurately, you will help set our professionals up for success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain excellent knowledge of Thumbtack’s products and services after completing our training  and onboarding program </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in 30-40 inbound requests through the different channels (phone, chat, SMS, and email) daily with our users to determine the best solution to get jobs done and grow small businesses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Obsess over customers and professionals by constantly focusing on solutions and guiding professionals to maximize their engagement and experience with Thumbtack </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate accountability by meeting/exceeding monthly productivity, quality, customer satisfaction, and resolution rate targets and finding ways to improve KPIs, guidelines, and processes </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a deep understanding of the Thumbtack policies and keep abreast of recent changes and new additions to the policy in order to process refund and email tickets effectively </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute as a team member by engaging in coaching sessions, team meetings, team-building activities, and other team and company events </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-obsessed with an understanding of what it takes to provide a great experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ year experience in a customer service-driven role- BPO, shared services, related industry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a multi-channel (Voice, Chat, Email) environment. Voice experience is a must! Excellent English verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expert de-escalation and conflict resolution skills </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptability and resilience for handling complex interactions and frequent change </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to work all shifts including daytime, mid-day, and graveyard shifts. Must be available to work weekend days and some holidays. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent critical and analytical thinking skills or the ability to assimilate a variety of information and make logical/consistent decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable navigating multiple systems (email, knowledge base, phone, chat, etc.) and getting up to speed quickly with our online tools</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE SERVICE OPERATIONS TEAM \n\nThe Thumbtack Service Operations Team brings the Thumbtack mission to life! We focus on providing a great experience to our users by building customer loyalty and helping professionals grow their business. Service Advocates are responsible for managing the user journey by providing the best solution for each individual- both pro and customer. We focus on providing a great experience to our users through consistent, quality, and efficient Email, Refund, Chat, SMS, and Voice support. To be successful, it’s important that our advocates prioritize the most important work first in order to navigate our fast-paced service environment. \n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE \n\nThe Service Advocate creates user experiences that are simple, valuable, and inspired. They are responsible for making sure that all professionals get best-in-class support whenever they contact Thumbtack Support Operations by addressing their concerns correctly and accurately, you will help set our professionals up for success.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Maintain excellent knowledge of Thumbtack’s products and services after completing our training  and onboarding program \n\n - Participate in 30-40 inbound requests through the different channels (phone, chat, SMS, and email) daily with our users to determine the best solution to get jobs done and grow small businesses\n\n - Obsess over customers and professionals by constantly focusing on solutions and guiding professionals to maximize their engagement and experience with Thumbtack \n\n - Demonstrate accountability by meeting/exceeding monthly productivity, quality, customer satisfaction, and resolution rate targets and finding ways to improve KPIs, guidelines, and processes \n\n - Maintain a deep understanding of the Thumbtack policies and keep abreast of recent changes and new additions to the policy in order to process refund and email tickets effectively \n\n - Contribute as a team member by engaging in coaching sessions, team meetings, team-building activities, and other team and company events \n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Customer-obsessed with an understanding of what it takes to provide a great experience\n\n - 2+ year experience in a customer service-driven role- BPO, shared services, related industry\n\n - Experience working in a multi-channel (Voice, Chat, Email) environment. Voice experience is a must! Excellent English verbal and written communication skills\n\n - Expert de-escalation and conflict resolution skills \n\n - Adaptability and resilience for handling complex interactions and frequent change \n\n - Willingness to work all shifts including daytime, mid-day, and graveyard shifts. Must be available to work weekend days and some holidays. \n\n - Excellent critical and analytical thinking skills or the ability to assimilate a variety of information and make logical/consistent decisions\n\n - Comfortable navigating multiple systems (email, knowledge base, phone, chat, etc.) and getting up to speed quickly with our online tools\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7ddfc7e0-81c6-41a5-9b18-1d8e4470c3de","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Developer Experience","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-08T13:06:03.286+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/7ddfc7e0-81c6-41a5-9b18-1d8e4470c3de","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/7ddfc7e0-81c6-41a5-9b18-1d8e4470c3de/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Developer Experience Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Developer Experience (DevEx) team makes Thumbtack's ~250 engineers more productive. We own the AI-powered developer workflows, cloud development environments, and internal developer platform the whole engineering org builds on. We're small and senior: a four-person team in Productivity Engineering, alongside Mobile Infra, Frontend Infrastructure, and Design Systems Engineering. We partner closely with engineers across the company to find their pain points and ship solutions. You can read more about our engineering culture on the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://medium.com/thumbtack-engineering\"><u>Thumbtack Engineering Blog</u></a>.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building the infrastructure for an AI-native engineering organization, and every stream here is active work today: agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor, backed by a library of skills that encode Thumbtack-specific knowledge; a catalog of Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers that make our internal tools AI-accessible; and cloud development environments (CDEs) built for humans and agents alike. Alongside these, we're modernizing the Web and CLI tooling layers engineers reach for every day. A single improvement we ship can move dozens of teams forward.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the platforms behind agentic developer workflows: roll out the tools the org builds on (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) and ship the skills, plugins, and MCP servers that run across them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build the product surfaces engineers and AI agents reach for daily: self-service workflows in our Backstage developer portal, our developer CLI, IDE integrations, and the framework engineers use to build and deploy their own agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve our Cloud Development Environment (CDE) platform for both human developers and AI agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve the build systems, CI/CD pipelines, test infrastructure, and observability the whole org depends on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prototype and evaluate new AI developer tools as they land, and decide what to adopt, configure, and scale across the engineering org.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience building developer infrastructure, DevEx, or platform tools that other engineers depend on, from CDE rollouts and internal CLIs to MCP servers and build/CI at 100+ engineer scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems thinking: you reason about build pipelines, CI/CD, dev environments, and test infrastructure as interconnected systems, not isolated tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A UX mindset applied to engineering systems: you think in personas, journeys, and end-to-end workflows, and design for the people and agents who use what you build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, and considered opinions about their limits, where they help, and how to scale their use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in the languages our tooling is built in: Go and Python for CLIs, services, MCP servers, and Slackbots, plus TypeScript and React for the web UIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of industry experience in software engineering, including cross-team projects with measurable impact on engineering productivity.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE TEAM\n\nThe Developer Experience (DevEx) team makes Thumbtack's ~250 engineers more productive. We own the AI-powered developer workflows, cloud development environments, and internal developer platform the whole engineering org builds on. We're small and senior: a four-person team in Productivity Engineering, alongside Mobile Infra, Frontend Infrastructure, and Design Systems Engineering. We partner closely with engineers across the company to find their pain points and ship solutions. You can read more about our engineering culture on the Thumbtack Engineering Blog https://medium.com/thumbtack-engineering.\n\n \n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nWe're building the infrastructure for an AI-native engineering organization, and every stream here is active work today: agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor, backed by a library of skills that encode Thumbtack-specific knowledge; a catalog of Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers that make our internal tools AI-accessible; and cloud development environments (CDEs) built for humans and agents alike. Alongside these, we're modernizing the Web and CLI tooling layers engineers reach for every day. A single improvement we ship can move dozens of teams forward.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build the platforms behind agentic developer workflows: roll out the tools the org builds on (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) and ship the skills, plugins, and MCP servers that run across them.\n\n - Design and build the product surfaces engineers and AI agents reach for daily: self-service workflows in our Backstage developer portal, our developer CLI, IDE integrations, and the framework engineers use to build and deploy their own agents.\n\n - Own and evolve our Cloud Development Environment (CDE) platform for both human developers and AI agents.\n\n - Improve the build systems, CI/CD pipelines, test infrastructure, and observability the whole org depends on.\n\n - Prototype and evaluate new AI developer tools as they land, and decide what to adopt, configure, and scale across the engineering org.\n   \n    \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Demonstrated experience building developer infrastructure, DevEx, or platform tools that other engineers depend on, from CDE rollouts and internal CLIs to MCP servers and build/CI at 100+ engineer scale.\n\n - Strong systems thinking: you reason about build pipelines, CI/CD, dev environments, and test infrastructure as interconnected systems, not isolated tools.\n\n - A UX mindset applied to engineering systems: you think in personas, journeys, and end-to-end workflows, and design for the people and agents who use what you build.\n\n - Hands-on experience with agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, and considered opinions about their limits, where they help, and how to scale their use.\n\n - Fluency in the languages our tooling is built in: Go and Python for CLIs, services, MCP servers, and Slackbots, plus TypeScript and React for the web UIs.\n\n - 6+ years of industry experience in software engineering, including cross-team projects with measurable impact on engineering productivity.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d2b3c9e1-01a6-4eee-9742-7ffda6cb4b27","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Developer Experience","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-03T18:21:54.256+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/d2b3c9e1-01a6-4eee-9742-7ffda6cb4b27","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/d2b3c9e1-01a6-4eee-9742-7ffda6cb4b27/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Developer Experience Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Developer Experience (DevEx) team makes Thumbtack's ~250 engineers more productive. We own the AI-powered developer workflows, cloud development environments, and internal developer platform the whole engineering org builds on. We're small and senior: a four-person team in Productivity Engineering, alongside Mobile Infra, Frontend Infrastructure, and Design Systems Engineering. We partner closely with engineers across the company to find their pain points and ship solutions. You can read more about our engineering culture on the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://medium.com/thumbtack-engineering\"><u>Thumbtack Engineering Blog</u></a>.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building the infrastructure for an AI-native engineering organization, and every stream here is active work today: agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor, backed by a library of skills that encode Thumbtack-specific knowledge; a catalog of Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers that make our internal tools AI-accessible; and cloud development environments (CDEs) built for humans and agents alike. Alongside these, we're modernizing the Web and CLI tooling layers engineers reach for every day. A single improvement we ship can move dozens of teams forward.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the platforms behind agentic developer workflows: roll out the tools the org builds on (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) and ship the skills, plugins, and MCP servers that run across them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build the product surfaces engineers and AI agents reach for daily: self-service workflows in our Backstage developer portal, our developer CLI, IDE integrations, and the framework engineers use to build and deploy their own agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve our Cloud Development Environment (CDE) platform for both human developers and AI agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve the build systems, CI/CD pipelines, test infrastructure, and observability the whole org depends on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prototype and evaluate new AI developer tools as they land, and decide what to adopt, configure, and scale across the engineering org.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience building developer infrastructure, DevEx, or platform tools that other engineers depend on, from CDE rollouts and internal CLIs to MCP servers and build/CI at 100+ engineer scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems thinking: you reason about build pipelines, CI/CD, dev environments, and test infrastructure as interconnected systems, not isolated tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A UX mindset applied to engineering systems: you think in personas, journeys, and end-to-end workflows, and design for the people and agents who use what you build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, and considered opinions about their limits, where they help, and how to scale their use.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in the languages our tooling is built in: Go and Python for CLIs, services, MCP servers, and Slackbots, plus TypeScript and React for the web UIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of industry experience in software engineering, including cross-team projects with measurable impact on engineering productivity.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE TEAM\n\nThe Developer Experience (DevEx) team makes Thumbtack's ~250 engineers more productive. We own the AI-powered developer workflows, cloud development environments, and internal developer platform the whole engineering org builds on. We're small and senior: a four-person team in Productivity Engineering, alongside Mobile Infra, Frontend Infrastructure, and Design Systems Engineering. We partner closely with engineers across the company to find their pain points and ship solutions. You can read more about our engineering culture on the Thumbtack Engineering Blog https://medium.com/thumbtack-engineering.\n\n \n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nWe're building the infrastructure for an AI-native engineering organization, and every stream here is active work today: agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor, backed by a library of skills that encode Thumbtack-specific knowledge; a catalog of Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers that make our internal tools AI-accessible; and cloud development environments (CDEs) built for humans and agents alike. Alongside these, we're modernizing the Web and CLI tooling layers engineers reach for every day. A single improvement we ship can move dozens of teams forward.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build the platforms behind agentic developer workflows: roll out the tools the org builds on (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) and ship the skills, plugins, and MCP servers that run across them.\n\n - Design and build the product surfaces engineers and AI agents reach for daily: self-service workflows in our Backstage developer portal, our developer CLI, IDE integrations, and the framework engineers use to build and deploy their own agents.\n\n - Own and evolve our Cloud Development Environment (CDE) platform for both human developers and AI agents.\n\n - Improve the build systems, CI/CD pipelines, test infrastructure, and observability the whole org depends on.\n\n - Prototype and evaluate new AI developer tools as they land, and decide what to adopt, configure, and scale across the engineering org.\n   \n    \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Demonstrated experience building developer infrastructure, DevEx, or platform tools that other engineers depend on, from CDE rollouts and internal CLIs to MCP servers and build/CI at 100+ engineer scale.\n\n - Strong systems thinking: you reason about build pipelines, CI/CD, dev environments, and test infrastructure as interconnected systems, not isolated tools.\n\n - A UX mindset applied to engineering systems: you think in personas, journeys, and end-to-end workflows, and design for the people and agents who use what you build.\n\n - Hands-on experience with agentic developer tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, and considered opinions about their limits, where they help, and how to scale their use.\n\n - Fluency in the languages our tooling is built in: Go and Python for CLIs, services, MCP servers, and Slackbots, plus TypeScript and React for the web UIs.\n\n - 6+ years of industry experience in software engineering, including cross-team projects with measurable impact on engineering productivity.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nNote: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fc9f96bc-bd4e-4883-95a8-91d25833fa35","title":"Software Engineer, AI/ML Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-03-11T18:49:01.835+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/fc9f96bc-bd4e-4883-95a8-91d25833fa35","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/fc9f96bc-bd4e-4883-95a8-91d25833fa35/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Machine Learning Infrastructure Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thumbtack, our challenges span a wide range of areas, including search, recommendations, matchmaking, pricing, safety, content generation, fraud detection, and more. The ML Infrastructure team is responsible for centralizing, standardizing and evolving AI/ML infrastructure that enables these experiences. We empower product engineering teams by providing scalable, high-performance systems that drive AI innovation at scale. To read more about some of the engineering challenges at Thumbtack, visit our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/engineering/\">engineering blog</a>.</p><h2><strong>Challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the ML Infrastructure team, you will work closely with product and platform engineering teams to build and evolve core AI platform capabilities. You will help design and improve systems that allow teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications in production. Your work will directly support AI-driven experiences used by millions of customers and pros across the Thumbtack ecosystem.</p><h2><strong>What you'll do </strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve core AI platform capabilities that enable teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications across Thumbtack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the design, development, and deployment of scalable tools and infrastructure to support the efforts of our applied scientists, including traditional ML model training and serving systems, feature and data workflows, CI/CD, orchestration, deployment, and evaluation tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work hands on across the stack, from backend services and execution infrastructure to integrations with AI models and tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with senior engineers to evaluate next-generation AI infrastructure frameworks and tools that help product teams harness advances in AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive projects to completion with a strong focus on business impact and measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solve complex technical problems and stay up to date with advances in this rapidly evolving space.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1 to 3 years of professional software engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fundamentals in data structures, algorithms, and software design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in at least one major programming language, and the ability to work across multiple languages. Our primary stack includes Go and Python.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with relational or NoSQL databases such as Postgres or DynamoDB.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to use AI coding tools in day-to-day workflows and validate, critique, and refine AI-generated output</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with a certain level of ambiguity, especially when learning and picking up new technologies when projects require it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You operate with a bias to action, quickly learning what is needed and taking decisive steps to move work forward in ambiguous, fast-paced environments.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Expected Salary Range</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $123,300 - $159,500. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE MACHINE LEARNING INFRASTRUCTURE TEAM\n\nAt Thumbtack, our challenges span a wide range of areas, including search, recommendations, matchmaking, pricing, safety, content generation, fraud detection, and more. The ML Infrastructure team is responsible for centralizing, standardizing and evolving AI/ML infrastructure that enables these experiences. We empower product engineering teams by providing scalable, high-performance systems that drive AI innovation at scale. To read more about some of the engineering challenges at Thumbtack, visit our engineering blog https://www.thumbtack.com/engineering/.\n\n\nCHALLENGE\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the ML Infrastructure team, you will work closely with product and platform engineering teams to build and evolve core AI platform capabilities. You will help design and improve systems that allow teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications in production. Your work will directly support AI-driven experiences used by millions of customers and pros across the Thumbtack ecosystem.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO \n\n - Build and evolve core AI platform capabilities that enable teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications across Thumbtack.\n\n - Contribute to the design, development, and deployment of scalable tools and infrastructure to support the efforts of our applied scientists, including traditional ML model training and serving systems, feature and data workflows, CI/CD, orchestration, deployment, and evaluation tooling.\n\n - Work hands on across the stack, from backend services and execution infrastructure to integrations with AI models and tooling.\n\n - Partner with senior engineers to evaluate next-generation AI infrastructure frameworks and tools that help product teams harness advances in AI.\n\n - Drive projects to completion with a strong focus on business impact and measurable outcomes.\n\n - Solve complex technical problems and stay up to date with advances in this rapidly evolving space.\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 1 to 3 years of professional software engineering experience.\n\n - Strong fundamentals in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\n\n - Proficiency in at least one major programming language, and the ability to work across multiple languages. Our primary stack includes Go and Python.\n\n - Experience working with relational or NoSQL databases such as Postgres or DynamoDB.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to use AI coding tools in day-to-day workflows and validate, critique, and refine AI-generated output\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with a certain level of ambiguity, especially when learning and picking up new technologies when projects require it.\n\n - You operate with a bias to action, quickly learning what is needed and taking decisive steps to move work forward in ambiguous, fast-paced environments.\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGE\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $123,300 - $159,500. \n   \n    \n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nNote: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b605d91e-a684-49b7-a8cb-363785f5be84","title":"Product Manager, Pro Fulfillment","department":"Product Management","team":"Product Management","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T14:58:08.599+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/b605d91e-a684-49b7-a8cb-363785f5be84","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/b605d91e-a684-49b7-a8cb-363785f5be84/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Product Management Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team is small but mighty, partnering closely with Engineering, Design, and Analytics to craft a two-sided marketplace that successfully delivers business to our pros while helping millions of customers complete their home projects each year. We have cultivated an environment defined by radical ownership and a strong bias for action, empowering you to move fast, define your own strategy, and drive outcomes quickly. We are outcome-obsessed and strive to spend our time on high-leverage product thinking rather than bureaucracy, minimizing administrative overhead to focus on what truly moves the needle for our users.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager who is driven by autonomy and fueled by ownership. You will be at the helm of innovation and execution, shaping industry-disrupting user experiences that simplify how millions of people confidently care for their homes and how home service professionals grow their business. This role is about defining product vision, challenging the status quo, and driving outcomes that leave a lasting impact on our customers, local service professionals, and the entire home services industry.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transform a vague, ambitious idea into a compelling business and product case, secure resources, and lead execution with clear success criteria.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion deep learnings and insights as a core metric, valuing them alongside traditional metrics to fuel smarter, more innovative product decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive a high-impact initiative from seed to scale, ensuring sustained focus by thoughtfully sunsetting or culling initiatives that do not meet success criteria.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record of launching impactful consumer mobile or web products that users love.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional user-centric thinking with strong user experience and product sense, allowing you to empathize with users and craft excellent experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent analytical thinking and problem-solving skills combined with strong business acumen.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding teamwork and collaboration skills, capable of considering multiple perspectives and driving cross-functional alignment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for articulating complex customer problems precisely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with and strong discerning judgment of AI</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $200,600.00 - $259,600.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $170,900.00 - $221,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PRODUCT MANAGEMENT TEAM\n\nOur team is small but mighty, partnering closely with Engineering, Design, and Analytics to craft a two-sided marketplace that successfully delivers business to our pros while helping millions of customers complete their home projects each year. We have cultivated an environment defined by radical ownership and a strong bias for action, empowering you to move fast, define your own strategy, and drive outcomes quickly. We are outcome-obsessed and strive to spend our time on high-leverage product thinking rather than bureaucracy, minimizing administrative overhead to focus on what truly moves the needle for our users.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager who is driven by autonomy and fueled by ownership. You will be at the helm of innovation and execution, shaping industry-disrupting user experiences that simplify how millions of people confidently care for their homes and how home service professionals grow their business. This role is about defining product vision, challenging the status quo, and driving outcomes that leave a lasting impact on our customers, local service professionals, and the entire home services industry.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Transform a vague, ambitious idea into a compelling business and product case, secure resources, and lead execution with clear success criteria.\n\n - Champion deep learnings and insights as a core metric, valuing them alongside traditional metrics to fuel smarter, more innovative product decisions.\n\n - Drive a high-impact initiative from seed to scale, ensuring sustained focus by thoughtfully sunsetting or culling initiatives that do not meet success criteria.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - A proven track record of launching impactful consumer mobile or web products that users love.\n\n - Exceptional user-centric thinking with strong user experience and product sense, allowing you to empathize with users and craft excellent experiences.\n\n - Excellent analytical thinking and problem-solving skills combined with strong business acumen.\n\n - Outstanding teamwork and collaboration skills, capable of considering multiple perspectives and driving cross-functional alignment.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for articulating complex customer problems precisely.\n\n - Comfort with and strong discerning judgment of AI\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $200,600.00 - $259,600.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $170,900.00 - $221,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3efb1a7b-cfaf-475a-86a9-abff37581b4b","title":"Software Engineer, AI/ML Infrastructure (US-Based) ","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-14T16:12:17.678+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/3efb1a7b-cfaf-475a-86a9-abff37581b4b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/3efb1a7b-cfaf-475a-86a9-abff37581b4b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Machine Learning Infrastructure Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thumbtack, our challenges span a wide range of areas, including search, recommendations, matchmaking, pricing, safety, content generation, fraud detection, and more. The ML Infrastructure team is responsible for centralizing, standardizing and evolving AI/ML infrastructure that enables these experiences. We empower product engineering teams by providing scalable, high-performance systems that drive AI innovation at scale. To read more about some of the engineering challenges at Thumbtack, visit our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/engineering/\">engineering blog</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer on the ML Infrastructure team, you will work closely with product and platform engineering teams to build and evolve core AI platform capabilities. You will help design and improve systems that allow teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications in production. Your work will directly support AI-driven experiences used by millions of customers and pros across the Thumbtack ecosystem.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve core AI platform capabilities that enable teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications across Thumbtack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the design, development, and deployment of scalable tools and infrastructure to support the efforts of our applied scientists, including traditional ML model training and serving systems, feature and data workflows, CI/CD, orchestration, deployment, and evaluation tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work hands on across the stack, from backend services and execution infrastructure to integrations with AI models and tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with senior engineers to evaluate next-generation AI infrastructure frameworks and tools that help product teams harness advances in AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive projects to completion with a strong focus on business impact and measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solve complex technical problems and stay up to date with advances in this rapidly evolving space.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1 to 3 years of professional software engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong fundamentals in data structures, algorithms, and software design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in at least one major programming language, and the ability to work across multiple languages. Our primary stack includes Go and Python.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with relational or NoSQL databases such as Postgres or DynamoDB.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to use AI coding tools in day-to-day workflows and validate, critique, and refine AI-generated output</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with a certain level of ambiguity, especially when learning and picking up new technologies when projects require it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You operate with a bias to action, quickly learning what is needed and taking decisive steps to move work forward in ambiguous, fast-paced environments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $145,400 - $188,100.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $130,900 - $169,400.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $123,300 - $159,500.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE MACHINE LEARNING INFRASTRUCTURE TEAM\n\nAt Thumbtack, our challenges span a wide range of areas, including search, recommendations, matchmaking, pricing, safety, content generation, fraud detection, and more. The ML Infrastructure team is responsible for centralizing, standardizing and evolving AI/ML infrastructure that enables these experiences. We empower product engineering teams by providing scalable, high-performance systems that drive AI innovation at scale. To read more about some of the engineering challenges at Thumbtack, visit our engineering blog https://www.thumbtack.com/engineering/.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nAs a Software Engineer on the ML Infrastructure team, you will work closely with product and platform engineering teams to build and evolve core AI platform capabilities. You will help design and improve systems that allow teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications in production. Your work will directly support AI-driven experiences used by millions of customers and pros across the Thumbtack ecosystem.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build and evolve core AI platform capabilities that enable teams to develop, run, and scale GenAI-powered applications across Thumbtack.\n\n - Contribute to the design, development, and deployment of scalable tools and infrastructure to support the efforts of our applied scientists, including traditional ML model training and serving systems, feature and data workflows, CI/CD, orchestration, deployment, and evaluation tooling.\n\n - Work hands on across the stack, from backend services and execution infrastructure to integrations with AI models and tooling.\n\n - Partner with senior engineers to evaluate next-generation AI infrastructure frameworks and tools that help product teams harness advances in AI.\n\n - Drive projects to completion with a strong focus on business impact and measurable outcomes.\n\n - Solve complex technical problems and stay up to date with advances in this rapidly evolving space.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 1 to 3 years of professional software engineering experience.\n\n - Strong fundamentals in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\n\n - Proficiency in at least one major programming language, and the ability to work across multiple languages. Our primary stack includes Go and Python.\n\n - Experience working with relational or NoSQL databases such as Postgres or DynamoDB.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to use AI coding tools in day-to-day workflows and validate, critique, and refine AI-generated output\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with a certain level of ambiguity, especially when learning and picking up new technologies when projects require it.\n\n - You operate with a bias to action, quickly learning what is needed and taking decisive steps to move work forward in ambiguous, fast-paced environments.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $145,400 - $188,100.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $130,900 - $169,400.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $123,300 - $159,500.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8bd503a6-e1e1-4c4a-80b4-96d1f276b6a4","title":"Applied Scientist, Pro Growth ","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-05-15T19:50:52.907+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/8bd503a6-e1e1-4c4a-80b4-96d1f276b6a4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/8bd503a6-e1e1-4c4a-80b4-96d1f276b6a4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Applied Science Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for applied scientists with deep expertise in machine learning, optimization, building data products, and/or statistical models. As part of a small product team you will have full ownership over your domain, so you should be a person who dreams big, then executes well.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thumbtack, the Applied Science team is responsible for a wide variety of problems spanning AI, machine learning, statistics, and computer science:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Improve customer and service provider matching.</em> Matching and optimization algorithms are fundamental to Thumbtack’s product: we now service millions of matches per week. Identifying better matches between customers and service providers has an incredible impact on the experience of customers and professionals transacting on our platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Model complex relationships in the presence of many confounding factors.</em> Predictive modeling problems are everywhere across our product. Our team works to scope, design and implement machine learning models to support Thumbtack’s product and marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Characterize marketplace dynamics.</em> Thumbtack’s marketplaces consist of thousands of active markets across our service categories and U.S. cities. Via exploratory data analysis and experimental design, our team works to understand trends and behaviors within these markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Build AI features.</em> Use state-of-the-art approaches such as large language models (LLMs), reinforcement learning and agentic workflows to enhance customer / pro experience, increase acquisition and marketplace efficiency, and to automate and enhance internal processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Build a healthy marketplace.</em> We evolve and manage the monetization mechanics of our marketplace, including defining the parameters that affect the prices we charge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack constantly works to balance supply and demand across thousands of local markets and hundreds of service categories. The Pro Growth pod is responsible for the science behind acquiring and activating the right pros, at the right time, in the right markets, to keep the marketplace healthy and growing. As an Applied Scientist on Pro Growth, you’ll build models and experiments that shape who joins Thumbtack, how they get activated, how we forecast supply needs by market and trade, and how we accelerate time-to-value for new pros. We leverage machine learning, causal inference, and optimization to strategically grow and shape our pro supply base. Our work directly contributes to meeting demand projections, unlocking strategic partnerships, and ultimately enhancing customer experience and platform growth by ensuring a robust and high-quality supply of pros.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll work shoulder-to-shoulder with engineers, product managers, and other applied scientists on a portfolio that ranges from incrementality and market forecasting to LLM-powered onboarding agents. You’ll own end-to-end: from problem framing, through experiment design, through deploying models to production, through measuring business impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Initiate and drive applied science projects to completion, with a focus on the business impact of those projects on pro acquisition, activation, retention, and supply health.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, deploy, and optimize machine learning models for supply-side problems, including: lead scoring and pro acquisition targeting, market-level supply forecasting, pro onboarding and activation, retention and churn prediction, and agentic onboarding workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute well-powered marketplace experiments to measure model and product impact on supply and business metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze structured and unstructured data such as marketplace interactions, pro profiles, external supply signals, to identify trends, opportunities, and risks related to supply health.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with engineering, product management, business development, and marketing teams to define problems, develop end-to-end solutions, and ensure successful implementation and monitoring of ML systems in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain the right balance between speed of execution and scientific rigor when designing solutions for a fast-paced marketplace environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to evolving the team’s agentic-first ways of working, including LLM-powered tooling, eval coverage, and the use of AI agents in day-to-day applied science.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Master’s degree in a quantitative field (Computer Science, Machine Learning, Statistics, Operations Research, Economics, or related), or equivalent industry experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of industry experience as an applied scientist, data scientist, or ML engineer with ownership of production ML models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in applied science within a marketplace, supply chain, or growth domain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid knowledge of machine learning techniques such as classification, regression, embedding-based approaches, and causal inference.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with modern LLMs (OpenAI, Anthropic Claude, Gemini, AWS Bedrock) and experience with agentic AI development practices and tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good knowledge of probability, statistics, and econometric methods, including experimental design, causal inference, and optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with large-scale distributed systems (Spark, Databricks, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to effectively read, write, and debug code in programming languages such as Python and SQL.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to break down complex problems rigorously and understand the tradeoffs necessary to deliver impactful projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate clearly and effectively to cross-functional partners of various technical levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to drive seamless execution end-to-end on at least one production ML project.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $161,500 - $209,000 </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE APPLIED SCIENCE TEAM\n\nWe’re looking for applied scientists with deep expertise in machine learning, optimization, building data products, and/or statistical models. As part of a small product team you will have full ownership over your domain, so you should be a person who dreams big, then executes well.\n\nAt Thumbtack, the Applied Science team is responsible for a wide variety of problems spanning AI, machine learning, statistics, and computer science:\n\n - Improve customer and service provider matching. Matching and optimization algorithms are fundamental to Thumbtack’s product: we now service millions of matches per week. Identifying better matches between customers and service providers has an incredible impact on the experience of customers and professionals transacting on our platform.\n\n - Model complex relationships in the presence of many confounding factors. Predictive modeling problems are everywhere across our product. Our team works to scope, design and implement machine learning models to support Thumbtack’s product and marketing.\n\n - Characterize marketplace dynamics. Thumbtack’s marketplaces consist of thousands of active markets across our service categories and U.S. cities. Via exploratory data analysis and experimental design, our team works to understand trends and behaviors within these markets.\n\n - Build AI features. Use state-of-the-art approaches such as large language models (LLMs), reinforcement learning and agentic workflows to enhance customer / pro experience, increase acquisition and marketplace efficiency, and to automate and enhance internal processes.\n\n - Build a healthy marketplace. We evolve and manage the monetization mechanics of our marketplace, including defining the parameters that affect the prices we charge.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThumbtack constantly works to balance supply and demand across thousands of local markets and hundreds of service categories. The Pro Growth pod is responsible for the science behind acquiring and activating the right pros, at the right time, in the right markets, to keep the marketplace healthy and growing. As an Applied Scientist on Pro Growth, you’ll build models and experiments that shape who joins Thumbtack, how they get activated, how we forecast supply needs by market and trade, and how we accelerate time-to-value for new pros. We leverage machine learning, causal inference, and optimization to strategically grow and shape our pro supply base. Our work directly contributes to meeting demand projections, unlocking strategic partnerships, and ultimately enhancing customer experience and platform growth by ensuring a robust and high-quality supply of pros.\n\nYou’ll work shoulder-to-shoulder with engineers, product managers, and other applied scientists on a portfolio that ranges from incrementality and market forecasting to LLM-powered onboarding agents. You’ll own end-to-end: from problem framing, through experiment design, through deploying models to production, through measuring business impact.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Initiate and drive applied science projects to completion, with a focus on the business impact of those projects on pro acquisition, activation, retention, and supply health.\n\n - Develop, deploy, and optimize machine learning models for supply-side problems, including: lead scoring and pro acquisition targeting, market-level supply forecasting, pro onboarding and activation, retention and churn prediction, and agentic onboarding workflows.\n\n - Design and execute well-powered marketplace experiments to measure model and product impact on supply and business metrics.\n\n - Analyze structured and unstructured data such as marketplace interactions, pro profiles, external supply signals, to identify trends, opportunities, and risks related to supply health.\n\n - Collaborate closely with engineering, product management, business development, and marketing teams to define problems, develop end-to-end solutions, and ensure successful implementation and monitoring of ML systems in production.\n\n - Maintain the right balance between speed of execution and scientific rigor when designing solutions for a fast-paced marketplace environment.\n\n - Contribute to evolving the team’s agentic-first ways of working, including LLM-powered tooling, eval coverage, and the use of AI agents in day-to-day applied science.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Master’s degree in a quantitative field (Computer Science, Machine Learning, Statistics, Operations Research, Economics, or related), or equivalent industry experience.\n\n - 3+ years of industry experience as an applied scientist, data scientist, or ML engineer with ownership of production ML models.\n\n - Experience in applied science within a marketplace, supply chain, or growth domain.\n\n - Solid knowledge of machine learning techniques such as classification, regression, embedding-based approaches, and causal inference.\n\n - Familiarity with modern LLMs (OpenAI, Anthropic Claude, Gemini, AWS Bedrock) and experience with agentic AI development practices and tools.\n\n - Good knowledge of probability, statistics, and econometric methods, including experimental design, causal inference, and optimization.\n\n - Experience with large-scale distributed systems (Spark, Databricks, or similar).\n\n - Ability to effectively read, write, and debug code in programming languages such as Python and SQL.\n\n - Ability to break down complex problems rigorously and understand the tradeoffs necessary to deliver impactful projects.\n\n - Ability to communicate clearly and effectively to cross-functional partners of various technical levels.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to drive seamless execution end-to-end on at least one production ML project.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $161,500 - $209,000 \n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nNote: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7b436f4e-e209-4735-bda5-cd32d60fdb4d","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Site Reliability Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-05T21:11:46.880+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/7b436f4e-e209-4735-bda5-cd32d60fdb4d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/7b436f4e-e209-4735-bda5-cd32d60fdb4d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Site Reliability Engineering Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack's Site Reliability Engineering team focuses on creating and maintaining a reliable, secure, and scalable platform vital for a seamless user experience. As a key contributor, you will design and support resilient systems, prioritizing high performance, availability, and throughput, with a focus on minimizing service disruptions, downtime, and latency. SRE impacts Thumbtack’s ecosystem across the entire stack, from linux systems to applications that drive the customer experience. Our work is high leverage impacting how Engineering, Applied Science, and many other teams deliver, run, and observe systems.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Site Reliability team is responsible for a broad set of technologies and systems with expectations to collaborate across the business. We are expected to develop and enhance existing capabilities while ensuring scalability, reliability and resiliency of infrastructure and software. You’ll work with engineering teams ranging from product development, developer experience, and backend infrastructure to collaboratively build Thumbtack’s ecosystem of platform services that have the right impact at the right time. Thumbtack values its cross functional collaborative culture, and you’d be positioned to contribute to the future direction and success of the engineering platform that serves as the engine of our applications.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, create, and maintain software and systems to improve the availability, scalability, and efficiency of Thumbtack's services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the architectural direction of infrastructure and platform services while supporting the engineering organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement tools and processes used for deployment, change, service, and infrastructure management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and debug critical systems throughout the SDLC</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the evolution and performance of capabilities we provide to engineering as a platform organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity planning and demand forecasting, anticipating performance bottlenecks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in rotating on-call duties</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive fluency in AWS and Linux</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to effectively read, write, and debug code in programming languages like but not limited to: Python, Go, PHP, Javascript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in designing, analyzing, and troubleshooting large-scale distributed systems across web technologies like: DNS, TLS, HTTP/S, TCP/IP</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to decompose complex problems while understanding the tradeoffs necessary to deliver impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5 years of experience managing infrastructure and systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrable knowledge of instrumenting, operating, and observing a distributed system of microservices in a production cloud environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate clearly and effectively to cross functional partners of various technical levels</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for reducing toil and improving developer experience</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE SITE RELIABILITY ENGINEERING TEAM\n\nThumbtack's Site Reliability Engineering team focuses on creating and maintaining a reliable, secure, and scalable platform vital for a seamless user experience. As a key contributor, you will design and support resilient systems, prioritizing high performance, availability, and throughput, with a focus on minimizing service disruptions, downtime, and latency. SRE impacts Thumbtack’s ecosystem across the entire stack, from linux systems to applications that drive the customer experience. Our work is high leverage impacting how Engineering, Applied Science, and many other teams deliver, run, and observe systems.\n\n \n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThe Site Reliability team is responsible for a broad set of technologies and systems with expectations to collaborate across the business. We are expected to develop and enhance existing capabilities while ensuring scalability, reliability and resiliency of infrastructure and software. You’ll work with engineering teams ranging from product development, developer experience, and backend infrastructure to collaboratively build Thumbtack’s ecosystem of platform services that have the right impact at the right time. Thumbtack values its cross functional collaborative culture, and you’d be positioned to contribute to the future direction and success of the engineering platform that serves as the engine of our applications.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design, create, and maintain software and systems to improve the availability, scalability, and efficiency of Thumbtack's services\n\n - Set the architectural direction of infrastructure and platform services while supporting the engineering organization\n\n - Design and implement tools and processes used for deployment, change, service, and infrastructure management\n\n - Troubleshoot and debug critical systems throughout the SDLC\n\n - Contribute to the evolution and performance of capabilities we provide to engineering as a platform organization\n\n - Capacity planning and demand forecasting, anticipating performance bottlenecks\n\n - Participate in rotating on-call duties\n   \n    \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Extensive fluency in AWS and Linux\n\n - Ability to effectively read, write, and debug code in programming languages like but not limited to: Python, Go, PHP, Javascript\n\n - Expertise in designing, analyzing, and troubleshooting large-scale distributed systems across web technologies like: DNS, TLS, HTTP/S, TCP/IP\n\n - Ability to decompose complex problems while understanding the tradeoffs necessary to deliver impact\n\n - 5 years of experience managing infrastructure and systems\n\n - Demonstrable knowledge of instrumenting, operating, and observing a distributed system of microservices in a production cloud environment\n\n - Ability to communicate clearly and effectively to cross functional partners of various technical levels\n\n - Passion for reducing toil and improving developer experience\n   \n    \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"334815d3-52e3-407d-9279-691f0397d190","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Site Reliability Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-05T21:11:43.715+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/334815d3-52e3-407d-9279-691f0397d190","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/334815d3-52e3-407d-9279-691f0397d190/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Site Reliability Engineering Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack's Site Reliability Engineering team focuses on creating and maintaining a reliable, secure, and scalable platform vital for a seamless user experience. As a key contributor, you will design and support resilient systems, prioritizing high performance, availability, and throughput, with a focus on minimizing service disruptions, downtime, and latency. SRE impacts Thumbtack’s ecosystem across the entire stack, from linux systems to applications that drive the customer experience. Our work is high leverage impacting how Engineering, Applied Science, and many other teams deliver, run, and observe systems.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Site Reliability team is responsible for a broad set of technologies and systems with expectations to collaborate across the business. We are expected to develop and enhance existing capabilities while ensuring scalability, reliability and resiliency of infrastructure and software. You’ll work with engineering teams ranging from product development, developer experience, and backend infrastructure to collaboratively build Thumbtack’s ecosystem of platform services that have the right impact at the right time. Thumbtack values its cross functional collaborative culture, and you’d be positioned to contribute to the future direction and success of the engineering platform that serves as the engine of our applications.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, create, and maintain software and systems to improve the availability, scalability, and efficiency of Thumbtack's services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the architectural direction of infrastructure and platform services while supporting the engineering organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement tools and processes used for deployment, change, service, and infrastructure management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and debug critical systems throughout the SDLC</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the evolution and performance of capabilities we provide to engineering as a platform organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity planning and demand forecasting, anticipating performance bottlenecks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in rotating on-call duties</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive fluency in AWS and Linux</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to effectively read, write, and debug code in programming languages like but not limited to: Python, Go, PHP, Javascript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in designing, analyzing, and troubleshooting large-scale distributed systems across web technologies like: DNS, TLS, HTTP/S, TCP/IP</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to decompose complex problems while understanding the tradeoffs necessary to deliver impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5 years of experience managing infrastructure and systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrable knowledge of instrumenting, operating, and observing a distributed system of microservices in a production cloud environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate clearly and effectively to cross functional partners of various technical levels</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for reducing toil and improving developer experience</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE SITE RELIABILITY ENGINEERING TEAM\n\nThumbtack's Site Reliability Engineering team focuses on creating and maintaining a reliable, secure, and scalable platform vital for a seamless user experience. As a key contributor, you will design and support resilient systems, prioritizing high performance, availability, and throughput, with a focus on minimizing service disruptions, downtime, and latency. SRE impacts Thumbtack’s ecosystem across the entire stack, from linux systems to applications that drive the customer experience. Our work is high leverage impacting how Engineering, Applied Science, and many other teams deliver, run, and observe systems.\n\n \n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThe Site Reliability team is responsible for a broad set of technologies and systems with expectations to collaborate across the business. We are expected to develop and enhance existing capabilities while ensuring scalability, reliability and resiliency of infrastructure and software. You’ll work with engineering teams ranging from product development, developer experience, and backend infrastructure to collaboratively build Thumbtack’s ecosystem of platform services that have the right impact at the right time. Thumbtack values its cross functional collaborative culture, and you’d be positioned to contribute to the future direction and success of the engineering platform that serves as the engine of our applications.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Design, create, and maintain software and systems to improve the availability, scalability, and efficiency of Thumbtack's services\n\n - Set the architectural direction of infrastructure and platform services while supporting the engineering organization\n\n - Design and implement tools and processes used for deployment, change, service, and infrastructure management\n\n - Troubleshoot and debug critical systems throughout the SDLC\n\n - Contribute to the evolution and performance of capabilities we provide to engineering as a platform organization\n\n - Capacity planning and demand forecasting, anticipating performance bottlenecks\n\n - Participate in rotating on-call duties\n   \n    \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Extensive fluency in AWS and Linux\n\n - Ability to effectively read, write, and debug code in programming languages like but not limited to: Python, Go, PHP, Javascript\n\n - Expertise in designing, analyzing, and troubleshooting large-scale distributed systems across web technologies like: DNS, TLS, HTTP/S, TCP/IP\n\n - Ability to decompose complex problems while understanding the tradeoffs necessary to deliver impact\n\n - 5 years of experience managing infrastructure and systems\n\n - Demonstrable knowledge of instrumenting, operating, and observing a distributed system of microservices in a production cloud environment\n\n - Ability to communicate clearly and effectively to cross functional partners of various technical levels\n\n - Passion for reducing toil and improving developer experience\n   \n    \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role\n\nNote: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"dfa0f7e7-120c-40cc-91e5-43630e061c85","title":"HR Business Partner","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T05:39:16.741+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/dfa0f7e7-120c-40cc-91e5-43630e061c85","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/dfa0f7e7-120c-40cc-91e5-43630e061c85/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the HRBP Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The People Team's vision is to power the success of the business through the success of our people. Our HR Business Partners are business leaders first, HR leaders second. We hold ourselves to a high standard of understanding the objectives, culture, and talent capabilities of our clients. We quickly identify trends and solve problems in service of achieving Thumbtack’s goals, driving high-performing individuals and teams. While we always seek out tangible facts and data, we also believe just as strongly in the intangibles – judgment, EQ, the ability to listen, having an inclusive mindset by default. We strive to be trusted partners and coaches to people at all levels of the organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As our HRBP supporting the Commercial function — Sales, Customer Success, Service, Commercial Operations, Partnerships and Business Development — you'll partner directly with managers and employees across the full employee lifecycle. This role requires working North American business hours (PST Preferred).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be part of a broader HRBP team spanning the US, Canada, and the Philippines, all working together to shape our company’s culture and Future of Work vision. Reporting to the Director, HR Business Partners, you'll bring sound judgment, strong communication, and a bias toward action to the client groups you support. We're looking for someone who's humble yet driven, ownership-oriented, and who can give and receive feedback with grace and authenticity. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Client Partnership:</strong> Partner with Commercial client groups — managers and employees across Sales, Customer Success, Service, Commercial Operations, Partnerships, and Business Development — as a trusted advisor across the full employee lifecycle: team effectiveness, manager coaching, org design, workforce planning and engagement survey action planning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employee Relations:</strong> Support employee relations casework in the Philippines and US — PIP, policy violations, and conflict resolution — partnering with managers to document consistently and reduce legal risk; use sound judgment on when to escalate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Change Management:</strong> Support managers and teams through organizational change, helping drive clarity and alignment during transitions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Excellence:</strong> Support execution of HR programs — performance cycles, calibrations, engagement survey insights — tailored to Thumbtack's needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Data-Driven Decision Making:</strong> Analyze people data to identify trends and translate findings into recommendations for managers and leaders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Culture and Employee Advocacy:</strong> Champion Thumbtack's culture and values within your client groups, leading by example</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Team Collaboration:</strong> Partner with Recruiting, DEI, OD, and Total Rewards to bring integrated People strategies to your client groups</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in HR business partnering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work North American business hours (PST Preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and the judgment to build trust and facilitate tough conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting high-volume frontline or commercial teams (e.g. Sales, Success, Customer Service, Business Development, Commercial Ops) in fast-paced, dynamic environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of performance management (including formal documentation like PIPs and NTEs), employee relations, and change management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort supporting employees across multiple geographies, including the Philippines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data literate — comfortable analyzing people data and translating findings into recommendations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE HRBP TEAM\n\nThe People Team's vision is to power the success of the business through the success of our people. Our HR Business Partners are business leaders first, HR leaders second. We hold ourselves to a high standard of understanding the objectives, culture, and talent capabilities of our clients. We quickly identify trends and solve problems in service of achieving Thumbtack’s goals, driving high-performing individuals and teams. While we always seek out tangible facts and data, we also believe just as strongly in the intangibles – judgment, EQ, the ability to listen, having an inclusive mindset by default. We strive to be trusted partners and coaches to people at all levels of the organization.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs our HRBP supporting the Commercial function — Sales, Customer Success, Service, Commercial Operations, Partnerships and Business Development — you'll partner directly with managers and employees across the full employee lifecycle. This role requires working North American business hours (PST Preferred).\n\nYou'll be part of a broader HRBP team spanning the US, Canada, and the Philippines, all working together to shape our company’s culture and Future of Work vision. Reporting to the Director, HR Business Partners, you'll bring sound judgment, strong communication, and a bias toward action to the client groups you support. We're looking for someone who's humble yet driven, ownership-oriented, and who can give and receive feedback with grace and authenticity. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Client Partnership: Partner with Commercial client groups — managers and employees across Sales, Customer Success, Service, Commercial Operations, Partnerships, and Business Development — as a trusted advisor across the full employee lifecycle: team effectiveness, manager coaching, org design, workforce planning and engagement survey action planning\n\n - Employee Relations: Support employee relations casework in the Philippines and US — PIP, policy violations, and conflict resolution — partnering with managers to document consistently and reduce legal risk; use sound judgment on when to escalate\n\n - Change Management: Support managers and teams through organizational change, helping drive clarity and alignment during transitions\n\n - Operational Excellence: Support execution of HR programs — performance cycles, calibrations, engagement survey insights — tailored to Thumbtack's needs\n\n - Data-Driven Decision Making: Analyze people data to identify trends and translate findings into recommendations for managers and leaders\n\n - Culture and Employee Advocacy: Champion Thumbtack's culture and values within your client groups, leading by example\n\n - Cross-Team Collaboration: Partner with Recruiting, DEI, OD, and Total Rewards to bring integrated People strategies to your client groups\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 6+ years of experience in HR business partnering\n\n - Ability to work North American business hours (PST Preferred)\n\n - Strong communication skills and the judgment to build trust and facilitate tough conversations\n\n - Experience supporting high-volume frontline or commercial teams (e.g. Sales, Success, Customer Service, Business Development, Commercial Ops) in fast-paced, dynamic environments\n\n - Strong knowledge of performance management (including formal documentation like PIPs and NTEs), employee relations, and change management\n\n - Comfort supporting employees across multiple geographies, including the Philippines\n\n - Data literate — comfortable analyzing people data and translating findings into recommendations.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2f4f4be1-49bc-4945-9fef-391c29a41a5f","title":"Growth Marketing Associate","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T09:42:38.927+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/2f4f4be1-49bc-4945-9fef-391c29a41a5f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/2f4f4be1-49bc-4945-9fef-391c29a41a5f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Growth Marketing Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Growth Marketing team at Thumbtack is an important lever of growth for the company, responsible for acquiring and retaining pros and consumers on Thumbtack via SEO, SEM, paid acquisition, and customer engagement channels. The Growth Marketing team is embedded in a larger highly cross-functional Growth org with Engineering, PM, and Analytics resources to help support its efforts.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Marketing Ops Associate who is excited to build out impactful marketing campaigns while developing their technical skills in working with automated marketing tools. As part of the Growth Marketing team, you'll be centrally involved in engagement and sales marketing operations – focused on implementation and execution of email, push and in-app campaigns.  Our team's scope is increasing this year as we start to support the full integrated marketing team so we expect there may be opportunities for this role to take on tasks outside of what is directly described below. We are looking for someone eager to help design, build, and operate world-class marketing programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and execute marketing campaigns across email, push, in-app messaging, and other marketing channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run A/B tests across campaigns to identify key levers of growth that we can scale across the program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help report on the impact of engagement programs, using learnings to iterate and make improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enforce marketing messaging best practices across all channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Creative team to ensure alignment on creative vision and voice across all marketing messaging touchpoints</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Constantly optimize our marketing operations processes for more efficient and seamless campaign deployment</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-3+ years of marketing experience, preferably in lifecycle/engagement marketing or marketing ops</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with ESPs and/or a marketing/engagement automation tool (Iterable or Pardot experience a plus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to pick up new processes and technologies quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent project management and communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Precise attention to detail</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE GROWTH MARKETING TEAM\n\nThe Growth Marketing team at Thumbtack is an important lever of growth for the company, responsible for acquiring and retaining pros and consumers on Thumbtack via SEO, SEM, paid acquisition, and customer engagement channels. The Growth Marketing team is embedded in a larger highly cross-functional Growth org with Engineering, PM, and Analytics resources to help support its efforts.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for a Marketing Ops Associate who is excited to build out impactful marketing campaigns while developing their technical skills in working with automated marketing tools. As part of the Growth Marketing team, you'll be centrally involved in engagement and sales marketing operations – focused on implementation and execution of email, push and in-app campaigns.  Our team's scope is increasing this year as we start to support the full integrated marketing team so we expect there may be opportunities for this role to take on tasks outside of what is directly described below. We are looking for someone eager to help design, build, and operate world-class marketing programs.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build and execute marketing campaigns across email, push, in-app messaging, and other marketing channels\n\n - Run A/B tests across campaigns to identify key levers of growth that we can scale across the program\n\n - Help report on the impact of engagement programs, using learnings to iterate and make improvements\n\n - Enforce marketing messaging best practices across all channels\n\n - Work closely with Creative team to ensure alignment on creative vision and voice across all marketing messaging touchpoints\n\n - Constantly optimize our marketing operations processes for more efficient and seamless campaign deployment\n   \n   \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 1-3+ years of marketing experience, preferably in lifecycle/engagement marketing or marketing ops\n\n - Experience working with ESPs and/or a marketing/engagement automation tool (Iterable or Pardot experience a plus)\n\n - Ability to pick up new processes and technologies quickly\n\n - Excellent project management and communication skills\n\n - Precise attention to detail\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"217678b3-3311-4d21-8339-1cb362ab7d12","title":"Sr. Director, Supply & Partner Marketing","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T19:03:07.651+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/217678b3-3311-4d21-8339-1cb362ab7d12","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/217678b3-3311-4d21-8339-1cb362ab7d12/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h3><strong>About the Marketing &amp; Communications Team</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack’s Marketing &amp; Communications team drives growth on both sides of the marketplace—for homeowners and the professionals who serve them. Pro Marketing is one of our highest-priority organizational investments in 2026, built to accelerate supply-side growth by acquiring the right professionals, helping them succeed on the platform, and keeping them engaged over time. Partner Marketing extends that reach through platform integrations, distribution relationships, and channel programs that create growth opportunities no single paid or organic channel can replicate on its own.</p><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This Sr. Director role leads both Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing at a pivotal moment for Thumbtack. Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing is a new function with a clear mandate: bring the right professionals into the right markets, help them succeed, and keep them engaged long enough to build durable marketplace health. Partner Marketing sits alongside that work, with the opportunity to move from opportunistic partnership deals to a coherent strategy that compounds over time. You will build both functions with direct accountability to supply outcomes — not a separate marketing scorecard.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and own the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing strategy across the full professional lifecycle — how Thumbtack acquires the right professionals in the right markets, activates and onboards them to reach early success, and engages and retains them over the long term</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the voice of the professional inside Thumbtack — building a deep understanding of what pros care about, how they evaluate ROI on the platform, and where their experience falls short of expectations, and bringing that perspective into product and commercial decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and manage the B2B marketing programs that support professional growth: targeted acquisition, onboarding and education, community and loyalty initiatives, events, sales enablement, and marketing collateral</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead Partner Marketing as a strategic function, developing the portfolio of external partnerships — platform integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, and co-marketing — that extend Thumbtack's reach on both sides of the marketplace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with product, commercial, and supply leadership to ensure Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing are grounded in the priorities that matter most to the business and accountable to shared supply growth goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build measurement frameworks tied to professional supply outcomes — acquisition rates, activation, retention — and communicate results and tradeoffs clearly to senior leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop your team, create clear accountability, and foster an environment where strong marketers do their best work</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h3><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience leading full-funnel Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing for a supply-side audience, business customers, or professionals in a marketplace or platform context — with a track record of building activation and retention programs that move the needle on business outcomes, not just acquisition</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building activation and retention programs that go beyond acquisition, measured against business outcomes rather than marketing proxies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">B2B marketing experience, including programs like ABM, sales enablement, and events, with the ability to translate complex platform economics into clear value propositions for an audience that prioritizes ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or managing external partnerships — integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, or co-marketing — and a demonstrated ability to move partner relationships from transactional to strategic</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional instincts: you earn trust by being specific about priorities, clear about what you need, and accountable for outcomes, and you can influence senior leaders without direct authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort building from scratch — the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing function is new, the strategy is still being defined, and you need to be energized by that</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A commitment to defining success in business terms, developing your team, and building an environment where strong people do their best work<strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $332,400 - $430,100</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE MARKETING & COMMUNICATIONS TEAM\n\nThumbtack’s Marketing & Communications team drives growth on both sides of the marketplace—for homeowners and the professionals who serve them. Pro Marketing is one of our highest-priority organizational investments in 2026, built to accelerate supply-side growth by acquiring the right professionals, helping them succeed on the platform, and keeping them engaged over time. Partner Marketing extends that reach through platform integrations, distribution relationships, and channel programs that create growth opportunities no single paid or organic channel can replicate on its own.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThis Sr. Director role leads both Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing at a pivotal moment for Thumbtack. Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing is a new function with a clear mandate: bring the right professionals into the right markets, help them succeed, and keep them engaged long enough to build durable marketplace health. Partner Marketing sits alongside that work, with the opportunity to move from opportunistic partnership deals to a coherent strategy that compounds over time. You will build both functions with direct accountability to supply outcomes — not a separate marketing scorecard.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Define and own the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing strategy across the full professional lifecycle — how Thumbtack acquires the right professionals in the right markets, activates and onboards them to reach early success, and engages and retains them over the long term\n\n - Serve as the voice of the professional inside Thumbtack — building a deep understanding of what pros care about, how they evaluate ROI on the platform, and where their experience falls short of expectations, and bringing that perspective into product and commercial decisions\n\n - Build and manage the B2B marketing programs that support professional growth: targeted acquisition, onboarding and education, community and loyalty initiatives, events, sales enablement, and marketing collateral\n\n - Lead Partner Marketing as a strategic function, developing the portfolio of external partnerships — platform integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, and co-marketing — that extend Thumbtack's reach on both sides of the marketplace\n\n - Work closely with product, commercial, and supply leadership to ensure Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing are grounded in the priorities that matter most to the business and accountable to shared supply growth goals\n\n - Build measurement frameworks tied to professional supply outcomes — acquisition rates, activation, retention — and communicate results and tradeoffs clearly to senior leadership\n\n - Develop your team, create clear accountability, and foster an environment where strong marketers do their best work\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 10+ years of experience leading full-funnel Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing for a supply-side audience, business customers, or professionals in a marketplace or platform context — with a track record of building activation and retention programs that move the needle on business outcomes, not just acquisition\n\n - A track record of building activation and retention programs that go beyond acquisition, measured against business outcomes rather than marketing proxies\n\n - B2B marketing experience, including programs like ABM, sales enablement, and events, with the ability to translate complex platform economics into clear value propositions for an audience that prioritizes ROI\n\n - Experience building or managing external partnerships — integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, or co-marketing — and a demonstrated ability to move partner relationships from transactional to strategic\n\n - Strong cross-functional instincts: you earn trust by being specific about priorities, clear about what you need, and accountable for outcomes, and you can influence senior leaders without direct authority\n\n - Comfort building from scratch — the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing function is new, the strategy is still being defined, and you need to be energized by that\n\n - A commitment to defining success in business terms, developing your team, and building an environment where strong people do their best workExpected salary ranges\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $332,400 - $430,100\n\nNote: Thumbtack uses AI tools to support our resume screening process. However, our Recruiting team’s expertise and judgment guide hiring decisions.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8c584fdf-8f23-40b3-90d6-6cec479f7c8c","title":"Senior Enterprise Security Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T17:45:25.655+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/8c584fdf-8f23-40b3-90d6-6cec479f7c8c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/8c584fdf-8f23-40b3-90d6-6cec479f7c8c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Cybersecurity Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Security Engineering team at Thumbtack is focused on enabling innovation at scale by making the secure path the easiest path. We believe strong security is not a blocker to velocity, but a force multiplier when it is designed into systems, platforms, and developer workflows from the start.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We partner closely with teams across the organization to shape system design, guide architectural decisions, and evolve Thumbtack’s security posture as the company scales. Through collaboration, automation, and thoughtful tradeoffs, we help ensure Thumbtack can ship fast, innovate boldly, and maintain customer trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI is reshaping how work gets done at Thumbtack. Employees leverage AI assistants in their daily work and teams are building autonomous agents that act on their behalf - reading data, calling APIs, and making changes across enterprise systems. This introduces changes in the risk landscape. Identities now belong to agents and services as often as to people. Protocols like MCP are opening new pathways between AI and enterprise data. And the pipelines feeding AI systems cross more services, vendors, and trust boundaries than they have previously.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The challenge is to evolve security controls to address these shifts in the technology and risk landscape driven by AI-adoption: hardening IAM for non-human and delegated identities, defining safe defaults for MCP servers and autonomous agents, and securing the data pipelines that feed AI systems. We package these controls as secure defaults, paved paths, and reusable patterns so teams can adopt them with confidence. The goal is straightforward — keep Thumbtack moving fast on AI while keeping customer and employee data protected.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role focuses on improving AI-adjacent security at Thumbtack, including the agents, identities, integrations, and data pipelines that modern AI systems depend on. It also covers broader security engineering work across the enterprise platforms and services that support them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver high-quality security assessments and threat models for first-party and third-party AI tools, agents, and AI-integrated systems, ensuring they adhere to enterprise security principles and approved patterns, with sound authentication, authorization, data access, and observability by design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and validate technical guardrails and reusable patterns that keep AI usage safe at Thumbtack. This spans AI behavior (safe defaults for agent actions, tool and permission scoping, human-in-the-loop boundaries for sensitive access, input and output controls, audit and observability) and AI connectivity (MCP servers, integrations, trust boundaries, and the data pipelines that feed first- and third-party AI systems). Contribute to the frameworks and tooling that support secure AI development and use across Thumbtack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harden IAM across the enterprise, with particular focus on the non-human and delegated identities behind AI systems (service accounts, agent credentials, SaaS-to-SaaS OAuth, and SCIM federation). Bring least-privilege and lifecycle hygiene to identities that increasingly act at machine speed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide broader security engineering support across Thumbtack's enterprise platforms and services, including SaaS security and posture management, third-party and integration security, data governance, endpoint security, and identity-centric controls. Build paved paths, shared tooling, and automation that scale these controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional security initiatives end-to-end. Partner with IT, Engineering, Legal, Privacy, Procurement, and business stakeholders to surface risk early, set clear requirements, and support scalable adoption of secure patterns. Conduct security design and architecture reviews for enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, and internally developed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers and partner-team members, raising the overall security bar through guidance and example.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support security incident response and drive learning through post-incident analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in security engineering, enterprise security, application security, cloud security, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing threat models and proposing technical guardrails for AI tooling and agentic systems, including non-human identities, tool/permission scoping, and safe defaults for agent behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in modern enterprise security disciplines: authentication and authorization (SSO, OAuth/OIDC, SAML, federation, SCIM), API security and token handling, secrets management, least-privilege design, SaaS security and posture management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience evaluating risk and conducting security design and architecture reviews across enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, integrations, and internally developed systems, including evaluating data flows, third-party integrations, trust boundaries, automation platforms, AI-connected workflows, and emerging integration patterns such as MCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience securing modern, cloud-native systems (AWS and/or GCP) and familiarity with core control domains such as audit logging, encryption, access control, data retention, and incident response.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sense of ownership and accountability, balancing hands-on technical execution with the ability to mentor others, raise standards, and drive measurable improvements in enterprise security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence without authority and translate technical risk into clear requirements and actionable guidance for both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE CYBERSECURITY TEAM\n\nThe Security Engineering team at Thumbtack is focused on enabling innovation at scale by making the secure path the easiest path. We believe strong security is not a blocker to velocity, but a force multiplier when it is designed into systems, platforms, and developer workflows from the start.\n\nWe partner closely with teams across the organization to shape system design, guide architectural decisions, and evolve Thumbtack’s security posture as the company scales. Through collaboration, automation, and thoughtful tradeoffs, we help ensure Thumbtack can ship fast, innovate boldly, and maintain customer trust.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nAI is reshaping how work gets done at Thumbtack. Employees leverage AI assistants in their daily work and teams are building autonomous agents that act on their behalf - reading data, calling APIs, and making changes across enterprise systems. This introduces changes in the risk landscape. Identities now belong to agents and services as often as to people. Protocols like MCP are opening new pathways between AI and enterprise data. And the pipelines feeding AI systems cross more services, vendors, and trust boundaries than they have previously.\n\nThe challenge is to evolve security controls to address these shifts in the technology and risk landscape driven by AI-adoption: hardening IAM for non-human and delegated identities, defining safe defaults for MCP servers and autonomous agents, and securing the data pipelines that feed AI systems. We package these controls as secure defaults, paved paths, and reusable patterns so teams can adopt them with confidence. The goal is straightforward — keep Thumbtack moving fast on AI while keeping customer and employee data protected.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - This role focuses on improving AI-adjacent security at Thumbtack, including the agents, identities, integrations, and data pipelines that modern AI systems depend on. It also covers broader security engineering work across the enterprise platforms and services that support them.\n\n - Deliver high-quality security assessments and threat models for first-party and third-party AI tools, agents, and AI-integrated systems, ensuring they adhere to enterprise security principles and approved patterns, with sound authentication, authorization, data access, and observability by design.\n\n - Design and validate technical guardrails and reusable patterns that keep AI usage safe at Thumbtack. This spans AI behavior (safe defaults for agent actions, tool and permission scoping, human-in-the-loop boundaries for sensitive access, input and output controls, audit and observability) and AI connectivity (MCP servers, integrations, trust boundaries, and the data pipelines that feed first- and third-party AI systems). Contribute to the frameworks and tooling that support secure AI development and use across Thumbtack.\n\n - Harden IAM across the enterprise, with particular focus on the non-human and delegated identities behind AI systems (service accounts, agent credentials, SaaS-to-SaaS OAuth, and SCIM federation). Bring least-privilege and lifecycle hygiene to identities that increasingly act at machine speed.\n\n - Provide broader security engineering support across Thumbtack's enterprise platforms and services, including SaaS security and posture management, third-party and integration security, data governance, endpoint security, and identity-centric controls. Build paved paths, shared tooling, and automation that scale these controls.\n\n - Lead cross-functional security initiatives end-to-end. Partner with IT, Engineering, Legal, Privacy, Procurement, and business stakeholders to surface risk early, set clear requirements, and support scalable adoption of secure patterns. Conduct security design and architecture reviews for enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, and internally developed systems.\n\n - Mentor engineers and partner-team members, raising the overall security bar through guidance and example.\n\n - Support security incident response and drive learning through post-incident analysis.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 6+ years of experience in security engineering, enterprise security, application security, cloud security, or a related field.\n\n - Experience developing threat models and proposing technical guardrails for AI tooling and agentic systems, including non-human identities, tool/permission scoping, and safe defaults for agent behavior.\n\n - Deep expertise in modern enterprise security disciplines: authentication and authorization (SSO, OAuth/OIDC, SAML, federation, SCIM), API security and token handling, secrets management, least-privilege design, SaaS security and posture management.\n\n - Strong experience evaluating risk and conducting security design and architecture reviews across enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, integrations, and internally developed systems, including evaluating data flows, third-party integrations, trust boundaries, automation platforms, AI-connected workflows, and emerging integration patterns such as MCP.\n\n - Strong experience securing modern, cloud-native systems (AWS and/or GCP) and familiarity with core control domains such as audit logging, encryption, access control, data retention, and incident response.\n\n - Strong sense of ownership and accountability, balancing hands-on technical execution with the ability to mentor others, raise standards, and drive measurable improvements in enterprise security.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence without authority and translate technical risk into clear requirements and actionable guidance for both technical and non-technical audiences.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4f88b69b-8870-4e63-bc72-133214104aab","title":"Senior Enterprise Security Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T17:45:31.647+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/4f88b69b-8870-4e63-bc72-133214104aab","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/4f88b69b-8870-4e63-bc72-133214104aab/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Cybersecurity Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Security Engineering team at Thumbtack is focused on enabling innovation at scale by making the secure path the easiest path. We believe strong security is not a blocker to velocity, but a force multiplier when it is designed into systems, platforms, and developer workflows from the start.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We partner closely with teams across the organization to shape system design, guide architectural decisions, and evolve Thumbtack’s security posture as the company scales. Through collaboration, automation, and thoughtful tradeoffs, we help ensure Thumbtack can ship fast, innovate boldly, and maintain customer trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI is reshaping how work gets done at Thumbtack. Employees leverage AI assistants in their daily work and teams are building autonomous agents that act on their behalf - reading data, calling APIs, and making changes across enterprise systems. This introduces changes in the risk landscape. Identities now belong to agents and services as often as to people. Protocols like MCP are opening new pathways between AI and enterprise data. And the pipelines feeding AI systems cross more services, vendors, and trust boundaries than they have previously.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The challenge is to evolve security controls to address these shifts in the technology and risk landscape driven by AI-adoption: hardening IAM for non-human and delegated identities, defining safe defaults for MCP servers and autonomous agents, and securing the data pipelines that feed AI systems. We package these controls as secure defaults, paved paths, and reusable patterns so teams can adopt them with confidence. The goal is straightforward — keep Thumbtack moving fast on AI while keeping customer and employee data protected.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role focuses on improving AI-adjacent security at Thumbtack, including the agents, identities, integrations, and data pipelines that modern AI systems depend on. It also covers broader security engineering work across the enterprise platforms and services that support them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver high-quality security assessments and threat models for first-party and third-party AI tools, agents, and AI-integrated systems, ensuring they adhere to enterprise security principles and approved patterns, with sound authentication, authorization, data access, and observability by design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and validate technical guardrails and reusable patterns that keep AI usage safe at Thumbtack. This spans AI behavior (safe defaults for agent actions, tool and permission scoping, human-in-the-loop boundaries for sensitive access, input and output controls, audit and observability) and AI connectivity (MCP servers, integrations, trust boundaries, and the data pipelines that feed first- and third-party AI systems). Contribute to the frameworks and tooling that support secure AI development and use across Thumbtack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Harden IAM across the enterprise, with particular focus on the non-human and delegated identities behind AI systems (service accounts, agent credentials, SaaS-to-SaaS OAuth, and SCIM federation). Bring least-privilege and lifecycle hygiene to identities that increasingly act at machine speed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide broader security engineering support across Thumbtack's enterprise platforms and services, including SaaS security and posture management, third-party and integration security, data governance, endpoint security, and identity-centric controls. Build paved paths, shared tooling, and automation that scale these controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional security initiatives end-to-end. Partner with IT, Engineering, Legal, Privacy, Procurement, and business stakeholders to surface risk early, set clear requirements, and support scalable adoption of secure patterns. Conduct security design and architecture reviews for enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, and internally developed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers and partner-team members, raising the overall security bar through guidance and example.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support security incident response and drive learning through post-incident analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in security engineering, enterprise security, application security, cloud security, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing threat models and proposing technical guardrails for AI tooling and agentic systems, including non-human identities, tool/permission scoping, and safe defaults for agent behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in modern enterprise security disciplines: authentication and authorization (SSO, OAuth/OIDC, SAML, federation, SCIM), API security and token handling, secrets management, least-privilege design, SaaS security and posture management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience evaluating risk and conducting security design and architecture reviews across enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, integrations, and internally developed systems, including evaluating data flows, third-party integrations, trust boundaries, automation platforms, AI-connected workflows, and emerging integration patterns such as MCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience securing modern, cloud-native systems (AWS and/or GCP) and familiarity with core control domains such as audit logging, encryption, access control, data retention, and incident response.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sense of ownership and accountability, balancing hands-on technical execution with the ability to mentor others, raise standards, and drive measurable improvements in enterprise security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence without authority and translate technical risk into clear requirements and actionable guidance for both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE CYBERSECURITY TEAM\n\nThe Security Engineering team at Thumbtack is focused on enabling innovation at scale by making the secure path the easiest path. We believe strong security is not a blocker to velocity, but a force multiplier when it is designed into systems, platforms, and developer workflows from the start.\n\nWe partner closely with teams across the organization to shape system design, guide architectural decisions, and evolve Thumbtack’s security posture as the company scales. Through collaboration, automation, and thoughtful tradeoffs, we help ensure Thumbtack can ship fast, innovate boldly, and maintain customer trust.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nAI is reshaping how work gets done at Thumbtack. Employees leverage AI assistants in their daily work and teams are building autonomous agents that act on their behalf - reading data, calling APIs, and making changes across enterprise systems. This introduces changes in the risk landscape. Identities now belong to agents and services as often as to people. Protocols like MCP are opening new pathways between AI and enterprise data. And the pipelines feeding AI systems cross more services, vendors, and trust boundaries than they have previously.\n\nThe challenge is to evolve security controls to address these shifts in the technology and risk landscape driven by AI-adoption: hardening IAM for non-human and delegated identities, defining safe defaults for MCP servers and autonomous agents, and securing the data pipelines that feed AI systems. We package these controls as secure defaults, paved paths, and reusable patterns so teams can adopt them with confidence. The goal is straightforward — keep Thumbtack moving fast on AI while keeping customer and employee data protected.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - This role focuses on improving AI-adjacent security at Thumbtack, including the agents, identities, integrations, and data pipelines that modern AI systems depend on. It also covers broader security engineering work across the enterprise platforms and services that support them.\n\n - Deliver high-quality security assessments and threat models for first-party and third-party AI tools, agents, and AI-integrated systems, ensuring they adhere to enterprise security principles and approved patterns, with sound authentication, authorization, data access, and observability by design.\n\n - Design and validate technical guardrails and reusable patterns that keep AI usage safe at Thumbtack. This spans AI behavior (safe defaults for agent actions, tool and permission scoping, human-in-the-loop boundaries for sensitive access, input and output controls, audit and observability) and AI connectivity (MCP servers, integrations, trust boundaries, and the data pipelines that feed first- and third-party AI systems). Contribute to the frameworks and tooling that support secure AI development and use across Thumbtack.\n\n - Harden IAM across the enterprise, with particular focus on the non-human and delegated identities behind AI systems (service accounts, agent credentials, SaaS-to-SaaS OAuth, and SCIM federation). Bring least-privilege and lifecycle hygiene to identities that increasingly act at machine speed.\n\n - Provide broader security engineering support across Thumbtack's enterprise platforms and services, including SaaS security and posture management, third-party and integration security, data governance, endpoint security, and identity-centric controls. Build paved paths, shared tooling, and automation that scale these controls.\n\n - Lead cross-functional security initiatives end-to-end. Partner with IT, Engineering, Legal, Privacy, Procurement, and business stakeholders to surface risk early, set clear requirements, and support scalable adoption of secure patterns. Conduct security design and architecture reviews for enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, and internally developed systems.\n\n - Mentor engineers and partner-team members, raising the overall security bar through guidance and example.\n\n - Support security incident response and drive learning through post-incident analysis.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 6+ years of experience in security engineering, enterprise security, application security, cloud security, or a related field.\n\n - Experience developing threat models and proposing technical guardrails for AI tooling and agentic systems, including non-human identities, tool/permission scoping, and safe defaults for agent behavior.\n\n - Deep expertise in modern enterprise security disciplines: authentication and authorization (SSO, OAuth/OIDC, SAML, federation, SCIM), API security and token handling, secrets management, least-privilege design, SaaS security and posture management.\n\n - Strong experience evaluating risk and conducting security design and architecture reviews across enterprise applications, SaaS platforms, integrations, and internally developed systems, including evaluating data flows, third-party integrations, trust boundaries, automation platforms, AI-connected workflows, and emerging integration patterns such as MCP.\n\n - Strong experience securing modern, cloud-native systems (AWS and/or GCP) and familiarity with core control domains such as audit logging, encryption, access control, data retention, and incident response.\n\n - Strong sense of ownership and accountability, balancing hands-on technical execution with the ability to mentor others, raise standards, and drive measurable improvements in enterprise security.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence without authority and translate technical risk into clear requirements and actionable guidance for both technical and non-technical audiences.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f4df4258-d7cb-45fb-a1d4-c1504e08ff14","title":"Account Executive","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T05:36:56.931+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/f4df4258-d7cb-45fb-a1d4-c1504e08ff14","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/f4df4258-d7cb-45fb-a1d4-c1504e08ff14/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Sales Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Sales team directly impacts the growth of the company by acquiring high quality + high capacity new professionals who will provide an amazing experience for our customers. Our sales approach drives product comprehension, pro retention, and generates a much higher ROI for the pro vs. pros who self-serve signup. We are a growing sales organization, currently looking for highly motivated leaders who want to be a part of scaling our Sales org.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Account Executives will directly impact the company's overall growth by finding new pros, surfacing learnings from sales conversations, testing new data sources and sales processes, improving the quality and quantity of pros on Thumbtack, and driving revenue for the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsible for driving revenue by obtaining quota by creating and managing your pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate and current notes and records for all accounts in Salesforce.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieving 100% of your assigned monthly quota while creating and cultivating a future sales pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help key stakeholders gain insight into their market, customers, and competitors which will allow them to make quicker and better data-driven decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become an expert in the Thumbtack product and clearly articulate why every business professional needs the product as part of their business plan.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You understand that your highest priority is closing sales &amp; driving revenue; history of carrying a quota</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have a collaborative attitude to share techniques and success with the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in high-call volume sales </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have 2+ years of sales experience </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prospecting and Pipeline Management experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE SALES TEAM\n\nThe Sales team directly impacts the growth of the company by acquiring high quality + high capacity new professionals who will provide an amazing experience for our customers. Our sales approach drives product comprehension, pro retention, and generates a much higher ROI for the pro vs. pros who self-serve signup. We are a growing sales organization, currently looking for highly motivated leaders who want to be a part of scaling our Sales org.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAccount Executives will directly impact the company's overall growth by finding new pros, surfacing learnings from sales conversations, testing new data sources and sales processes, improving the quality and quantity of pros on Thumbtack, and driving revenue for the company.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Responsible for driving revenue by obtaining quota by creating and managing your pipeline.\n\n - Maintain accurate and current notes and records for all accounts in Salesforce.\n\n - Achieving 100% of your assigned monthly quota while creating and cultivating a future sales pipeline.\n\n - Help key stakeholders gain insight into their market, customers, and competitors which will allow them to make quicker and better data-driven decisions.\n\n - Become an expert in the Thumbtack product and clearly articulate why every business professional needs the product as part of their business plan.\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - You understand that your highest priority is closing sales & driving revenue; history of carrying a quota\n\n - Have a collaborative attitude to share techniques and success with the team\n\n - Experience in high-call volume sales \n\n - Must have 2+ years of sales experience \n\n - Prospecting and Pipeline Management experience\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a8c9ee4d-d5b9-4209-87b7-3e5c7dfa6222","title":"Product Manager, Growth","department":"Product Management","team":"Product Management","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-07T16:20:17.629+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":null,"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/a8c9ee4d-d5b9-4209-87b7-3e5c7dfa6222","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/a8c9ee4d-d5b9-4209-87b7-3e5c7dfa6222/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Product Management Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our team is small but mighty, partnering closely with Engineering, Design, and Analytics to craft a two-sided marketplace that successfully delivers business to our pros while helping millions of customers complete their home projects each year. We have cultivated an environment defined by radical ownership and a strong bias for action, empowering you to move fast, define your own strategy, and drive outcomes quickly. We are outcome-obsessed and strive to spend our time on high-leverage product thinking rather than bureaucracy, minimizing administrative overhead to focus on what truly moves the needle for our users.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager who is driven by autonomy and fueled by ownership. You will be at the helm of innovation and execution, shaping industry-disrupting user experiences that simplify how millions of people confidently care for their homes and how home service professionals grow their business. This role is about defining product vision, challenging the status quo, and driving outcomes that leave a lasting impact on our customers, local service professionals, and the entire home services industry.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a PM on the Growth team at Thumbtack you will be responsible for driving customer and pro lifetime value by creating product solutions for homeowners and home-service professionals to accomplish their goals with ease and confidence. You will be responsible for building new 0 to 1 product experiences as well as optimizing existing products to drive more user repeat and growth.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead a significant portion of our product experience and be accountable for business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct user research and lightweight tests to scope and prioritize product initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transform a vague, ambitious idea into a compelling business and product case, secure resources, and lead execution with clear success criteria.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion deep learnings and insights as a core metric, valuing them alongside traditional metrics to fuel smarter, more innovative product decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with marketing, engineers, designers, data and applied scientists to ideate, prioritize and deliver great solutions for our customers and professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate within your team and among teams at Thumbtack to ensure understanding of and alignment around projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive a high-impact initiative from seed to scale, ensuring sustained focus by thoughtfully sunsetting or culling initiatives that do not meet success criteria.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of product management experience with a proven track record of launching impactful consumer web or mobile products that users love.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent user-centric thinking with strong user experience and product sense, allowing you to empathize with users and craft excellent experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent analytical thinking and problem-solving skills combined with strong business acumen.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding teamwork and collaboration skills, capable of considering multiple perspectives and driving cross-functional alignment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for articulating complex customer problems precisely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with and strong discerning judgment of AI.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $200,600.00 - $259,600.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $170,900.00 - $221,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PRODUCT MANAGEMENT TEAM\n\nOur team is small but mighty, partnering closely with Engineering, Design, and Analytics to craft a two-sided marketplace that successfully delivers business to our pros while helping millions of customers complete their home projects each year. We have cultivated an environment defined by radical ownership and a strong bias for action, empowering you to move fast, define your own strategy, and drive outcomes quickly. We are outcome-obsessed and strive to spend our time on high-leverage product thinking rather than bureaucracy, minimizing administrative overhead to focus on what truly moves the needle for our users.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager who is driven by autonomy and fueled by ownership. You will be at the helm of innovation and execution, shaping industry-disrupting user experiences that simplify how millions of people confidently care for their homes and how home service professionals grow their business. This role is about defining product vision, challenging the status quo, and driving outcomes that leave a lasting impact on our customers, local service professionals, and the entire home services industry.\n\nAs a PM on the Growth team at Thumbtack you will be responsible for driving customer and pro lifetime value by creating product solutions for homeowners and home-service professionals to accomplish their goals with ease and confidence. You will be responsible for building new 0 to 1 product experiences as well as optimizing existing products to drive more user repeat and growth.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead a significant portion of our product experience and be accountable for business outcomes.\n\n - Conduct user research and lightweight tests to scope and prioritize product initiatives.\n\n - Transform a vague, ambitious idea into a compelling business and product case, secure resources, and lead execution with clear success criteria.\n\n - Champion deep learnings and insights as a core metric, valuing them alongside traditional metrics to fuel smarter, more innovative product decisions.\n\n - Partner with marketing, engineers, designers, data and applied scientists to ideate, prioritize and deliver great solutions for our customers and professionals.\n\n - Coordinate within your team and among teams at Thumbtack to ensure understanding of and alignment around projects.\n\n - Drive a high-impact initiative from seed to scale, ensuring sustained focus by thoughtfully sunsetting or culling initiatives that do not meet success criteria.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 5+ years of product management experience with a proven track record of launching impactful consumer web or mobile products that users love.\n\n - Excellent user-centric thinking with strong user experience and product sense, allowing you to empathize with users and craft excellent experiences.\n\n - Excellent analytical thinking and problem-solving skills combined with strong business acumen.\n\n - Outstanding teamwork and collaboration skills, capable of considering multiple perspectives and driving cross-functional alignment.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for articulating complex customer problems precisely.\n\n - Comfort with and strong discerning judgment of AI.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $200,600.00 - $259,600.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $170,900.00 - $221,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f4b2823d-ab17-465d-b246-c0e3629f4a30","title":"Sr. Director, Product & Experience Marketing","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T21:34:45.439+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/f4b2823d-ab17-465d-b246-c0e3629f4a30","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/f4b2823d-ab17-465d-b246-c0e3629f4a30/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2>About the Marketing &amp; Communications Team</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Marketing &amp; Communications team at Thumbtack is responsible for turning the company’s product ambitions into relationships that last. Product Marketing translates Thumbtack’s strategy into positioning that homeowners and professionals genuinely understand and value. Experience Marketing—spanning Lifecycle, Landing Page Optimization and Content Marketing—builds the ongoing engagement that makes Thumbtack indispensable after the first interaction. Together, these functions connect product, growth, and commercial efforts to the outcomes that matter most to the business.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This Sr. Director role leads both Product Marketing and Experience Marketing at a pivotal moment for Thumbtack. Demand is growing ahead of plan, the product roadmap is ambitious, and the company is investing seriously in the marketing capability that will turn transactional usage into lasting relationships. You will own strategy and execution across PMM and Experience Marketing, manage a team of experienced marketers, and work closely with Product, Commercial, and Growth leadership to keep these functions tied to the outcomes that drive the business forward.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What you’ll do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the voice of the homeowner and the professional inside Thumbtack — building a continuous, rigorous understanding of what both audiences need, how they make decisions, and where the product earns or loses their trust, and bringing that perspective into product planning before decisions are made</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product and senior leadership to shape product vision and strategy, contributing customer insight, market perspective, and positioning upstream of the roadmap rather than downstream of engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead Product Marketing to define positioning and product narrative ahead of the roadmap — for both homeowners and professionals — ensuring messaging holds coherence across a two-sided marketplace from company narrative through in-product copy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the strategic direction for Experience Marketing, connecting Lifecycle, Landing Page optimization and Content Marketing so behavioral signals and content performance inform each other and align with the broader growth strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner directly with the CPO, CCO, and Growth leadership on roadmap priorities, go-to-market strategy, and commercial alignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent your team's strategy and results clearly to senior leadership and serve as a credible voice for PMM and Experience Marketing in cross-functional conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop your team, create clear accountability, and foster an environment where strong marketers do their best work</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>In order to be successful, you must bring</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in product marketing, lifecycle marketing, or both, including significant experience leading high-performing teams at the Senior Director level (or equivalent) within a high-growth company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of working closely with product teams, not just downstream of them; you have built positioning and messaging frameworks that hold across multiple audiences and a complex product portfolio.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to build positioning and messaging frameworks that hold across multiple audiences and a complex product portfolio. Preferred experience in a two-sided marketplace, where the same product must earn trust with consumers and business users who care about very different things.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A clear point of view on how segmentation, personalization, and behavioral data should shape how a company communicates with its users over time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional instincts—you earn trust with product, engineering, and commercial teams by being specific, rigorous, and useful.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A commitment to developing your team and building clear accountability structures that help strong people do their best work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $270,300 - $349,800</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $243,100 - $314,600</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $229,500 - $297,000</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE MARKETING & COMMUNICATIONS TEAM\n\nThe Marketing & Communications team at Thumbtack is responsible for turning the company’s product ambitions into relationships that last. Product Marketing translates Thumbtack’s strategy into positioning that homeowners and professionals genuinely understand and value. Experience Marketing—spanning Lifecycle, Landing Page Optimization and Content Marketing—builds the ongoing engagement that makes Thumbtack indispensable after the first interaction. Together, these functions connect product, growth, and commercial efforts to the outcomes that matter most to the business.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThis Sr. Director role leads both Product Marketing and Experience Marketing at a pivotal moment for Thumbtack. Demand is growing ahead of plan, the product roadmap is ambitious, and the company is investing seriously in the marketing capability that will turn transactional usage into lasting relationships. You will own strategy and execution across PMM and Experience Marketing, manage a team of experienced marketers, and work closely with Product, Commercial, and Growth leadership to keep these functions tied to the outcomes that drive the business forward.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Serve as the voice of the homeowner and the professional inside Thumbtack — building a continuous, rigorous understanding of what both audiences need, how they make decisions, and where the product earns or loses their trust, and bringing that perspective into product planning before decisions are made\n\n - Partner with product and senior leadership to shape product vision and strategy, contributing customer insight, market perspective, and positioning upstream of the roadmap rather than downstream of engineering\n\n - Lead Product Marketing to define positioning and product narrative ahead of the roadmap — for both homeowners and professionals — ensuring messaging holds coherence across a two-sided marketplace from company narrative through in-product copy\n\n - Set the strategic direction for Experience Marketing, connecting Lifecycle, Landing Page optimization and Content Marketing so behavioral signals and content performance inform each other and align with the broader growth strategy\n\n - Partner directly with the CPO, CCO, and Growth leadership on roadmap priorities, go-to-market strategy, and commercial alignment\n\n - Represent your team's strategy and results clearly to senior leadership and serve as a credible voice for PMM and Experience Marketing in cross-functional conversations\n\n - Develop your team, create clear accountability, and foster an environment where strong marketers do their best work\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 10+ years of experience in product marketing, lifecycle marketing, or both, including significant experience leading high-performing teams at the Senior Director level (or equivalent) within a high-growth company.\n\n - A track record of working closely with product teams, not just downstream of them; you have built positioning and messaging frameworks that hold across multiple audiences and a complex product portfolio.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to build positioning and messaging frameworks that hold across multiple audiences and a complex product portfolio. Preferred experience in a two-sided marketplace, where the same product must earn trust with consumers and business users who care about very different things.\n\n - A clear point of view on how segmentation, personalization, and behavioral data should shape how a company communicates with its users over time.\n\n - Strong cross-functional instincts—you earn trust with product, engineering, and commercial teams by being specific, rigorous, and useful.\n\n - A commitment to developing your team and building clear accountability structures that help strong people do their best work.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $270,300 - $349,800\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $243,100 - $314,600\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $229,500 - $297,000\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1553e47f-ec18-4d8c-8de1-9c28d2e74d04","title":"Sr. Director, Supply & Partner Marketing","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T19:03:04.139+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/1553e47f-ec18-4d8c-8de1-9c28d2e74d04","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/1553e47f-ec18-4d8c-8de1-9c28d2e74d04/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h3><strong>About the Marketing &amp; Communications Team</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack’s Marketing &amp; Communications team drives growth on both sides of the marketplace—for homeowners and the professionals who serve them. Pro Marketing is one of our highest-priority organizational investments in 2026, built to accelerate supply-side growth by acquiring the right professionals, helping them succeed on the platform, and keeping them engaged over time. Partner Marketing extends that reach through platform integrations, distribution relationships, and channel programs that create growth opportunities no single paid or organic channel can replicate on its own.</p><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This Sr. Director role leads both Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing at a pivotal moment for Thumbtack. Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing is a new function with a clear mandate: bring the right professionals into the right markets, help them succeed, and keep them engaged long enough to build durable marketplace health. Partner Marketing sits alongside that work, with the opportunity to move from opportunistic partnership deals to a coherent strategy that compounds over time. You will build both functions with direct accountability to supply outcomes — not a separate marketing scorecard.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and own the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing strategy across the full professional lifecycle — how Thumbtack acquires the right professionals in the right markets, activates and onboards them to reach early success, and engages and retains them over the long term</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the voice of the professional inside Thumbtack — building a deep understanding of what pros care about, how they evaluate ROI on the platform, and where their experience falls short of expectations, and bringing that perspective into product and commercial decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and manage the B2B marketing programs that support professional growth: targeted acquisition, onboarding and education, community and loyalty initiatives, events, sales enablement, and marketing collateral</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead Partner Marketing as a strategic function, developing the portfolio of external partnerships — platform integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, and co-marketing — that extend Thumbtack's reach on both sides of the marketplace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with product, commercial, and supply leadership to ensure Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing are grounded in the priorities that matter most to the business and accountable to shared supply growth goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build measurement frameworks tied to professional supply outcomes — acquisition rates, activation, retention — and communicate results and tradeoffs clearly to senior leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop your team, create clear accountability, and foster an environment where strong marketers do their best work</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience leading full-funnel Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing for a supply-side audience, business customers, or professionals in a marketplace or platform context — with a track record of building activation and retention programs that move the needle on business outcomes, not just acquisition</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building activation and retention programs that go beyond acquisition, measured against business outcomes rather than marketing proxies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">B2B marketing experience, including programs like ABM, sales enablement, and events, with the ability to translate complex platform economics into clear value propositions for an audience that prioritizes ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or managing external partnerships — integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, or co-marketing — and a demonstrated ability to move partner relationships from transactional to strategic</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional instincts: you earn trust by being specific about priorities, clear about what you need, and accountable for outcomes, and you can influence senior leaders without direct authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort building from scratch — the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing function is new, the strategy is still being defined, and you need to be energized by that</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A commitment to defining success in business terms, developing your team, and building an environment where strong people do their best work</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $251,600 - $325,600</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $226,100 - $292,600</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $214,200 - $277,200</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE MARKETING & COMMUNICATIONS TEAM\n\nThumbtack’s Marketing & Communications team drives growth on both sides of the marketplace—for homeowners and the professionals who serve them. Pro Marketing is one of our highest-priority organizational investments in 2026, built to accelerate supply-side growth by acquiring the right professionals, helping them succeed on the platform, and keeping them engaged over time. Partner Marketing extends that reach through platform integrations, distribution relationships, and channel programs that create growth opportunities no single paid or organic channel can replicate on its own.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThis Sr. Director role leads both Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing at a pivotal moment for Thumbtack. Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing is a new function with a clear mandate: bring the right professionals into the right markets, help them succeed, and keep them engaged long enough to build durable marketplace health. Partner Marketing sits alongside that work, with the opportunity to move from opportunistic partnership deals to a coherent strategy that compounds over time. You will build both functions with direct accountability to supply outcomes — not a separate marketing scorecard.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Define and own the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing strategy across the full professional lifecycle — how Thumbtack acquires the right professionals in the right markets, activates and onboards them to reach early success, and engages and retains them over the long term\n\n - Serve as the voice of the professional inside Thumbtack — building a deep understanding of what pros care about, how they evaluate ROI on the platform, and where their experience falls short of expectations, and bringing that perspective into product and commercial decisions\n\n - Build and manage the B2B marketing programs that support professional growth: targeted acquisition, onboarding and education, community and loyalty initiatives, events, sales enablement, and marketing collateral\n\n - Lead Partner Marketing as a strategic function, developing the portfolio of external partnerships — platform integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, and co-marketing — that extend Thumbtack's reach on both sides of the marketplace\n\n - Work closely with product, commercial, and supply leadership to ensure Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing and Partner Marketing are grounded in the priorities that matter most to the business and accountable to shared supply growth goals\n\n - Build measurement frameworks tied to professional supply outcomes — acquisition rates, activation, retention — and communicate results and tradeoffs clearly to senior leadership\n\n - Develop your team, create clear accountability, and foster an environment where strong marketers do their best work\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 10+ years of experience leading full-funnel Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing for a supply-side audience, business customers, or professionals in a marketplace or platform context — with a track record of building activation and retention programs that move the needle on business outcomes, not just acquisition\n\n - A track record of building activation and retention programs that go beyond acquisition, measured against business outcomes rather than marketing proxies\n\n - B2B marketing experience, including programs like ABM, sales enablement, and events, with the ability to translate complex platform economics into clear value propositions for an audience that prioritizes ROI\n\n - Experience building or managing external partnerships — integrations, distribution relationships, channel programs, or co-marketing — and a demonstrated ability to move partner relationships from transactional to strategic\n\n - Strong cross-functional instincts: you earn trust by being specific about priorities, clear about what you need, and accountable for outcomes, and you can influence senior leaders without direct authority\n\n - Comfort building from scratch — the Supply Marketing / B2B Marketing function is new, the strategy is still being defined, and you need to be energized by that\n\n - A commitment to defining success in business terms, developing your team, and building an environment where strong people do their best work\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $251,600 - $325,600\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $226,100 - $292,600\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $214,200 - $277,200\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"097b6d6d-3f94-4ef0-84c9-4c7e631d7b54","title":"Lead Internal Communications Manager ","department":"Communications","team":"Communications","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T15:20:42.245+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/097b6d6d-3f94-4ef0-84c9-4c7e631d7b54","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/097b6d6d-3f94-4ef0-84c9-4c7e631d7b54/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Employee Communications Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We shape how it feels to work at Thumbtack. The Employee Communications team sits at the intersection of culture, communication, and brand. We translate Thumbtack's mission and strategy into meaningful moments for employees and candidates alike. By bringing together internal communications and employer brand storytelling, we ensure our values are not just articulated, but experienced.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From leadership messaging and key company moments to recruitment marketing campaigns, we create a cohesive narrative that resonates from a candidate's first interaction through every stage of the employee experience, reinforcing who we are and what we stand for along the way.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Lead Internal Communications Manager, you'll serve as a senior strategist and thought leader on internal communications. You'll own the development and execution of high-impact strategies that span internal communications, employer brand, and executive messaging, driving alignment across the organization and shaping how Thumbtack's story is told.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-visibility role that requires both strategic vision and hands-on execution. You'll independently lead multi-year communications initiatives, manage complex stakeholder relationships end-to-end, and serve as a trusted partner to senior leaders and cross-functional teams, influencing decisions at the highest levels of the organization.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute global internal communications strategies that connect business priorities to clear, consistent messaging across teams and audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive long-term, high-impact communications initiatives from strategy through execution, establishing communications frameworks and best practices that improve consistency, effectiveness, and organizational alignment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise senior leaders on communications strategy, shaping executive messaging and employee narratives through high-stakes, high-visibility, and sensitive business moments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish success metrics for communications programs, evaluate effectiveness, and use insights to continuously improve communications strategy and employee engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape executive and enterprise communications, including all-hands presentations, AMA materials, leadership updates, and company announcements, ensuring every communication aligns with business priorities, audience needs, and Thumbtack's narrative.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence cross-functional partners at all levels, driving strategic alignment and advancing key initiatives in partnership with leaders across Brand &amp; Communications, Marketing, People, Engineering, Product, and other business functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI to accelerate research, drafting, synthesis, and iteration while applying exceptional editorial judgment to ensure quality, accuracy, and audience fit.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in internal or executive communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record of independently leading enterprise communications strategies that shape business priorities, influence executive stakeholders, and drive measurable organizational impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success leading communications for company-wide moments such as all-hands meetings, AMAs, executive announcements, reorganizations, and culture initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex business topics into clear, compelling narratives that inform, inspire, and align diverse audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence with a demonstrated ability to advise senior leaders on messaging, narrative development, organizational change, and employee communications strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to establish scalable communications programs, operating models, and best practices, using data-driven insights and measurement to continuously improve effectiveness, team performance, and organizational impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional editorial judgment, including the ability to thoughtfully integrate AI into communications workflows while maintaining accountability for every final deliverable.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $163,200 - $211,200.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE EMPLOYEE COMMUNICATIONS TEAM\n\nWe shape how it feels to work at Thumbtack. The Employee Communications team sits at the intersection of culture, communication, and brand. We translate Thumbtack's mission and strategy into meaningful moments for employees and candidates alike. By bringing together internal communications and employer brand storytelling, we ensure our values are not just articulated, but experienced.\n\nFrom leadership messaging and key company moments to recruitment marketing campaigns, we create a cohesive narrative that resonates from a candidate's first interaction through every stage of the employee experience, reinforcing who we are and what we stand for along the way.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Lead Internal Communications Manager, you'll serve as a senior strategist and thought leader on internal communications. You'll own the development and execution of high-impact strategies that span internal communications, employer brand, and executive messaging, driving alignment across the organization and shaping how Thumbtack's story is told.\n\nThis is a high-visibility role that requires both strategic vision and hands-on execution. You'll independently lead multi-year communications initiatives, manage complex stakeholder relationships end-to-end, and serve as a trusted partner to senior leaders and cross-functional teams, influencing decisions at the highest levels of the organization.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Develop and execute global internal communications strategies that connect business priorities to clear, consistent messaging across teams and audiences.\n\n - Drive long-term, high-impact communications initiatives from strategy through execution, establishing communications frameworks and best practices that improve consistency, effectiveness, and organizational alignment.\n\n - Advise senior leaders on communications strategy, shaping executive messaging and employee narratives through high-stakes, high-visibility, and sensitive business moments.\n\n - Establish success metrics for communications programs, evaluate effectiveness, and use insights to continuously improve communications strategy and employee engagement.\n\n - Shape executive and enterprise communications, including all-hands presentations, AMA materials, leadership updates, and company announcements, ensuring every communication aligns with business priorities, audience needs, and Thumbtack's narrative.\n\n - Influence cross-functional partners at all levels, driving strategic alignment and advancing key initiatives in partnership with leaders across Brand & Communications, Marketing, People, Engineering, Product, and other business functions.\n\n - Leverage AI to accelerate research, drafting, synthesis, and iteration while applying exceptional editorial judgment to ensure quality, accuracy, and audience fit.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 8+ years of experience in internal or executive communications.\n\n - A proven track record of independently leading enterprise communications strategies that shape business priorities, influence executive stakeholders, and drive measurable organizational impact.\n\n - Success leading communications for company-wide moments such as all-hands meetings, AMAs, executive announcements, reorganizations, and culture initiatives.\n\n - Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex business topics into clear, compelling narratives that inform, inspire, and align diverse audiences.\n\n - Strong executive presence with a demonstrated ability to advise senior leaders on messaging, narrative development, organizational change, and employee communications strategy.\n\n - Ability to establish scalable communications programs, operating models, and best practices, using data-driven insights and measurement to continuously improve effectiveness, team performance, and organizational impact.\n\n - Exceptional editorial judgment, including the ability to thoughtfully integrate AI into communications workflows while maintaining accountability for every final deliverable.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $163,200 - $211,200.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c448ea87-2aa9-4f46-bf6b-0f10e2cc28fd","title":"Lead Internal Communications Manager","department":"Communications","team":"Communications","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T15:13:45.433+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/c448ea87-2aa9-4f46-bf6b-0f10e2cc28fd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/c448ea87-2aa9-4f46-bf6b-0f10e2cc28fd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Employee Communications Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We shape how it feels to work at Thumbtack. The Employee Communications team sits at the intersection of culture, communication, and brand. We translate Thumbtack's mission and strategy into meaningful moments for employees and candidates alike. By bringing together internal communications and employer brand storytelling, we ensure our values are not just articulated, but experienced.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From leadership messaging and key company moments to recruitment marketing campaigns, we create a cohesive narrative that resonates from a candidate's first interaction through every stage of the employee experience, reinforcing who we are and what we stand for along the way.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Lead Internal Communications Manager, you'll serve as a senior strategist and thought leader on internal communications. You'll own the development and execution of high-impact strategies that span internal communications, employer brand, and executive messaging, driving alignment across the organization and shaping how Thumbtack's story is told.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-visibility role that requires both strategic vision and hands-on execution. You'll independently lead multi-year communications initiatives, manage complex stakeholder relationships end-to-end, and serve as a trusted partner to senior leaders and cross-functional teams, influencing decisions at the highest levels of the organization.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute global internal communications strategies that connect business priorities to clear, consistent messaging across teams and audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive long-term, high-impact communications initiatives from strategy through execution, establishing communications frameworks and best practices that improve consistency, effectiveness, and organizational alignment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise senior leaders on communications strategy, shaping executive messaging and employee narratives through high-stakes, high-visibility, and sensitive business moments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish success metrics for communications programs, evaluate effectiveness, and use insights to continuously improve communications strategy and employee engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape executive and enterprise communications, including all-hands presentations, AMA materials, leadership updates, and company announcements, ensuring every communication aligns with business priorities, audience needs, and Thumbtack's narrative.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence cross-functional partners at all levels, driving strategic alignment and advancing key initiatives in partnership with leaders across Brand &amp; Communications, Marketing, People, Engineering, Product, and other business functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI to accelerate research, drafting, synthesis, and iteration while applying exceptional editorial judgment to ensure quality, accuracy, and audience fit.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in internal or executive communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record of independently leading enterprise communications strategies that shape business priorities, influence executive stakeholders, and drive measurable organizational impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success leading communications for company-wide moments such as all-hands meetings, AMAs, executive announcements, reorganizations, and culture initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex business topics into clear, compelling narratives that inform, inspire, and align diverse audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence with a demonstrated ability to advise senior leaders on messaging, narrative development, organizational change, and employee communications strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to establish scalable communications programs, operating models, and best practices, using data-driven insights and measurement to continuously improve effectiveness, team performance, and organizational impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional editorial judgment, including the ability to thoughtfully integrate AI into communications workflows while maintaining accountability for every final deliverable.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $187,000 - $242,000.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $168,300 - $217,800.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $159,000 - $205,700.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE EMPLOYEE COMMUNICATIONS TEAM\n\nWe shape how it feels to work at Thumbtack. The Employee Communications team sits at the intersection of culture, communication, and brand. We translate Thumbtack's mission and strategy into meaningful moments for employees and candidates alike. By bringing together internal communications and employer brand storytelling, we ensure our values are not just articulated, but experienced.\n\nFrom leadership messaging and key company moments to recruitment marketing campaigns, we create a cohesive narrative that resonates from a candidate's first interaction through every stage of the employee experience, reinforcing who we are and what we stand for along the way.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Lead Internal Communications Manager, you'll serve as a senior strategist and thought leader on internal communications. You'll own the development and execution of high-impact strategies that span internal communications, employer brand, and executive messaging, driving alignment across the organization and shaping how Thumbtack's story is told.\n\nThis is a high-visibility role that requires both strategic vision and hands-on execution. You'll independently lead multi-year communications initiatives, manage complex stakeholder relationships end-to-end, and serve as a trusted partner to senior leaders and cross-functional teams, influencing decisions at the highest levels of the organization.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Develop and execute global internal communications strategies that connect business priorities to clear, consistent messaging across teams and audiences.\n\n - Drive long-term, high-impact communications initiatives from strategy through execution, establishing communications frameworks and best practices that improve consistency, effectiveness, and organizational alignment.\n\n - Advise senior leaders on communications strategy, shaping executive messaging and employee narratives through high-stakes, high-visibility, and sensitive business moments.\n\n - Establish success metrics for communications programs, evaluate effectiveness, and use insights to continuously improve communications strategy and employee engagement.\n\n - Shape executive and enterprise communications, including all-hands presentations, AMA materials, leadership updates, and company announcements, ensuring every communication aligns with business priorities, audience needs, and Thumbtack's narrative.\n\n - Influence cross-functional partners at all levels, driving strategic alignment and advancing key initiatives in partnership with leaders across Brand & Communications, Marketing, People, Engineering, Product, and other business functions.\n\n - Leverage AI to accelerate research, drafting, synthesis, and iteration while applying exceptional editorial judgment to ensure quality, accuracy, and audience fit.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 8+ years of experience in internal or executive communications.\n\n - A proven track record of independently leading enterprise communications strategies that shape business priorities, influence executive stakeholders, and drive measurable organizational impact.\n\n - Success leading communications for company-wide moments such as all-hands meetings, AMAs, executive announcements, reorganizations, and culture initiatives.\n\n - Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex business topics into clear, compelling narratives that inform, inspire, and align diverse audiences.\n\n - Strong executive presence with a demonstrated ability to advise senior leaders on messaging, narrative development, organizational change, and employee communications strategy.\n\n - Ability to establish scalable communications programs, operating models, and best practices, using data-driven insights and measurement to continuously improve effectiveness, team performance, and organizational impact.\n\n - Exceptional editorial judgment, including the ability to thoughtfully integrate AI into communications workflows while maintaining accountability for every final deliverable.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $187,000 - $242,000.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $168,300 - $217,800.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $159,000 - $205,700.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"41fd3b7d-b31e-4609-b935-ad5a568146dc","title":"Sales Team Manager","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-03T06:21:38.136+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/41fd3b7d-b31e-4609-b935-ad5a568146dc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/41fd3b7d-b31e-4609-b935-ad5a568146dc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Sales Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At our core, the Sales team is built to grow the company. We're focused on bringing in top-tier professionals who are prepared to offer an exceptional experience for our customers. What sets us apart is our consultative sales approach, which ensures our pros deeply understand our product and stay with us longer. We're a scaling sales organization on the lookout for dynamic leaders who are ready to build with us.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As our Sales Manager, you will recruit, train, and manage a team of Sales Development Representatives (SDRs) or Account Executives (AEs). You'll serve as a coach and strategist, empowering your team to hit key performance indicators (KPIs) and overcome sales obstacles by optimizing pitches and processes. The ideal candidate has strong sales expertise and understands that building trust and rapport with our pros is crucial for long-term relationships. In this pivotal role, you will directly influence the team's growth and company revenue by surfacing key insights from sales conversations, testing new data sources and processes, and improving the quality and quantity of pros on our platform.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Leadership</strong>: Cultivate a high-morale, high-performance sales culture by setting and achieving ambitious team goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coaching &amp; Development</strong>: Train and mentor all team members, from new hires to tenured staff, on sales strategies, scripting, and processes, particularly within a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Process Improvement</strong>: Manage dynamic sales campaigns, optimize team productivity, and streamline the workflow and operations for SDRs or AEs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Feedback</strong>: Provide direct feedback to Sales Leadership, Operations, and Enablement to improve workflow efficiency and identify key training opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Expertise</strong>: Become an expert in the product and clearly articulate its value to every professional.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Performance Management</strong>: Consistently monitor and document team performance.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An expert in solution-based selling, able to align prospect goals and pain points with product solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A minimum of 3 years of sales experience, plus 2–3 years of direct people management experience leading a team of sales closers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to motivate and influence a team, fostering a positive and collaborative sales environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in creating scalable processes and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Proficient with CRM and sales tools; Salesforce experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to articulate product benefits and features clearly and persuasively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized, detail-oriented, and able to multitask effectively while remaining available and accessible to the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior B2B, marketing, or advertising sales experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Salesforce and Google Suite.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A tech-savvy individual who quickly adapts to new tools.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE SALES TEAM\n\nAt our core, the Sales team is built to grow the company. We're focused on bringing in top-tier professionals who are prepared to offer an exceptional experience for our customers. What sets us apart is our consultative sales approach, which ensures our pros deeply understand our product and stay with us longer. We're a scaling sales organization on the lookout for dynamic leaders who are ready to build with us.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs our Sales Manager, you will recruit, train, and manage a team of Sales Development Representatives (SDRs) or Account Executives (AEs). You'll serve as a coach and strategist, empowering your team to hit key performance indicators (KPIs) and overcome sales obstacles by optimizing pitches and processes. The ideal candidate has strong sales expertise and understands that building trust and rapport with our pros is crucial for long-term relationships. In this pivotal role, you will directly influence the team's growth and company revenue by surfacing key insights from sales conversations, testing new data sources and processes, and improving the quality and quantity of pros on our platform.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Team Leadership: Cultivate a high-morale, high-performance sales culture by setting and achieving ambitious team goals.\n\n - Coaching & Development: Train and mentor all team members, from new hires to tenured staff, on sales strategies, scripting, and processes, particularly within a remote environment.\n\n - Process Improvement: Manage dynamic sales campaigns, optimize team productivity, and streamline the workflow and operations for SDRs or AEs.\n\n - Strategic Feedback: Provide direct feedback to Sales Leadership, Operations, and Enablement to improve workflow efficiency and identify key training opportunities.\n\n - Product Expertise: Become an expert in the product and clearly articulate its value to every professional.\n\n - Performance Management: Consistently monitor and document team performance.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - An expert in solution-based selling, able to align prospect goals and pain points with product solutions.\n\n - A minimum of 3 years of sales experience, plus 2–3 years of direct people management experience leading a team of sales closers.\n\n - Proven ability to motivate and influence a team, fostering a positive and collaborative sales environment.\n\n - Expertise in creating scalable processes and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Proficient with CRM and sales tools; Salesforce experience is a plus.\n\n - Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to articulate product benefits and features clearly and persuasively.\n\n - Highly organized, detail-oriented, and able to multitask effectively while remaining available and accessible to the team.\n\n - Prior B2B, marketing, or advertising sales experience.\n\n - Proficiency with Salesforce and Google Suite.\n\n - A tech-savvy individual who quickly adapts to new tools.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"13ddbea0-a15a-40ba-a889-8fccbde0a10d","title":"Senior Accounting Associate (Accounts Payable)","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T01:24:15.785+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/13ddbea0-a15a-40ba-a889-8fccbde0a10d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/13ddbea0-a15a-40ba-a889-8fccbde0a10d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Accounting Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Accounting Team is involved in all aspects of the business ensuring we properly capture, account for, and record all the activities that occur as they occur.  We keep the books and records for the Company, help to ensure Thumbtack has appropriate policies and procedures in place, and provide the business with the information in order to make critical decisions in support of Thumbtack’s success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a highly skilled Accounts Payable Senior Accountant to join our Accounting team. This is a unique opportunity for a motivated professional based in the Philippines to work remotely on a Pacific Time (PT) schedule. You'll be the primary point person for all accounts payable and employee reimbursement activities for Thumbtack globally, ensuring accuracy, timeliness, and compliance. This role is crucial to our financial operations and requires someone with a strong attention to detail and a proactive, problem-solving mindset.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is growing quickly, and so is our finance function. Our systems and processes will change — you should expect this role's scope to evolve, and be genuinely excited to learn new tools, take on adjacent areas, and help implement new systems as we scale.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform the full cycle of accounts payable, including receiving, processing, verifying, and reconciling invoices for Thumbtack’s US, Canada, and Philippines entities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure timely and accurate processing of payments, adhering to company policies and deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reconcile vendor statements and resolve any discrepancies or issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with various departments to gather necessary approvals and documentation for invoice processing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the employee expense report processing tool and process expense reports reviews, approvals, accruals and reconciliations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Aid in prepaid preparation and run monthly prepaid amortization in preparation for month end close</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in the month-end and year-end close processes, specifically related to bank matching, accounts payable accruals, and reconciliations in accordance with US GAAP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively identify and implement process improvements to enhance efficiency and accuracy in any of the areas in your work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support audit requests by providing relevant documentation and explanations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with and/or complete ad hoc projects as requested. Research and document issues, special projects, AP automation, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner on finance systems changes - evaluating, testing, and implementing new tools or new functionality within existing ones (e.g., NetSuite, Coupa, Navan) — and take on new areas of ownership as the team's scope grows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 5 years of solid experience as an Accountant, with focus on Accounts Payable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Accountancy, Finance, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of accounting principles and financial reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail and a high degree of accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and manage time effectively to meet deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Critical thinking and the confidence to challenge the status quo</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptability and learning agility - comfortable with ambiguity and shifting priorities, quick to pick up new systems, and eager to take on new areas of ownership as the business grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must be able to work during Pacific Time (PT) hours (9 AM - 6 PM PT).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A CPA license is preferred but not required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in accounting software (e.g., NetSuite, Coupa, GSuite, Navan) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with accounts payable in a shared service entity is preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with system implementations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE ACCOUNTING TEAM\n\nThe Accounting Team is involved in all aspects of the business ensuring we properly capture, account for, and record all the activities that occur as they occur.  We keep the books and records for the Company, help to ensure Thumbtack has appropriate policies and procedures in place, and provide the business with the information in order to make critical decisions in support of Thumbtack’s success.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for a highly skilled Accounts Payable Senior Accountant to join our Accounting team. This is a unique opportunity for a motivated professional based in the Philippines to work remotely on a Pacific Time (PT) schedule. You'll be the primary point person for all accounts payable and employee reimbursement activities for Thumbtack globally, ensuring accuracy, timeliness, and compliance. This role is crucial to our financial operations and requires someone with a strong attention to detail and a proactive, problem-solving mindset.\n\nThumbtack is growing quickly, and so is our finance function. Our systems and processes will change — you should expect this role's scope to evolve, and be genuinely excited to learn new tools, take on adjacent areas, and help implement new systems as we scale.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Perform the full cycle of accounts payable, including receiving, processing, verifying, and reconciling invoices for Thumbtack’s US, Canada, and Philippines entities\n\n - Ensure timely and accurate processing of payments, adhering to company policies and deadlines.\n\n - Reconcile vendor statements and resolve any discrepancies or issues.\n\n - Collaborate with various departments to gather necessary approvals and documentation for invoice processing.\n\n - Own the employee expense report processing tool and process expense reports reviews, approvals, accruals and reconciliations\n\n - Aid in prepaid preparation and run monthly prepaid amortization in preparation for month end close\n\n - Assist in the month-end and year-end close processes, specifically related to bank matching, accounts payable accruals, and reconciliations in accordance with US GAAP.\n\n - Proactively identify and implement process improvements to enhance efficiency and accuracy in any of the areas in your work.\n\n - Support audit requests by providing relevant documentation and explanations.\n\n - Assist with and/or complete ad hoc projects as requested. Research and document issues, special projects, AP automation, etc.\n\n - Partner on finance systems changes - evaluating, testing, and implementing new tools or new functionality within existing ones (e.g., NetSuite, Coupa, Navan) — and take on new areas of ownership as the team's scope grows.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - At least 5 years of solid experience as an Accountant, with focus on Accounts Payable.\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Accountancy, Finance, or a related field.\n\n - Strong understanding of accounting principles and financial reporting.\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail and a high degree of accuracy.\n\n - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Ability to work independently and manage time effectively to meet deadlines.\n\n - Critical thinking and the confidence to challenge the status quo\n\n - Adaptability and learning agility - comfortable with ambiguity and shifting priorities, quick to pick up new systems, and eager to take on new areas of ownership as the business grows\n\n - Must be able to work during Pacific Time (PT) hours (9 AM - 6 PM PT).\n\n - A CPA license is preferred but not required\n\n - Proficiency in accounting software (e.g., NetSuite, Coupa, GSuite, Navan) is a plus.\n\n - Experience with accounts payable in a shared service entity is preferred.\n\n - Experience with AI tools\n\n - Experience with system implementations\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bce9ea92-b80c-4cc7-8eda-fd008ae34205","title":"HR Business Partner","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T16:18:24.838+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/bce9ea92-b80c-4cc7-8eda-fd008ae34205","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/bce9ea92-b80c-4cc7-8eda-fd008ae34205/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the People Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our HR Business Partners are business leaders first, HR leaders second. We hold ourselves to a high standard of understanding the objectives, culture, and talent capabilities of our clients, and we quickly identify trends and solve problems in service of Thumbtack’s goals. While we value data and facts, we believe just as strongly in the intangibles — judgment, EQ, and an inclusive mindset by default. We strive to be trusted partners and coaches to people at every level of the organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring an HRBP with a knack for operations and AI solutions building — someone who can spot high-impact opportunities to apply AI across HRBP workflows and help build those solutions. You’ll embed with the HRBP team to learn how the organization works, then partner closely with the team to turn the most valuable opportunities into products, such as an exit interview synthesizer or an engagement survey action planner that eliminates manual work. This role spans three pillars — client-facing HRBP support, AI and operations, and employee relations support — and reports to the Director of HR Business Partners.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with client groups as a trusted advisor to managers and employees across the full employee lifecycle, from team effectiveness to engagement survey action planning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flag legal and compliance risks in day-to-day people management, partnering with the global HRBP team on shared strategies and priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-powered HRBP workflows: map processes, structure HR policies and playbooks into AI-ready formats, and lead rollout, training, and success metrics for AI tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the HRBP team’s COE connector, building templates, communications, and enablement materials, and support board prep, calibrations, and engagement survey insights</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cover employee relations work during team absences — PIP prep, investigations, policy violations, and conflict mediation — while helping managers document PIPs consistently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and own AI tools that automate HRBP work, iterating based on feedback and usage data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own HRBP’s North America emergency response playbook and support quarterly exit project work</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in HR with HRBP experience, including examples of using AI or automation to improve your work — a template you built, a workflow you automated, or a process you reimagined</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort experimenting with AI tools and turning ideas into working solutions, with or without engineering support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Broad understanding of HR practices including performance, risk management, coaching, engagement and retention, workforce planning, employee relations, compensation, culture and values</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of delivering in ambiguous environments, partnering closely with senior stakeholders on direction and priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills — able to speak, write, and present information clearly; comfortable mediating and facilitating discussions at the manager level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data literacy: comfort analyzing people data, identifying trends, and translating findings into recommendations for leaders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with HRIS and HR tech platforms, plus change management experience guiding leaders and teams through organizational transitions</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $119,000 - $161,000.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $107,100 - $144,900.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $101,200 - $136,900.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PEOPLE TEAM\n\nOur HR Business Partners are business leaders first, HR leaders second. We hold ourselves to a high standard of understanding the objectives, culture, and talent capabilities of our clients, and we quickly identify trends and solve problems in service of Thumbtack’s goals. While we value data and facts, we believe just as strongly in the intangibles — judgment, EQ, and an inclusive mindset by default. We strive to be trusted partners and coaches to people at every level of the organization.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe’re hiring an HRBP with a knack for operations and AI solutions building — someone who can spot high-impact opportunities to apply AI across HRBP workflows and help build those solutions. You’ll embed with the HRBP team to learn how the organization works, then partner closely with the team to turn the most valuable opportunities into products, such as an exit interview synthesizer or an engagement survey action planner that eliminates manual work. This role spans three pillars — client-facing HRBP support, AI and operations, and employee relations support — and reports to the Director of HR Business Partners.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Partner with client groups as a trusted advisor to managers and employees across the full employee lifecycle, from team effectiveness to engagement survey action planning\n\n - Flag legal and compliance risks in day-to-day people management, partnering with the global HRBP team on shared strategies and priorities\n\n - Build AI-powered HRBP workflows: map processes, structure HR policies and playbooks into AI-ready formats, and lead rollout, training, and success metrics for AI tools\n\n - Serve as the HRBP team’s COE connector, building templates, communications, and enablement materials, and support board prep, calibrations, and engagement survey insights\n\n - Cover employee relations work during team absences — PIP prep, investigations, policy violations, and conflict mediation — while helping managers document PIPs consistently\n\n - Build and own AI tools that automate HRBP work, iterating based on feedback and usage data\n\n - Own HRBP’s North America emergency response playbook and support quarterly exit project work\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 3+ years of experience in HR with HRBP experience, including examples of using AI or automation to improve your work — a template you built, a workflow you automated, or a process you reimagined\n\n - Comfort experimenting with AI tools and turning ideas into working solutions, with or without engineering support\n\n - Broad understanding of HR practices including performance, risk management, coaching, engagement and retention, workforce planning, employee relations, compensation, culture and values\n\n - A track record of delivering in ambiguous environments, partnering closely with senior stakeholders on direction and priorities\n\n - Strong communication skills — able to speak, write, and present information clearly; comfortable mediating and facilitating discussions at the manager level\n\n - Data literacy: comfort analyzing people data, identifying trends, and translating findings into recommendations for leaders\n\n - Familiarity with HRIS and HR tech platforms, plus change management experience guiding leaders and teams through organizational transitions\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $119,000 - $161,000.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $107,100 - $144,900.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $101,200 - $136,900.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c4f7952e-33cf-4f52-90e2-90d692eff604","title":"Senior iOS Engineer, Customer Growth","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T18:17:32.213+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/c4f7952e-33cf-4f52-90e2-90d692eff604","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/c4f7952e-33cf-4f52-90e2-90d692eff604/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Growth Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The <em>Customer Acquisition, Growth, and Engagement</em> team (CAGE) is focused on streamlining and innovating around the new and returning user experience for Thumbtack. By adding value for users and meeting their needs, we can activate them as first time customers and convince them to return to Thumbtack to help solve future problems by ensuring their experience was a good one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We accomplish this by focusing both on getting the fundamentals right around core experiences like login and auth, as well as by building new features that allow us to better understand user needs early in their journey to get them to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Many of the sorts of changes we’re making are unproven, and as a data driven company, we prefer to run experiments that vet our hypotheses. As an engineer, balancing places we can be scrappy to test ideas quickly  vs places we need to take more care to exercise engineering rigor and build things the right way is important. Given we have cross functional teams, if you like looking at user problems from a product or design perspective, you’ll be a great fit for this.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive iOS feature projects to completion, focusing on the business and customer impact of those projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Break down large projects into concrete deliverables and milestones that make it easy to track progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with back-end engineers, product managers, designers, data analysts, and other teams to gather feedback, prioritize projects, and deliver solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate project status to stakeholders, proactively raising potential blockers and other risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore new frameworks and processes while also being able to discuss when (or when not) to use them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in a culture that values thoughtful code reviews and frequent deployments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate iOS engineer with experience building, testing, releasing, and maintaining apps written in Swift or Objective-C.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of shipping consumer-facing apps that users love on the App Store.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional collaboration and communication. We’re moving quickly, so it’s important for our engineers to communicate their status regularly, proactively bring up potential blockers and risks, and keep our cross-functional partners in the loop.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE GROWTH TEAM\n\nThe Customer Acquisition, Growth, and Engagement team (CAGE) is focused on streamlining and innovating around the new and returning user experience for Thumbtack. By adding value for users and meeting their needs, we can activate them as first time customers and convince them to return to Thumbtack to help solve future problems by ensuring their experience was a good one.\n\nWe accomplish this by focusing both on getting the fundamentals right around core experiences like login and auth, as well as by building new features that allow us to better understand user needs early in their journey to get them to the right place.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nMany of the sorts of changes we’re making are unproven, and as a data driven company, we prefer to run experiments that vet our hypotheses. As an engineer, balancing places we can be scrappy to test ideas quickly  vs places we need to take more care to exercise engineering rigor and build things the right way is important. Given we have cross functional teams, if you like looking at user problems from a product or design perspective, you’ll be a great fit for this.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Drive iOS feature projects to completion, focusing on the business and customer impact of those projects.\n\n - Break down large projects into concrete deliverables and milestones that make it easy to track progress.\n\n - Work closely with back-end engineers, product managers, designers, data analysts, and other teams to gather feedback, prioritize projects, and deliver solutions.\n\n - Communicate project status to stakeholders, proactively raising potential blockers and other risks.\n\n - Explore new frameworks and processes while also being able to discuss when (or when not) to use them.\n\n - Participate in a culture that values thoughtful code reviews and frequent deployments.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Passionate iOS engineer with experience building, testing, releasing, and maintaining apps written in Swift or Objective-C.\n\n - Proven track record of shipping consumer-facing apps that users love on the App Store.\n\n - Cross-functional collaboration and communication. We’re moving quickly, so it’s important for our engineers to communicate their status regularly, proactively bring up potential blockers and risks, and keep our cross-functional partners in the loop.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a6f52c2f-1036-4ea6-ac44-5e50990a8933","title":"Senior iOS Engineer, Customer Growth","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-10T18:17:35.757+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/a6f52c2f-1036-4ea6-ac44-5e50990a8933","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/a6f52c2f-1036-4ea6-ac44-5e50990a8933/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Growth Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The <em>Customer Acquisition, Growth, and Engagement</em> team (CAGE) is focused on streamlining and innovating around the new and returning user experience for Thumbtack. By adding value for users and meeting their needs, we can activate them as first time customers and convince them to return to Thumbtack to help solve future problems by ensuring their experience was a good one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We accomplish this by focusing both on getting the fundamentals right around core experiences like login and auth, as well as by building new features that allow us to better understand user needs early in their journey to get them to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Many of the sorts of changes we’re making are unproven, and as a data driven company, we prefer to run experiments that vet our hypotheses. As an engineer, balancing places we can be scrappy to test ideas quickly  vs places we need to take more care to exercise engineering rigor and build things the right way is important. Given we have cross functional teams, if you like looking at user problems from a product or design perspective, you’ll be a great fit for this.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive iOS feature projects to completion, focusing on the business and customer impact of those projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Break down large projects into concrete deliverables and milestones that make it easy to track progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with back-end engineers, product managers, designers, data analysts, and other teams to gather feedback, prioritize projects, and deliver solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate project status to stakeholders, proactively raising potential blockers and other risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore new frameworks and processes while also being able to discuss when (or when not) to use them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in a culture that values thoughtful code reviews and frequent deployments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate iOS engineer with experience building, testing, releasing, and maintaining apps written in Swift or Objective-C.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of shipping consumer-facing apps that users love on the App Store.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional collaboration and communication. We’re moving quickly, so it’s important for our engineers to communicate their status regularly, proactively bring up potential blockers and risks, and keep our cross-functional partners in the loop.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE GROWTH TEAM\n\nThe Customer Acquisition, Growth, and Engagement team (CAGE) is focused on streamlining and innovating around the new and returning user experience for Thumbtack. By adding value for users and meeting their needs, we can activate them as first time customers and convince them to return to Thumbtack to help solve future problems by ensuring their experience was a good one.\n\nWe accomplish this by focusing both on getting the fundamentals right around core experiences like login and auth, as well as by building new features that allow us to better understand user needs early in their journey to get them to the right place.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nMany of the sorts of changes we’re making are unproven, and as a data driven company, we prefer to run experiments that vet our hypotheses. As an engineer, balancing places we can be scrappy to test ideas quickly  vs places we need to take more care to exercise engineering rigor and build things the right way is important. Given we have cross functional teams, if you like looking at user problems from a product or design perspective, you’ll be a great fit for this.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Drive iOS feature projects to completion, focusing on the business and customer impact of those projects.\n\n - Break down large projects into concrete deliverables and milestones that make it easy to track progress.\n\n - Work closely with back-end engineers, product managers, designers, data analysts, and other teams to gather feedback, prioritize projects, and deliver solutions.\n\n - Communicate project status to stakeholders, proactively raising potential blockers and other risks.\n\n - Explore new frameworks and processes while also being able to discuss when (or when not) to use them.\n\n - Participate in a culture that values thoughtful code reviews and frequent deployments.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - Passionate iOS engineer with experience building, testing, releasing, and maintaining apps written in Swift or Objective-C.\n\n - Proven track record of shipping consumer-facing apps that users love on the App Store.\n\n - Cross-functional collaboration and communication. We’re moving quickly, so it’s important for our engineers to communicate their status regularly, proactively bring up potential blockers and risks, and keep our cross-functional partners in the loop.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"62aafbf1-0e11-434e-8f05-121f59a09261","title":"Sales Success Specialist (B2B)","department":"Success","team":"Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T02:53:11.951+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/62aafbf1-0e11-434e-8f05-121f59a09261","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/62aafbf1-0e11-434e-8f05-121f59a09261/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Success Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the leading marketplace platform connecting customers with local professionals for all their project and service needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a rapidly growing organization looking for highly motivated individuals to join us in scaling our success team. Our culture prides itself on diversity and inclusion and our mission is to empower independent pros to grow their businesses, and that's where you come in.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Success Specialist</strong>, you'll be on the front lines, helping our pros unlock their full potential and build thriving businesses on Thumbtack. It's all about being a strategic partner and champion for our pros. You'll be the ultimate guide for our pros, helping them navigate their journey to success. We're looking for someone who is not just great at building rapport but is also a consultative partner who can dive deep into a pro's business, marketing strategy, and growth goals.  Your day will be packed with high-impact activities building trust and loyalty and driving revenue and departmental goals.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with our pros on our platform by listening to their needs and providing the best solutions - you’re the expert! Pro satisfaction and longevity will be your #1 priority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain excellent knowledge of Thumbtack’s products and services, as well as industry standards and best practices for home maintenance and repairs and other service industries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in at least 50 outbound interactions per day with our pros to determine the best solution to help them get hired. This can include using tools such as AI to optimize their accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successfully build rapport with the pros and be able to anticipate their needs and long term business goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct comprehensive profile reviews, guiding pros through key areas like response time, reviews, profile pictures, and quick replies to help them shine. You’ll encourage them to complete product recommendations and set competitive budgets, setting them up for success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to cross-sell additional products or services to existing pros.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively listen to pro concerns taking on a consultative approach, have the ability to probe, and be able to provide recommendations when necessary.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have the ability to set the proper expectations on lead costs, marketing and ROI with our pros so they are satisfied and can justify their marketing spend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and resolve pro inquiries with effective problem-solving and de-escalating skills while building a relationship with the pro.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively follow up with pros via call, SMS and/or email.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high-performance metrics including revenue attainment, quality adherence, efficiency, pro satisfaction, and net promoter scores.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously look for areas of improvements that drive revenue and communicate trends to the appropriate parties.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make independent and insightful decisions while keeping the pro and company needs in mind.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with team members through weekly development sessions, training, and support interactions that help build each other.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 1–2 years of B2B selling and or success experience, with a minimum of 6 months of outbound calling or collections exposure, preferably in the BPO or Shared Services industry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer retention, churn, onboarding and reactivation experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record meeting or exceeding quotas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in English.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, consultative and problem solving mindset, with a willingness to share techniques and successes with the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in pipeline management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in customer support and product education.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Marketing or advertising sales experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salesforce experience, AI experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Google Suite experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">B2B sales experience preferably in the home service space</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tech-savvy</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE SUCCESS TEAM\n\nThumbtack is the leading marketplace platform connecting customers with local professionals for all their project and service needs.\n\nWe are a rapidly growing organization looking for highly motivated individuals to join us in scaling our success team. Our culture prides itself on diversity and inclusion and our mission is to empower independent pros to grow their businesses, and that's where you come in.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs a Success Specialist, you'll be on the front lines, helping our pros unlock their full potential and build thriving businesses on Thumbtack. It's all about being a strategic partner and champion for our pros. You'll be the ultimate guide for our pros, helping them navigate their journey to success. We're looking for someone who is not just great at building rapport but is also a consultative partner who can dive deep into a pro's business, marketing strategy, and growth goals.  Your day will be packed with high-impact activities building trust and loyalty and driving revenue and departmental goals.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Partner with our pros on our platform by listening to their needs and providing the best solutions - you’re the expert! Pro satisfaction and longevity will be your #1 priority.\n\n - Maintain excellent knowledge of Thumbtack’s products and services, as well as industry standards and best practices for home maintenance and repairs and other service industries.\n\n - Participate in at least 50 outbound interactions per day with our pros to determine the best solution to help them get hired. This can include using tools such as AI to optimize their accounts.\n\n - Successfully build rapport with the pros and be able to anticipate their needs and long term business goals.\n\n - Conduct comprehensive profile reviews, guiding pros through key areas like response time, reviews, profile pictures, and quick replies to help them shine. You’ll encourage them to complete product recommendations and set competitive budgets, setting them up for success.\n\n - Identify opportunities to cross-sell additional products or services to existing pros.\n\n - Actively listen to pro concerns taking on a consultative approach, have the ability to probe, and be able to provide recommendations when necessary.\n\n - Have the ability to set the proper expectations on lead costs, marketing and ROI with our pros so they are satisfied and can justify their marketing spend.\n\n - Troubleshoot and resolve pro inquiries with effective problem-solving and de-escalating skills while building a relationship with the pro.\n\n - Proactively follow up with pros via call, SMS and/or email.\n\n - Maintain high-performance metrics including revenue attainment, quality adherence, efficiency, pro satisfaction, and net promoter scores.\n\n - Continuously look for areas of improvements that drive revenue and communicate trends to the appropriate parties.\n\n - Make independent and insightful decisions while keeping the pro and company needs in mind.\n\n - Engage with team members through weekly development sessions, training, and support interactions that help build each other.\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - At least 1–2 years of B2B selling and or success experience, with a minimum of 6 months of outbound calling or collections exposure, preferably in the BPO or Shared Services industry\n\n - Customer retention, churn, onboarding and reactivation experience.\n\n - A proven track record meeting or exceeding quotas.\n\n - Proficiency in English.\n\n - A collaborative, consultative and problem solving mindset, with a willingness to share techniques and successes with the team.\n\n - Experience in pipeline management.\n\n - Experience in customer support and product education.\n\n - Marketing or advertising sales experience\n\n - Salesforce experience, AI experience\n\n - Google Suite experience\n\n - B2B sales experience preferably in the home service space\n\n - Tech-savvy\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"98152b9a-e475-4793-b25a-416d14a0a373","title":"Sales Success Specialist (B2C)","department":"Success","team":"Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-24T00:49:16.324+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/98152b9a-e475-4793-b25a-416d14a0a373","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/98152b9a-e475-4793-b25a-416d14a0a373/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Thumbtack Service &amp; Support Team brings the Thumbtack mission to life! We focus on providing a great experience to our users through building customer loyalty and helping professionals grow their businesses.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Customer Success Specialist (CSS), you bring our Thumbtack mission to life! This is a part of our inbound/outbound sales and success efforts, where you would work specifically to resolve customer plans to service their homes. By handling customer requests through our users' different channels (phone, chat, SMS, and email), you navigate the challenges of customer needs, profile requests, and more specifically service inquiries. Our best representatives are enthusiastic individuals who thrive in a fast-paced revenue-driving environment that builds customer trust, loyalty, and drive departmental goals. The ideal candidate will have a proven track record in outbound and inbound sales efforts, with experience in recovery and expansion programs. Must also be adaptable in your sales pitch to meet customer and departmental needs. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with our customers by listening to their needs and providing the best solutions - you’re the expert! </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain excellent knowledge of Thumbtack’s products and services, as well as industry standards and best practices for home maintenance, improvement, and repair projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in at least 55 inbound and outbound calls per day with our users to determine the best solution to get jobs done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successfully build rapport with the customers and be able to anticipate their needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to cross-sell additional products or services to existing customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively listen to customer concerns, have the ability to probe, and be able to provide recommendations when necessary.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and resolve customer inquiries with effective problem-solving and de-escalating skills while building a relationship with the caller.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively follow up with customers via SMS and/or email.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high-performance metrics including revenue attainment, quality adherence, efficiency, customer satisfaction, and net promoter scores.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously look for areas of improvements that drive revenue and communicate trends to the appropriate parties.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make independent and insightful decisions while keeping the customer and company needs in mind.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with team members through weekly development sessions, training, and support interactions that help build each other. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 1–2 years of customer service experience, with a minimum of 6 months of pure inbound and/or outbound sales exposure, preferably in the BPO or Shared Services industry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience in high-volume, revenue-driven sales with a track record of meeting or exceeding quotas. You prioritize converting customer requests and driving revenue while delivering an exceptional customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">English proficiency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have a collaborative attitude to share techniques and success with the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prospecting and Pipeline Management experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Thumbtack Service & Support Team brings the Thumbtack mission to life! We focus on providing a great experience to our users through building customer loyalty and helping professionals grow their businesses.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs a Customer Success Specialist (CSS), you bring our Thumbtack mission to life! This is a part of our inbound/outbound sales and success efforts, where you would work specifically to resolve customer plans to service their homes. By handling customer requests through our users' different channels (phone, chat, SMS, and email), you navigate the challenges of customer needs, profile requests, and more specifically service inquiries. Our best representatives are enthusiastic individuals who thrive in a fast-paced revenue-driving environment that builds customer trust, loyalty, and drive departmental goals. The ideal candidate will have a proven track record in outbound and inbound sales efforts, with experience in recovery and expansion programs. Must also be adaptable in your sales pitch to meet customer and departmental needs. \n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Partner with our customers by listening to their needs and providing the best solutions - you’re the expert! \n\n - Maintain excellent knowledge of Thumbtack’s products and services, as well as industry standards and best practices for home maintenance, improvement, and repair projects.\n\n - Participate in at least 55 inbound and outbound calls per day with our users to determine the best solution to get jobs done.\n\n - Successfully build rapport with the customers and be able to anticipate their needs\n\n - Identify opportunities to cross-sell additional products or services to existing customers.\n\n - Actively listen to customer concerns, have the ability to probe, and be able to provide recommendations when necessary.\n\n - Troubleshoot and resolve customer inquiries with effective problem-solving and de-escalating skills while building a relationship with the caller.\n\n - Proactively follow up with customers via SMS and/or email.\n\n - Maintain high-performance metrics including revenue attainment, quality adherence, efficiency, customer satisfaction, and net promoter scores.\n\n - Continuously look for areas of improvements that drive revenue and communicate trends to the appropriate parties.\n\n - Make independent and insightful decisions while keeping the customer and company needs in mind.\n\n - Engage with team members through weekly development sessions, training, and support interactions that help build each other. \n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - At least 1–2 years of customer service experience, with a minimum of 6 months of pure inbound and/or outbound sales exposure, preferably in the BPO or Shared Services industry\n\n - Proven experience in high-volume, revenue-driven sales with a track record of meeting or exceeding quotas. You prioritize converting customer requests and driving revenue while delivering an exceptional customer experience.\n\n - English proficiency\n\n - Have a collaborative attitude to share techniques and success with the team\n\n - Prospecting and Pipeline Management experience\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6af41110-6afd-4cb6-8bf1-998eb869170a","title":"Director, Business Finance","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T22:07:37.573+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6af41110-6afd-4cb6-8bf1-998eb869170a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6af41110-6afd-4cb6-8bf1-998eb869170a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Finance Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Thumbtack Finance team’s mission is to be a strategic finance partner to the business — enabling better decisions supported by data, building a world-class finance function, and doing it all with integrity. We work closely with every part of the organization to connect financial insight to business outcomes and help Thumbtack grow responsibly. Our team values clear thinking, sound analysis, and a genuine partnership with the leaders we support.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Finance Business Partner to the Chief Commercial Officer, you’ll be a trusted advisor to C-suite leadership — bringing expertise in managing resources and growing the business to achieve company goals. You’ll be instrumental in optimizing go-to-market, sales, and revenue-generating initiatives, evaluating performance, and enabling data-driven decision-making. Working with Partnerships, Sales, Revenue Operations, Biz Ops, and Growth Ops, you’ll provide decision support for how sales and partnership choices impact the P&amp;L. This role is built for someone who thrives in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct financial analysis, forecasting, and budgeting for sales and go-to-market activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop financial models that guide strategic decision-making on key P&amp;L drivers, including where incremental investments will have the greatest impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Sales and Product to assess the impact of incentives, promotions, and pricing changes on revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee monthly and quarterly forecasting, reporting, and spend management, providing recommendations to optimize against budget.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze and synthesize financial results and communicate key insights to internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the business in planning, and help develop team targets and OKRs.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of FP&amp;A experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred experience in a public company and/or marketplace environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Business Development and Sales teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong financial modeling and analytical skills using Excel and G-Suite.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to tell the story beyond the numbers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to translate financial analysis into clear and insightful recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive approach to embracing AI tools to scale processes and deliver actionable insights.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $225,300.00 - $291,500.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $203,200.00 - $262,900.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $191,300.00 - $247,500.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE FINANCE TEAM\n\nThe Thumbtack Finance team’s mission is to be a strategic finance partner to the business — enabling better decisions supported by data, building a world-class finance function, and doing it all with integrity. We work closely with every part of the organization to connect financial insight to business outcomes and help Thumbtack grow responsibly. Our team values clear thinking, sound analysis, and a genuine partnership with the leaders we support.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Finance Business Partner to the Chief Commercial Officer, you’ll be a trusted advisor to C-suite leadership — bringing expertise in managing resources and growing the business to achieve company goals. You’ll be instrumental in optimizing go-to-market, sales, and revenue-generating initiatives, evaluating performance, and enabling data-driven decision-making. Working with Partnerships, Sales, Revenue Operations, Biz Ops, and Growth Ops, you’ll provide decision support for how sales and partnership choices impact the P&L. This role is built for someone who thrives in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Conduct financial analysis, forecasting, and budgeting for sales and go-to-market activities.\n\n - Develop financial models that guide strategic decision-making on key P&L drivers, including where incremental investments will have the greatest impact.\n\n - Work closely with Sales and Product to assess the impact of incentives, promotions, and pricing changes on revenue.\n\n - Oversee monthly and quarterly forecasting, reporting, and spend management, providing recommendations to optimize against budget.\n\n - Analyze and synthesize financial results and communicate key insights to internal stakeholders.\n\n - Support the business in planning, and help develop team targets and OKRs.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 8+ years of FP&A experience.\n\n - Preferred experience in a public company and/or marketplace environment.\n\n - Experience working with Business Development and Sales teams.\n\n - Strong financial modeling and analytical skills using Excel and G-Suite.\n\n - Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to tell the story beyond the numbers.\n\n - Ability to translate financial analysis into clear and insightful recommendations.\n\n - A proactive approach to embracing AI tools to scale processes and deliver actionable insights.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $225,300.00 - $291,500.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $203,200.00 - $262,900.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $191,300.00 - $247,500.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f2f3f334-2353-4bc7-8e9b-058e84c398a1","title":"Senior Engineering Manager, Pro Feedback and Targeting","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T17:50:05.060+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/f2f3f334-2353-4bc7-8e9b-058e84c398a1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/f2f3f334-2353-4bc7-8e9b-058e84c398a1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Pro Feedback and Targeting Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thumbtack, the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is focused on 0-&gt;1 work that reinvents the way pro is matched with jobs. This involves moving away from a rigid and static set of questions to understand pro preferences, which often limits innovation and product changes. Our goal is to revamp this to a new, more flexible experience by building systems that leverage AI/LLMs to gain a deeper understanding of the types of jobs pros want and can do. This new system will learn and improve as pros use it, rather than remaining static, ultimately helping pros secure more and better jobs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've built conviction through research, experiments, and market-based tests that doing this successfully would be a big unlock for Thumbtack. We are starting to pilot this with a small group of pros. Joining this team now means you are joining an area that already has high conviction and momentum behind, but still has plenty of opportunity to be involved in driving the strategy and making large product changes. Successfully achieving this will not only strengthen Thumbtack's partnership with our pros but also unlock greater impact on the marketplace side and enhance the overall customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The primary challenge for an Engineering Manager (EM) within the New Hiring Experience org that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of is to help homeowners across the U.S. search for and hire the most relevant home service professionals—and ultimately get their jobs done. We address this by tackling complex problems at the intersection of engineering, data science, and applied science.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We help homeowners start more projects on Thumbtack by enabling them to express their needs in everyday, conversational language through our search bar. This involves solving underlying challenges around query comprehension and problem scoping. As customers define their project, we help them share their preferences and availability to better match them with the most relevant professionals. We then support them in comparing and selecting the right pros for their job.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an Engineering Manager for one of the cross-functional product teams (pods) within the larger New Hiring Experience org. You will partner with the Product Manager to help define technical &amp; product strategy that include your team’s goals, and will be responsible for driving execution. You will also be responsible for coaching and managing engineers (backend, front end, iOS, Android) on a full-stack product team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Given that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of the New Hiring Experience org that is doing the 0-&gt;1 work to revamp Thumbtack’s core hiring journey, this is a high impact, high visibility role within the company. To be successful in this role, you will need to effectively collaborate with cross functional counterparts (product, design, applied science, data science etc.) across the company.​​</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and evolve the technical vision and strategy for your team in partnership with Product, Design, and Applied Science.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate effectively with teams across the company (e.g., Trust &amp; Safety, Monetization) to drive cross-functional initiatives and resolve dependencies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive execution against team goals and OKRs while guiding the team through complex technical tradeoffs and delivering high-quality outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hire, coach, and manage full-stack engineers at all levels, including Staff+ engineers, while developing future technical leaders through regular feedback, performance management, and career development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve a high-performing culture of excellence, accountability, and continuous learning on the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be accountable for maintaining, scaling, and operating the infrastructure owned by your team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with other engineering leaders to evolve Thumbtack's engineering culture, strengthen organizational effectiveness, and improve engineering practices in a high-paced growth environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in an engineering management role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience building software at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with Product, Design, Applied Science, and Data Science to define product and technical strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical judgment with experience guiding teams through complex architectural and product tradeoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading senior engineers, building high-performing teams, and coaching engineers through growth, performance, and career development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional communication and collaboration skills with experience influencing across organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using experimentation, A/B testing, market-based testing, qualitative research, and metrics to inform product and engineering decisions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $265,200.00 - $343,200.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $238,900.00 - $309,100.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $225,300.00 - $291,500.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PRO FEEDBACK AND TARGETING TEAM\n\nAt Thumbtack, the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is focused on 0->1 work that reinvents the way pro is matched with jobs. This involves moving away from a rigid and static set of questions to understand pro preferences, which often limits innovation and product changes. Our goal is to revamp this to a new, more flexible experience by building systems that leverage AI/LLMs to gain a deeper understanding of the types of jobs pros want and can do. This new system will learn and improve as pros use it, rather than remaining static, ultimately helping pros secure more and better jobs.\n\nWe've built conviction through research, experiments, and market-based tests that doing this successfully would be a big unlock for Thumbtack. We are starting to pilot this with a small group of pros. Joining this team now means you are joining an area that already has high conviction and momentum behind, but still has plenty of opportunity to be involved in driving the strategy and making large product changes. Successfully achieving this will not only strengthen Thumbtack's partnership with our pros but also unlock greater impact on the marketplace side and enhance the overall customer experience.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThe primary challenge for an Engineering Manager (EM) within the New Hiring Experience org that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of is to help homeowners across the U.S. search for and hire the most relevant home service professionals—and ultimately get their jobs done. We address this by tackling complex problems at the intersection of engineering, data science, and applied science.\n\nWe help homeowners start more projects on Thumbtack by enabling them to express their needs in everyday, conversational language through our search bar. This involves solving underlying challenges around query comprehension and problem scoping. As customers define their project, we help them share their preferences and availability to better match them with the most relevant professionals. We then support them in comparing and selecting the right pros for their job.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are seeking an Engineering Manager for one of the cross-functional product teams (pods) within the larger New Hiring Experience org. You will partner with the Product Manager to help define technical & product strategy that include your team’s goals, and will be responsible for driving execution. You will also be responsible for coaching and managing engineers (backend, front end, iOS, Android) on a full-stack product team.\n\nGiven that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of the New Hiring Experience org that is doing the 0->1 work to revamp Thumbtack’s core hiring journey, this is a high impact, high visibility role within the company. To be successful in this role, you will need to effectively collaborate with cross functional counterparts (product, design, applied science, data science etc.) across the company.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Define and evolve the technical vision and strategy for your team in partnership with Product, Design, and Applied Science.\n\n - Collaborate effectively with teams across the company (e.g., Trust & Safety, Monetization) to drive cross-functional initiatives and resolve dependencies.\n\n - Drive execution against team goals and OKRs while guiding the team through complex technical tradeoffs and delivering high-quality outcomes.\n\n - Hire, coach, and manage full-stack engineers at all levels, including Staff+ engineers, while developing future technical leaders through regular feedback, performance management, and career development.\n\n - Build and evolve a high-performing culture of excellence, accountability, and continuous learning on the team.\n\n - Be accountable for maintaining, scaling, and operating the infrastructure owned by your team.\n\n - Work closely with other engineering leaders to evolve Thumbtack's engineering culture, strengthen organizational effectiveness, and improve engineering practices in a high-paced growth environment.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 2+ years of experience in an engineering management role.\n\n - 5+ years of experience building software at scale.\n\n - Experience partnering with Product, Design, Applied Science, and Data Science to define product and technical strategy.\n\n - Strong technical judgment with experience guiding teams through complex architectural and product tradeoffs.\n\n - Experience leading senior engineers, building high-performing teams, and coaching engineers through growth, performance, and career development.\n\n - Strong cross-functional communication and collaboration skills with experience influencing across organizations.\n\n - Experience using experimentation, A/B testing, market-based testing, qualitative research, and metrics to inform product and engineering decisions.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $265,200.00 - $343,200.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $238,900.00 - $309,100.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $225,300.00 - $291,500.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d5afd3e9-77a1-4e0d-9757-8be3a5cb31fb","title":"Senior Engineering Manager, Pro Feedback and Targeting","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T17:50:07.181+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/d5afd3e9-77a1-4e0d-9757-8be3a5cb31fb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/d5afd3e9-77a1-4e0d-9757-8be3a5cb31fb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Pro Feedback and Targeting Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thumbtack, the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is focused on 0-&gt;1 work that reinvents the way pro is matched with jobs. This involves moving away from a rigid and static set of questions to understand pro preferences, which often limits innovation and product changes. Our goal is to revamp this to a new, more flexible experience by building systems that leverage AI/LLMs to gain a deeper understanding of the types of jobs pros want and can do. This new system will learn and improve as pros use it, rather than remaining static, ultimately helping pros secure more and better jobs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've built conviction through research, experiments, and market-based tests that doing this successfully would be a big unlock for Thumbtack. We are starting to pilot this with a small group of pros. Joining this team now means you are joining an area that already has high conviction and momentum behind, but still has plenty of opportunity to be involved in driving the strategy and making large product changes. Successfully achieving this will not only strengthen Thumbtack's partnership with our pros but also unlock greater impact on the marketplace side and enhance the overall customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The primary challenge for an Engineering Manager (EM) within the New Hiring Experience org that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of is to help homeowners across the U.S. search for and hire the most relevant home service professionals—and ultimately get their jobs done. We address this by tackling complex problems at the intersection of engineering, data science, and applied science.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We help homeowners start more projects on Thumbtack by enabling them to express their needs in everyday, conversational language through our search bar. This involves solving underlying challenges around query comprehension and problem scoping. As customers define their project, we help them share their preferences and availability to better match them with the most relevant professionals. We then support them in comparing and selecting the right pros for their job.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an Engineering Manager for one of the cross-functional product teams (pods) within the larger New Hiring Experience org. You will partner with the Product Manager to help define technical &amp; product strategy that include your team’s goals, and will be responsible for driving execution. You will also be responsible for coaching and managing engineers (backend, front end, iOS, Android) on a full-stack product team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Given that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of the New Hiring Experience org that is doing the 0-&gt;1 work to revamp Thumbtack’s core hiring journey, this is a high impact, high visibility role within the company. To be successful in this role, you will need to effectively collaborate with cross functional counterparts (product, design, applied science, data science etc.) across the company.​​</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and evolve the technical vision and strategy for your team in partnership with Product, Design, and Applied Science.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate effectively with teams across the company (e.g., Trust &amp; Safety, Monetization) to drive cross-functional initiatives and resolve dependencies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive execution against team goals and OKRs while guiding the team through complex technical tradeoffs and delivering high-quality outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hire, coach, and manage full-stack engineers at all levels, including Staff+ engineers, while developing future technical leaders through regular feedback, performance management, and career development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve a high-performing culture of excellence, accountability, and continuous learning on the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be accountable for maintaining, scaling, and operating the infrastructure owned by your team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with other engineering leaders to evolve Thumbtack's engineering culture, strengthen organizational effectiveness, and improve engineering practices in a high-paced growth environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in an engineering management role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience building software at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with Product, Design, Applied Science, and Data Science to define product and technical strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical judgment with experience guiding teams through complex architectural and product tradeoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading senior engineers, building high-performing teams, and coaching engineers through growth, performance, and career development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional communication and collaboration skills with experience influencing across organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using experimentation, A/B testing, market-based testing, qualitative research, and metrics to inform product and engineering decisions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $231,200.00 - $299,200.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PRO FEEDBACK AND TARGETING TEAM\n\nAt Thumbtack, the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is focused on 0->1 work that reinvents the way pro is matched with jobs. This involves moving away from a rigid and static set of questions to understand pro preferences, which often limits innovation and product changes. Our goal is to revamp this to a new, more flexible experience by building systems that leverage AI/LLMs to gain a deeper understanding of the types of jobs pros want and can do. This new system will learn and improve as pros use it, rather than remaining static, ultimately helping pros secure more and better jobs.\n\nWe've built conviction through research, experiments, and market-based tests that doing this successfully would be a big unlock for Thumbtack. We are starting to pilot this with a small group of pros. Joining this team now means you are joining an area that already has high conviction and momentum behind, but still has plenty of opportunity to be involved in driving the strategy and making large product changes. Successfully achieving this will not only strengthen Thumbtack's partnership with our pros but also unlock greater impact on the marketplace side and enhance the overall customer experience.\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThe primary challenge for an Engineering Manager (EM) within the New Hiring Experience org that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of is to help homeowners across the U.S. search for and hire the most relevant home service professionals—and ultimately get their jobs done. We address this by tackling complex problems at the intersection of engineering, data science, and applied science.\n\nWe help homeowners start more projects on Thumbtack by enabling them to express their needs in everyday, conversational language through our search bar. This involves solving underlying challenges around query comprehension and problem scoping. As customers define their project, we help them share their preferences and availability to better match them with the most relevant professionals. We then support them in comparing and selecting the right pros for their job.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are seeking an Engineering Manager for one of the cross-functional product teams (pods) within the larger New Hiring Experience org. You will partner with the Product Manager to help define technical & product strategy that include your team’s goals, and will be responsible for driving execution. You will also be responsible for coaching and managing engineers (backend, front end, iOS, Android) on a full-stack product team.\n\nGiven that the Pro Feedback and Targeting team is part of the New Hiring Experience org that is doing the 0->1 work to revamp Thumbtack’s core hiring journey, this is a high impact, high visibility role within the company. To be successful in this role, you will need to effectively collaborate with cross functional counterparts (product, design, applied science, data science etc.) across the company.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Define and evolve the technical vision and strategy for your team in partnership with Product, Design, and Applied Science.\n\n - Collaborate effectively with teams across the company (e.g., Trust & Safety, Monetization) to drive cross-functional initiatives and resolve dependencies.\n\n - Drive execution against team goals and OKRs while guiding the team through complex technical tradeoffs and delivering high-quality outcomes.\n\n - Hire, coach, and manage full-stack engineers at all levels, including Staff+ engineers, while developing future technical leaders through regular feedback, performance management, and career development.\n\n - Build and evolve a high-performing culture of excellence, accountability, and continuous learning on the team.\n\n - Be accountable for maintaining, scaling, and operating the infrastructure owned by your team.\n\n - Work closely with other engineering leaders to evolve Thumbtack's engineering culture, strengthen organizational effectiveness, and improve engineering practices in a high-paced growth environment.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 2+ years of experience in an engineering management role.\n\n - 5+ years of experience building software at scale.\n\n - Experience partnering with Product, Design, Applied Science, and Data Science to define product and technical strategy.\n\n - Strong technical judgment with experience guiding teams through complex architectural and product tradeoffs.\n\n - Experience leading senior engineers, building high-performing teams, and coaching engineers through growth, performance, and career development.\n\n - Strong cross-functional communication and collaboration skills with experience influencing across organizations.\n\n - Experience using experimentation, A/B testing, market-based testing, qualitative research, and metrics to inform product and engineering decisions.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $231,200.00 - $299,200.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d98e63a2-bbfb-48eb-8b73-abd3a8eb5976","title":"Senior Data Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T21:06:29.490+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/d98e63a2-bbfb-48eb-8b73-abd3a8eb5976","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/d98e63a2-bbfb-48eb-8b73-abd3a8eb5976/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Data Engineering Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack’s Data Engineering org is split into 3 groups: Core Data Engineering, Data Platform and Embedded Data Engineering. This role is on the Embedded Data Engineering team, which breaks down into multiple business units that data engineers are embedded into. This role would be on the commercial operations side of the house and will work closely with engineers, analysts, data scientists and machine learning engineers to help design and curate data sets originating from internal and third-party sources to meet current and future needs. Over the next year, it will continue to build on its prior successes in building a more cohesive data warehouse while starting to work more deeply upstream to build data best practices into the full software development lifecycle (SDLC).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">There are several teams all over Thumbtack with Terabytes of data and unique challenges trying to clean and organize this data to measure their performance.  In this role, you will work with Engineers, Data Scientists, Managers, and others to understand their needs, and actively work to build datasets to tackle these challenges.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboratively refine and evangelize a comprehensive framework for integrating data-thinking into the software development lifecycle for product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, architect, and maintain core operations datasets, data marts, and feature stores that support a blend of mature products and features with a rapidly evolving product line, in partnership with analytics, data science, and machine learning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Integrate deeply with our cross functional partners to understand their data needs, and help design datasets with the same engineering rigor as any other software we design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive data quality and best practices across different business areas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build the next generation data products at Thumbtack, leveraging AI models for code generation and incorporating agents into our workflows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience designing and building data sets and warehouses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent ability to understand the needs of and collaborate with stakeholders in other functions, especially Analytics, and identify opportunities for process improvements across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in SQL for analytics/reporting/business intelligence and also for building SQL- and Python-based transforms inside an ETL pipeline, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing, architecting, and maintaining a data warehouse and data marts that seamlessly stitches together data from production databases, clickstream data, and external APIs to serve multiple stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise building the above with a modern data stack based on a cloud-native data warehouse, in our case we use BigQuery, dbt, and Apache Airflow, but a similar stack is fine.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using AI to generate design plans, code and documentation as well as applying AI-enabled workflows to accelerate development velocity and improve data engineering practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sense of ownership and pride in your work, from ideation and requirements-gathering to project completion and maintenance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE DATA ENGINEERING TEAM\n\nThumbtack’s Data Engineering org is split into 3 groups: Core Data Engineering, Data Platform and Embedded Data Engineering. This role is on the Embedded Data Engineering team, which breaks down into multiple business units that data engineers are embedded into. This role would be on the commercial operations side of the house and will work closely with engineers, analysts, data scientists and machine learning engineers to help design and curate data sets originating from internal and third-party sources to meet current and future needs. Over the next year, it will continue to build on its prior successes in building a more cohesive data warehouse while starting to work more deeply upstream to build data best practices into the full software development lifecycle (SDLC).\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThere are several teams all over Thumbtack with Terabytes of data and unique challenges trying to clean and organize this data to measure their performance.  In this role, you will work with Engineers, Data Scientists, Managers, and others to understand their needs, and actively work to build datasets to tackle these challenges.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Collaboratively refine and evangelize a comprehensive framework for integrating data-thinking into the software development lifecycle for product teams.\n\n - Design, architect, and maintain core operations datasets, data marts, and feature stores that support a blend of mature products and features with a rapidly evolving product line, in partnership with analytics, data science, and machine learning.\n\n - Integrate deeply with our cross functional partners to understand their data needs, and help design datasets with the same engineering rigor as any other software we design.\n\n - Drive data quality and best practices across different business areas.\n\n - Help build the next generation data products at Thumbtack, leveraging AI models for code generation and incorporating agents into our workflows.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 4+ years of experience designing and building data sets and warehouses.\n\n - Excellent ability to understand the needs of and collaborate with stakeholders in other functions, especially Analytics, and identify opportunities for process improvements across teams.\n\n - Expertise in SQL for analytics/reporting/business intelligence and also for building SQL- and Python-based transforms inside an ETL pipeline, or similar.\n\n - Experience designing, architecting, and maintaining a data warehouse and data marts that seamlessly stitches together data from production databases, clickstream data, and external APIs to serve multiple stakeholders.\n\n - Expertise building the above with a modern data stack based on a cloud-native data warehouse, in our case we use BigQuery, dbt, and Apache Airflow, but a similar stack is fine.\n\n - Experience using AI to generate design plans, code and documentation as well as applying AI-enabled workflows to accelerate development velocity and improve data engineering practices.\n\n - Strong sense of ownership and pride in your work, from ideation and requirements-gathering to project completion and maintenance.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $210,800.00 - $272,800.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $189,600.00 - $245,300.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $179,400.00 - $232,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6d2c77ba-1678-4682-8908-e6416e5e29ff","title":"Partner Success Manager II – Demand Partnerships ","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T22:16:03.083+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6d2c77ba-1678-4682-8908-e6416e5e29ff","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6d2c77ba-1678-4682-8908-e6416e5e29ff/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2>About the Demand Partnerships Team</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Demand Partnerships team builds and grows strategic partnerships that expand customer demand across Thumbtack's marketplace. We work cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Operations, and external partners to develop scalable integrations, launch new capabilities, and unlock new marketplace opportunities. Our team combines strategic partnership management with operational excellence to deliver measurable business outcomes for both our partners and Thumbtack.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Partner Success Manager II, you will own a portfolio of Thumbtack's most strategic Demand API partners, serving as both the executive relationship owner and trusted business advisor responsible for long-term partner success and marketplace growth. You'll leverage data, market insights, and a deep understanding of partner objectives to develop account strategies, identify expansion opportunities, and influence cross-functional decisions that improve partner and marketplace performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success in this role requires balancing strategic thinking with operational excellence. You'll lead complex initiatives across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Operations, and Support to launch new capabilities, solve partner challenges, and scale programs that create value beyond your own portfolio. Your work will directly influence Thumbtack's partnership strategy, Demand API platform, and long-term marketplace growth.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the strategy, performance, and long-term growth of a portfolio of Thumbtack's highest-impact Demand API partners, driving partner health, retention, expansion, and measurable business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted executive relationships and develop strategic account plans that align partner priorities with Thumbtack's long-term marketplace strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead complex cross-functional initiatives across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Operations, and other teams to launch integrations, new capabilities, and go-to-market initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use partner performance data, market insights, and business trends to identify growth opportunities, influence strategic decisions, and improve marketplace outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Engineering to shape roadmap priorities while identifying and executing partner expansion opportunities from business case through launch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and scale partner success strategies, operational improvements, and best practices while serving as a subject matter expert within the Demand Partnerships organization.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, customer success, business development, account management, or a similar customer-facing role with increasing ownership and complexity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success managing strategic or enterprise partnerships, building executive relationships, and delivering measurable business growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to develop data-driven strategies, identify growth opportunities, and lead complex cross-functional initiatives in ambiguous environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong business acumen with experience influencing senior stakeholders, building business cases, and balancing partner needs with company priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with API, platform, or systems integrations, with the ability to translate technical concepts into business value for technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication, analytical, stakeholder management, and project leadership skills. Experience working with retailers, e-commerce companies, marketplaces, or other large consumer-facing partners is a plus.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected base salary range for the role is currently $85,000 - $117,000, with a potential On-Target Earning (OTE)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $85,000 - $117,000, with a potential On-Target Earning (OTE).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $85,000 - $117,000, with a potential On-Target Earning (OTE)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE DEMAND PARTNERSHIPS TEAM\n\nThe Demand Partnerships team builds and grows strategic partnerships that expand customer demand across Thumbtack's marketplace. We work cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Operations, and external partners to develop scalable integrations, launch new capabilities, and unlock new marketplace opportunities. Our team combines strategic partnership management with operational excellence to deliver measurable business outcomes for both our partners and Thumbtack.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs a Partner Success Manager II, you will own a portfolio of Thumbtack's most strategic Demand API partners, serving as both the executive relationship owner and trusted business advisor responsible for long-term partner success and marketplace growth. You'll leverage data, market insights, and a deep understanding of partner objectives to develop account strategies, identify expansion opportunities, and influence cross-functional decisions that improve partner and marketplace performance.\n\nSuccess in this role requires balancing strategic thinking with operational excellence. You'll lead complex initiatives across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Operations, and Support to launch new capabilities, solve partner challenges, and scale programs that create value beyond your own portfolio. Your work will directly influence Thumbtack's partnership strategy, Demand API platform, and long-term marketplace growth.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own the strategy, performance, and long-term growth of a portfolio of Thumbtack's highest-impact Demand API partners, driving partner health, retention, expansion, and measurable business outcomes.\n\n - Build trusted executive relationships and develop strategic account plans that align partner priorities with Thumbtack's long-term marketplace strategy.\n\n - Lead complex cross-functional initiatives across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Operations, and other teams to launch integrations, new capabilities, and go-to-market initiatives.\n\n - Use partner performance data, market insights, and business trends to identify growth opportunities, influence strategic decisions, and improve marketplace outcomes.\n\n - Partner with Product and Engineering to shape roadmap priorities while identifying and executing partner expansion opportunities from business case through launch.\n\n - Design and scale partner success strategies, operational improvements, and best practices while serving as a subject matter expert within the Demand Partnerships organization.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 5+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, customer success, business development, account management, or a similar customer-facing role with increasing ownership and complexity.\n\n - Demonstrated success managing strategic or enterprise partnerships, building executive relationships, and delivering measurable business growth.\n\n - Proven ability to develop data-driven strategies, identify growth opportunities, and lead complex cross-functional initiatives in ambiguous environments.\n\n - Strong business acumen with experience influencing senior stakeholders, building business cases, and balancing partner needs with company priorities.\n\n - Experience working with API, platform, or systems integrations, with the ability to translate technical concepts into business value for technical and non-technical audiences.\n\n - Excellent communication, analytical, stakeholder management, and project leadership skills. Experience working with retailers, e-commerce companies, marketplaces, or other large consumer-facing partners is a plus.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected base salary range for the role is currently $85,000 - $117,000, with a potential On-Target Earning (OTE)\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $85,000 - $117,000, with a potential On-Target Earning (OTE).\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $85,000 - $117,000, with a potential On-Target Earning (OTE)\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1ded15c4-4268-4565-b900-867807645823","title":"Senior Data Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T21:06:32.619+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/1ded15c4-4268-4565-b900-867807645823","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/1ded15c4-4268-4565-b900-867807645823/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Data Engineering Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack’s Data Engineering org is split into 3 groups: Core Data Engineering, Data Platform and Embedded Data Engineering. This role is on the Embedded Data Engineering team, which breaks down into multiple business units that data engineers are embedded into. This role would be on the commercial operations side of the house and will work closely with engineers, analysts, data scientists and machine learning engineers to help design and curate data sets originating from internal and third-party sources to meet current and future needs. Over the next year, it will continue to build on its prior successes in building a more cohesive data warehouse while starting to work more deeply upstream to build data best practices into the full software development lifecycle (SDLC).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The challenge</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">There are several teams all over Thumbtack with Terabytes of data and unique challenges trying to clean and organize this data to measure their performance.  In this role, you will work with Engineers, Data Scientists, Managers, and others to understand their needs, and actively work to build datasets to tackle these challenges.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboratively refine and evangelize a comprehensive framework for integrating data-thinking into the software development lifecycle for product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, architect, and maintain core operations datasets, data marts, and feature stores that support a blend of mature products and features with a rapidly evolving product line, in partnership with analytics, data science, and machine learning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Integrate deeply with our cross functional partners to understand their data needs, and help design datasets with the same engineering rigor as any other software we design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive data quality and best practices across different business areas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build the next generation data products at Thumbtack, leveraging AI models for code generation and incorporating agents into our workflows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience designing and building data sets and warehouses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent ability to understand the needs of and collaborate with stakeholders in other functions, especially Analytics, and identify opportunities for process improvements across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in SQL for analytics/reporting/business intelligence and also for building SQL- and Python-based transforms inside an ETL pipeline, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing, architecting, and maintaining a data warehouse and data marts that seamlessly stitches together data from production databases, clickstream data, and external APIs to serve multiple stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise building the above with a modern data stack based on a cloud-native data warehouse, in our case we use BigQuery, dbt, and Apache Airflow, but a similar stack is fine.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using AI to generate design plans, code and documentation as well as applying AI-enabled workflows to accelerate development velocity and improve data engineering practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sense of ownership and pride in your work, from ideation and requirements-gathering to project completion and maintenance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE DATA ENGINEERING TEAM\n\nThumbtack’s Data Engineering org is split into 3 groups: Core Data Engineering, Data Platform and Embedded Data Engineering. This role is on the Embedded Data Engineering team, which breaks down into multiple business units that data engineers are embedded into. This role would be on the commercial operations side of the house and will work closely with engineers, analysts, data scientists and machine learning engineers to help design and curate data sets originating from internal and third-party sources to meet current and future needs. Over the next year, it will continue to build on its prior successes in building a more cohesive data warehouse while starting to work more deeply upstream to build data best practices into the full software development lifecycle (SDLC).\n\n\n\n\nTHE CHALLENGE\n\nThere are several teams all over Thumbtack with Terabytes of data and unique challenges trying to clean and organize this data to measure their performance.  In this role, you will work with Engineers, Data Scientists, Managers, and others to understand their needs, and actively work to build datasets to tackle these challenges.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Collaboratively refine and evangelize a comprehensive framework for integrating data-thinking into the software development lifecycle for product teams.\n\n - Design, architect, and maintain core operations datasets, data marts, and feature stores that support a blend of mature products and features with a rapidly evolving product line, in partnership with analytics, data science, and machine learning.\n\n - Integrate deeply with our cross functional partners to understand their data needs, and help design datasets with the same engineering rigor as any other software we design.\n\n - Drive data quality and best practices across different business areas.\n\n - Help build the next generation data products at Thumbtack, leveraging AI models for code generation and incorporating agents into our workflows.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 4+ years of experience designing and building data sets and warehouses.\n\n - Excellent ability to understand the needs of and collaborate with stakeholders in other functions, especially Analytics, and identify opportunities for process improvements across teams.\n\n - Expertise in SQL for analytics/reporting/business intelligence and also for building SQL- and Python-based transforms inside an ETL pipeline, or similar.\n\n - Experience designing, architecting, and maintaining a data warehouse and data marts that seamlessly stitches together data from production databases, clickstream data, and external APIs to serve multiple stakeholders.\n\n - Expertise building the above with a modern data stack based on a cloud-native data warehouse, in our case we use BigQuery, dbt, and Apache Airflow, but a similar stack is fine.\n\n - Experience using AI to generate design plans, code and documentation as well as applying AI-enabled workflows to accelerate development velocity and improve data engineering practices.\n\n - Strong sense of ownership and pride in your work, from ideation and requirements-gathering to project completion and maintenance.\n\n\n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"73f01c2f-103a-4627-928b-4dedcc2a3013","title":"Cybersecurity Senior Analyst","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T05:40:51.086+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Manila","addressCountry":"Philippines","addressLocality":"Makati City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/73f01c2f-103a-4627-928b-4dedcc2a3013","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/73f01c2f-103a-4627-928b-4dedcc2a3013/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Cybersecurity Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Security Engineering team at Thumbtack is focused on enabling innovation at scale by making the secure path the easiest path. We believe strong security is not a blocker to velocity, but a force multiplier when it is designed into systems, platforms, and developer workflows from the start.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We partner closely with Product, Engineering, Platform, and Data teams to shape system design, guide architectural decisions, and evolve Thumbtack’s security posture as the company scales. Through collaboration, automation, and thoughtful tradeoffs, we help ensure Thumbtack can ship fast, innovate boldly, and maintain customer trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Thumbtack scales, the volume and variety of security telemetry grows with it, spanning cloud infrastructure, SaaS applications, endpoints, and identity systems. We’re looking for a Cybersecurity Senior Analyst to help build and operate a detection and response capability that is fast, high-fidelity, and increasingly automated.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll be a cornerstone of our day-to-day security operations, treating detections as code, tuning our SIEM for signal over noise, partnering closely with our MDR provider, and automating response workflows so that human attention is reserved for the incidents that matter most. You’ll combine hands-on security operations with an engineering mindset, continuously finding ways to improve our detections, processes, and tooling as Thumbtack evolves.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">While security operations will be your primary focus, you’ll also support the broader security program and flex into areas such as GRC, third-party risk, and vulnerability management as needed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own day-to-day security operations: monitoring, triage, and investigation of security alerts across our production, corporate, and SaaS environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and continuously improve our SIEM: log source onboarding, parsing and normalization, detection rule development and tuning, and cost/coverage optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage our MDR (Managed Detection &amp; Response) partnership: escalation workflows, SLAs, detection feedback loops, and quality of response.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead security incidents end-to-end: triage, scoping, containment, eradication, recovery, and blameless post-incident reviews.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build automation that reduces manual toil and response times: SOAR playbooks, detection-as-code pipelines, enrichment integrations, and response scripting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct proactive threat hunting informed by threat intelligence and knowledge of Thumbtack’s environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define, track, and report on operational metrics (e.g. MTTD, MTTR, alert fidelity, coverage against ATT&amp;CK) and use them to drive improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply AI tools to accelerate security operations, and continuously adapt our detections, processes, and tooling to address evolving and novel threats, including AI-related risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Security Engineering, Platform, IT, and Compliance to close detection gaps and improve our overall security posture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the broader security program as needed: GRC (audit support, evidence collection, control monitoring), endpoint security, network security, third party risk reviews, vulnerability management (scanning, triage, and remediation coordination), etc.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in security operations, detection &amp; response, or a related security engineering discipline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep hands-on experience operating and tuning a SIEM, including detection engineering and log pipeline management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing or working closely with an MDR/MSSP partner, including escalation design and holding vendors accountable to quality and SLAs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong incident response skills across cloud-native environments (AWS and/or GCP), SaaS applications, endpoints, and identity systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with AI tools in daily security work, and the adaptability to evolve detections, processes, and tooling to address novel and emerging threats, including AI-related risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scripting and automation proficiency (e.g. Python), with experience building SOAR playbooks, detection-as-code, or similar automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Risk-based, analytical thinking: the judgment to prioritize what matters, tune out noise, and articulate trade-offs between coverage, fidelity, and effort.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working familiarity with adjacent security domains, including GRC and compliance frameworks (e.g. SOC 2, PCI DSS), third party risk assessment, and vulnerability management, with the flexibility to support them as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including clear incident communications, and the ability to collaborate effectively with a distributed, primarily US-based team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE CYBERSECURITY TEAM\n\nThe Security Engineering team at Thumbtack is focused on enabling innovation at scale by making the secure path the easiest path. We believe strong security is not a blocker to velocity, but a force multiplier when it is designed into systems, platforms, and developer workflows from the start.\n\nWe partner closely with Product, Engineering, Platform, and Data teams to shape system design, guide architectural decisions, and evolve Thumbtack’s security posture as the company scales. Through collaboration, automation, and thoughtful tradeoffs, we help ensure Thumbtack can ship fast, innovate boldly, and maintain customer trust.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Thumbtack scales, the volume and variety of security telemetry grows with it, spanning cloud infrastructure, SaaS applications, endpoints, and identity systems. We’re looking for a Cybersecurity Senior Analyst to help build and operate a detection and response capability that is fast, high-fidelity, and increasingly automated.\n\nIn this role, you’ll be a cornerstone of our day-to-day security operations, treating detections as code, tuning our SIEM for signal over noise, partnering closely with our MDR provider, and automating response workflows so that human attention is reserved for the incidents that matter most. You’ll combine hands-on security operations with an engineering mindset, continuously finding ways to improve our detections, processes, and tooling as Thumbtack evolves.\n\nWhile security operations will be your primary focus, you’ll also support the broader security program and flex into areas such as GRC, third-party risk, and vulnerability management as needed.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own day-to-day security operations: monitoring, triage, and investigation of security alerts across our production, corporate, and SaaS environments.\n\n - Manage and continuously improve our SIEM: log source onboarding, parsing and normalization, detection rule development and tuning, and cost/coverage optimization.\n\n - Manage our MDR (Managed Detection & Response) partnership: escalation workflows, SLAs, detection feedback loops, and quality of response.\n\n - Lead security incidents end-to-end: triage, scoping, containment, eradication, recovery, and blameless post-incident reviews.\n\n - Build automation that reduces manual toil and response times: SOAR playbooks, detection-as-code pipelines, enrichment integrations, and response scripting.\n\n - Conduct proactive threat hunting informed by threat intelligence and knowledge of Thumbtack’s environment.\n\n - Define, track, and report on operational metrics (e.g. MTTD, MTTR, alert fidelity, coverage against ATT&CK) and use them to drive improvement.\n\n - Apply AI tools to accelerate security operations, and continuously adapt our detections, processes, and tooling to address evolving and novel threats, including AI-related risks.\n\n - Partner with Security Engineering, Platform, IT, and Compliance to close detection gaps and improve our overall security posture.\n\n - Support the broader security program as needed: GRC (audit support, evidence collection, control monitoring), endpoint security, network security, third party risk reviews, vulnerability management (scanning, triage, and remediation coordination), etc.\n\n\n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 6+ years of experience in security operations, detection & response, or a related security engineering discipline.\n\n - Deep hands-on experience operating and tuning a SIEM, including detection engineering and log pipeline management.\n\n - Experience managing or working closely with an MDR/MSSP partner, including escalation design and holding vendors accountable to quality and SLAs.\n\n - Strong incident response skills across cloud-native environments (AWS and/or GCP), SaaS applications, endpoints, and identity systems.\n\n - Fluency with AI tools in daily security work, and the adaptability to evolve detections, processes, and tooling to address novel and emerging threats, including AI-related risks.\n\n - Scripting and automation proficiency (e.g. Python), with experience building SOAR playbooks, detection-as-code, or similar automation.\n\n - Risk-based, analytical thinking: the judgment to prioritize what matters, tune out noise, and articulate trade-offs between coverage, fidelity, and effort.\n\n - Working familiarity with adjacent security domains, including GRC and compliance frameworks (e.g. SOC 2, PCI DSS), third party risk assessment, and vulnerability management, with the flexibility to support them as needed.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including clear incident communications, and the ability to collaborate effectively with a distributed, primarily US-based team\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"114e85c7-83e4-42c2-aa3f-242560adf9a2","title":"Sr. Finance Mgr, Partnerships and Special Projects","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T21:34:28.655+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/114e85c7-83e4-42c2-aa3f-242560adf9a2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/114e85c7-83e4-42c2-aa3f-242560adf9a2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the </strong>Finance<strong> Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Thumbtack Finance team’s mission is to be a strategic finance partner to the business — enabling better decisions supported by data, building a world-class finance function, and doing it all with integrity. We work closely with every part of the organization to connect financial insight to business outcomes and help Thumbtack grow responsibly. Our team values clear thinking, sound analysis, and a genuine partnership with the leaders we support.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Senior Manager, Partnerships and Special Projects Business Finance, you’ll help define how we grow our business through our network of partners, build frameworks that enable us to scale efficiently, and influence strategic decision-making.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will build the financial framework that powers one of our biggest growth levers. You’ll partner with Product, Marketing, Operations, Sales, and Finance leaders to evaluate where we should invest, how to scale partnerships profitably, and where opportunities exist to expand into new verticals. Approximately 25% of the role will focus on special projects designed to build scalable frameworks that help keep both sides of the marketplace in equilibrium and guide investment decisions accordingly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a strategic finance role for someone who can move beyond reporting and forecasting into business architecture, deal economics, decision support, and investment strategy. The ideal candidate is highly analytical, commercially minded, and comfortable bringing structure to ambiguous marketplace problems.<br /></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve the company’s partnership financial framework, helping teams develop sustainable financial strategies and evaluate valuation, payback periods, scenario analysis, and revenue-share structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reporting infrastructure and KPI dashboards to monitor the ongoing ROI of partnerships, hold cross-functional partners accountable to financial commitments, and identify actions to improve performance when results are off track</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop business cases for major partner investments, pricing levers, supply acquisition, demand generation, and operational capacity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support annual planning, quarterly business reviews, and resource allocation by connecting partnership strategy and execution to the company’s financial goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build executive-ready narratives that clearly explain marketplace performance, investment tradeoffs, risks, opportunities, and recommended actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Analytics and Data Science to build dashboards and decision tools that give business leaders visibility into partnership health and investment performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead special projects focused on developing scalable financial frameworks that inform marketplace investment decisions and help maintain healthy supply-and-demand dynamics<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in strategic finance, FP&amp;A, marketplace strategy, business operations, corporate strategy, consulting, analytics, or a related function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong financial modeling skills, including experience with driver-based models, cohort models, unit economics, LTV/CAC, contribution margin, ROI analysis, scenario planning, and long-range planning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of marketplace dynamics, including supply-and-demand balance, liquidity, matching, utilization, pricing, incentives, retention, and monetization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to translate complex analysis into clear, actionable recommendations for senior executives and cross-functional partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to build concise executive narratives and influence stakeholders across Finance, Product, Marketing, Sales, and Operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL, BI, AI fluency, or data visualization experience preferred but not required, depending on the analytics support model</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $191,300.00 - $247,500.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $172,600.00 - $223,300.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $162,400.00 - $210,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE FINANCE TEAM\n\nThe Thumbtack Finance team’s mission is to be a strategic finance partner to the business — enabling better decisions supported by data, building a world-class finance function, and doing it all with integrity. We work closely with every part of the organization to connect financial insight to business outcomes and help Thumbtack grow responsibly. Our team values clear thinking, sound analysis, and a genuine partnership with the leaders we support.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Senior Manager, Partnerships and Special Projects Business Finance, you’ll help define how we grow our business through our network of partners, build frameworks that enable us to scale efficiently, and influence strategic decision-making.\n\nThis role will build the financial framework that powers one of our biggest growth levers. You’ll partner with Product, Marketing, Operations, Sales, and Finance leaders to evaluate where we should invest, how to scale partnerships profitably, and where opportunities exist to expand into new verticals. Approximately 25% of the role will focus on special projects designed to build scalable frameworks that help keep both sides of the marketplace in equilibrium and guide investment decisions accordingly.\n\nThis is a strategic finance role for someone who can move beyond reporting and forecasting into business architecture, deal economics, decision support, and investment strategy. The ideal candidate is highly analytical, commercially minded, and comfortable bringing structure to ambiguous marketplace problems.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own and evolve the company’s partnership financial framework, helping teams develop sustainable financial strategies and evaluate valuation, payback periods, scenario analysis, and revenue-share structures\n\n - Establish reporting infrastructure and KPI dashboards to monitor the ongoing ROI of partnerships, hold cross-functional partners accountable to financial commitments, and identify actions to improve performance when results are off track\n\n - Develop business cases for major partner investments, pricing levers, supply acquisition, demand generation, and operational capacity\n\n - Support annual planning, quarterly business reviews, and resource allocation by connecting partnership strategy and execution to the company’s financial goals\n\n - Build executive-ready narratives that clearly explain marketplace performance, investment tradeoffs, risks, opportunities, and recommended actions\n\n - Partner with Analytics and Data Science to build dashboards and decision tools that give business leaders visibility into partnership health and investment performance\n\n - Lead special projects focused on developing scalable financial frameworks that inform marketplace investment decisions and help maintain healthy supply-and-demand dynamics\n   \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 6+ years of experience in strategic finance, FP&A, marketplace strategy, business operations, corporate strategy, consulting, analytics, or a related function\n\n - Strong financial modeling skills, including experience with driver-based models, cohort models, unit economics, LTV/CAC, contribution margin, ROI analysis, scenario planning, and long-range planning\n\n - Strong understanding of marketplace dynamics, including supply-and-demand balance, liquidity, matching, utilization, pricing, incentives, retention, and monetization\n\n - Ability to translate complex analysis into clear, actionable recommendations for senior executives and cross-functional partners\n\n - Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to build concise executive narratives and influence stakeholders across Finance, Product, Marketing, Sales, and Operations\n\n - SQL, BI, AI fluency, or data visualization experience preferred but not required, depending on the analytics support model\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $191,300.00 - $247,500.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $172,600.00 - $223,300.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $162,400.00 - $210,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6c846bc0-d08a-4aba-9cc1-3100a8e398dd","title":"Senior Brand Manager","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:16:57.550+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6c846bc0-d08a-4aba-9cc1-3100a8e398dd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6c846bc0-d08a-4aba-9cc1-3100a8e398dd/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Brand Strategy Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We act as the architects of the Thumbtack brand - claiming a distinct position in the market, defining a brand promise that delivers on that position, and partnering with skilled experts across the company to bring it to life. Our work spans brand insights, brand strategy, content strategy, and integrated marketing. We set the roadmap for the brand and extend our influence beyond Marketing &amp; Communications into all parts of the organization to make sure every touchpoint strengthens the brand.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Senior Brand Manager focused on our pro audience, you’ll help define how we position the company, what we promise pros, and how that promise comes to life across every touchpoint. Reporting directly to the Director of Brand Strategy, you’ll set vision for major brand workstreams while shaping how the team and the company think about the pro side of our brand.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead foundational workstreams to help roll out our new brand playbook, including defining pro positioning and content strategy, educating and training partner teams, and more — and refresh these artifacts as the market shifts and new learnings emerge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify high-leverage opportunities for the brand to drive growth on the pro side of our business, then translate them into clear creative briefs and strategic direction for internal and external creative partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own pro brand insights work that informs strategy — including audience deep dives, creative experimentation, competitive analysis, and brand health tracking — and turn findings into clear, actionable recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with channel owners across Marketing and Communications to translate pro brand strategy into an integrated content strategy and creative calendar that meets business and brand goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extend the brand’s influence beyond Marketing and Communications by building relationships with cross-functional partners in the product, service and sales organizations; create proactive moments to communicate brand vision and align company priorities to it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead brand support for AI-driven content, building prompts, skills, brand review systems, and other infrastructure that allows the brand to scale as content creation becomes more decentralized.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Orchestrate brand strategy and creative work for tentpole moments, including campaign launches, product launches, and major events like our annual Pro Summit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a senior voice on the Brand Strategy team — setting standards, shaping how we work, and driving alignment with leadership and cross-functional stakeholders.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-8+ years of brand marketing experience, with a strong focus on brand strategy, positioning, and messaging; experience marketing to SMBs is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience defining and implementing brand strategy - including brand promises, positioning frameworks, playbooks, and messaging architecture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience setting brand vision and roadmap, not just managing executions - comfortable operating upstream of campaigns and influencing how the broader org thinks about brand</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and managing brand health measurement programs (brand tracking, awareness, perception, brand lift) and translating findings into clear strategic action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong creative judgment, including experience writing compelling creative briefs, providing strategic guidance to creative agencies and in-house studios, and partnering with creative teams to develop standout work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and running creative experimentation programs that improve campaign performance and feed back into brand strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical rigor — comfortable planning and executing research with the help of internal or external research partners. Adept at synthesizing quantitative and qualitative data into insights, recommendations, and business cases</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $147,100 - $190,300.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $132,600 - $171,600.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $125,000 - $161,700.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE BRAND STRATEGY TEAM\n\nWe act as the architects of the Thumbtack brand - claiming a distinct position in the market, defining a brand promise that delivers on that position, and partnering with skilled experts across the company to bring it to life. Our work spans brand insights, brand strategy, content strategy, and integrated marketing. We set the roadmap for the brand and extend our influence beyond Marketing & Communications into all parts of the organization to make sure every touchpoint strengthens the brand.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Senior Brand Manager focused on our pro audience, you’ll help define how we position the company, what we promise pros, and how that promise comes to life across every touchpoint. Reporting directly to the Director of Brand Strategy, you’ll set vision for major brand workstreams while shaping how the team and the company think about the pro side of our brand.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead foundational workstreams to help roll out our new brand playbook, including defining pro positioning and content strategy, educating and training partner teams, and more — and refresh these artifacts as the market shifts and new learnings emerge.\n\n - Identify high-leverage opportunities for the brand to drive growth on the pro side of our business, then translate them into clear creative briefs and strategic direction for internal and external creative partners.\n\n - Own pro brand insights work that informs strategy — including audience deep dives, creative experimentation, competitive analysis, and brand health tracking — and turn findings into clear, actionable recommendations.\n\n - Partner with channel owners across Marketing and Communications to translate pro brand strategy into an integrated content strategy and creative calendar that meets business and brand goals.\n\n - Extend the brand’s influence beyond Marketing and Communications by building relationships with cross-functional partners in the product, service and sales organizations; create proactive moments to communicate brand vision and align company priorities to it.\n\n - Lead brand support for AI-driven content, building prompts, skills, brand review systems, and other infrastructure that allows the brand to scale as content creation becomes more decentralized.\n\n - Orchestrate brand strategy and creative work for tentpole moments, including campaign launches, product launches, and major events like our annual Pro Summit.\n\n - Serve as a senior voice on the Brand Strategy team — setting standards, shaping how we work, and driving alignment with leadership and cross-functional stakeholders.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 6-8+ years of brand marketing experience, with a strong focus on brand strategy, positioning, and messaging; experience marketing to SMBs is a plus\n\n - Experience defining and implementing brand strategy - including brand promises, positioning frameworks, playbooks, and messaging architecture\n\n - Experience setting brand vision and roadmap, not just managing executions - comfortable operating upstream of campaigns and influencing how the broader org thinks about brand\n\n - Experience designing and managing brand health measurement programs (brand tracking, awareness, perception, brand lift) and translating findings into clear strategic action\n\n - Strong creative judgment, including experience writing compelling creative briefs, providing strategic guidance to creative agencies and in-house studios, and partnering with creative teams to develop standout work\n\n - Experience designing and running creative experimentation programs that improve campaign performance and feed back into brand strategy\n\n - Analytical rigor — comfortable planning and executing research with the help of internal or external research partners. Adept at synthesizing quantitative and qualitative data into insights, recommendations, and business cases\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $147,100 - $190,300.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $132,600 - $171,600.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $125,000 - $161,700.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6f36232c-f98f-4590-8f82-99319d1c7037","title":"Senior Brand Manager","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:17:03.952+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6f36232c-f98f-4590-8f82-99319d1c7037","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/6f36232c-f98f-4590-8f82-99319d1c7037/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Brand Strategy Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We act as the architects of the Thumbtack brand - claiming a distinct position in the market, defining a brand promise that delivers on that position, and partnering with skilled experts across the company to bring it to life. Our work spans brand insights, brand strategy, content strategy, and integrated marketing. We set the roadmap for the brand and extend our influence beyond Marketing &amp; Communications into all parts of the organization to make sure every touchpoint strengthens the brand.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Senior Brand Manager focused on our pro audience, you’ll help define how we position the company, what we promise pros, and how that promise comes to life across every touchpoint. Reporting directly to the Director of Brand Strategy, you’ll set vision for major brand workstreams while shaping how the team and the company think about the pro side of our brand.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead foundational workstreams to help roll out our new brand playbook, including defining pro positioning and content strategy, educating and training partner teams, and more — and refresh these artifacts as the market shifts and new learnings emerge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify high-leverage opportunities for the brand to drive growth on the pro side of our business, then translate them into clear creative briefs and strategic direction for internal and external creative partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own pro brand insights work that informs strategy — including audience deep dives, creative experimentation, competitive analysis, and brand health tracking — and turn findings into clear, actionable recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with channel owners across Marketing and Communications to translate pro brand strategy into an integrated content strategy and creative calendar that meets business and brand goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extend the brand’s influence beyond Marketing and Communications by building relationships with cross-functional partners in the product, service and sales organizations; create proactive moments to communicate brand vision and align company priorities to it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead brand support for AI-driven content, building prompts, skills, brand review systems, and other infrastructure that allows the brand to scale as content creation becomes more decentralized.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Orchestrate brand strategy and creative work for tentpole moments, including campaign launches, product launches, and major events like our annual Pro Summit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a senior voice on the Brand Strategy team — setting standards, shaping how we work, and driving alignment with leadership and cross-functional stakeholders.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-8+ years of brand marketing experience, with a strong focus on brand strategy, positioning, and messaging; experience marketing to SMBs is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience defining and implementing brand strategy - including brand promises, positioning frameworks, playbooks, and messaging architecture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience setting brand vision and roadmap, not just managing executions - comfortable operating upstream of campaigns and influencing how the broader org thinks about brand</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and managing brand health measurement programs (brand tracking, awareness, perception, brand lift) and translating findings into clear strategic action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong creative judgment, including experience writing compelling creative briefs, providing strategic guidance to creative agencies and in-house studios, and partnering with creative teams to develop standout work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and running creative experimentation programs that improve campaign performance and feed back into brand strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical rigor — comfortable planning and executing research with the help of internal or external research partners. Adept at synthesizing quantitative and qualitative data into insights, recommendations, and business cases</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong>.</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $117,300 - $151,800.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE BRAND STRATEGY TEAM\n\nWe act as the architects of the Thumbtack brand - claiming a distinct position in the market, defining a brand promise that delivers on that position, and partnering with skilled experts across the company to bring it to life. Our work spans brand insights, brand strategy, content strategy, and integrated marketing. We set the roadmap for the brand and extend our influence beyond Marketing & Communications into all parts of the organization to make sure every touchpoint strengthens the brand.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Senior Brand Manager focused on our pro audience, you’ll help define how we position the company, what we promise pros, and how that promise comes to life across every touchpoint. Reporting directly to the Director of Brand Strategy, you’ll set vision for major brand workstreams while shaping how the team and the company think about the pro side of our brand.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead foundational workstreams to help roll out our new brand playbook, including defining pro positioning and content strategy, educating and training partner teams, and more — and refresh these artifacts as the market shifts and new learnings emerge.\n\n - Identify high-leverage opportunities for the brand to drive growth on the pro side of our business, then translate them into clear creative briefs and strategic direction for internal and external creative partners.\n\n - Own pro brand insights work that informs strategy — including audience deep dives, creative experimentation, competitive analysis, and brand health tracking — and turn findings into clear, actionable recommendations.\n\n - Partner with channel owners across Marketing and Communications to translate pro brand strategy into an integrated content strategy and creative calendar that meets business and brand goals.\n\n - Extend the brand’s influence beyond Marketing and Communications by building relationships with cross-functional partners in the product, service and sales organizations; create proactive moments to communicate brand vision and align company priorities to it.\n\n - Lead brand support for AI-driven content, building prompts, skills, brand review systems, and other infrastructure that allows the brand to scale as content creation becomes more decentralized.\n\n - Orchestrate brand strategy and creative work for tentpole moments, including campaign launches, product launches, and major events like our annual Pro Summit.\n\n - Serve as a senior voice on the Brand Strategy team — setting standards, shaping how we work, and driving alignment with leadership and cross-functional stakeholders.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 6-8+ years of brand marketing experience, with a strong focus on brand strategy, positioning, and messaging; experience marketing to SMBs is a plus\n\n - Experience defining and implementing brand strategy - including brand promises, positioning frameworks, playbooks, and messaging architecture\n\n - Experience setting brand vision and roadmap, not just managing executions - comfortable operating upstream of campaigns and influencing how the broader org thinks about brand\n\n - Experience designing and managing brand health measurement programs (brand tracking, awareness, perception, brand lift) and translating findings into clear strategic action\n\n - Strong creative judgment, including experience writing compelling creative briefs, providing strategic guidance to creative agencies and in-house studios, and partnering with creative teams to develop standout work\n\n - Experience designing and running creative experimentation programs that improve campaign performance and feed back into brand strategy\n\n - Analytical rigor — comfortable planning and executing research with the help of internal or external research partners. Adept at synthesizing quantitative and qualitative data into insights, recommendations, and business cases\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES.\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected salary range for the role is currently $117,300 - $151,800.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3d3a24fc-588c-4a11-972a-f9fd46ff0f06","title":"Director, Organizational Development","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:18:38.706+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/3d3a24fc-588c-4a11-972a-f9fd46ff0f06","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/3d3a24fc-588c-4a11-972a-f9fd46ff0f06/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the People Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The People team builds the systems, programs, and culture that let a virtual-first, AI-first company move fast without losing its edge. Organizational Development sits at the center of that work — designing how Thumbtack develops leaders, grows careers, structures teams, and navigates change. We’re a small, senior team with an unusually wide surface area: our programs reach every employee, and our partners are the executives running the business.<br /></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re seeking a Director of Talent &amp; Organizational Development to raise both the floor and the bar for performance and capability across Thumbtack, building the talent systems, leadership practices, and developmental plan to enable our talent to scale ahead of the business. Reporting to the Head of People, you’ll set the multi-year direction for an integrated portfolio spanning performance management, career architecture, talent and succession planning, leadership development, organizational design, and enterprise change.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on leadership role. You’ll lead a small team of experienced practitioners while partnering directly with senior leaders and HRBPs on Thumbtack’s highest-priority talent and organizational challenges. You’ll move comfortably between company-wide strategy and detailed execution: advising leaders, designing frameworks and operating rhythms, building development experiences, and ensuring the work translates into stronger performance, deeper talent density, and clearer paths for growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your initial priorities will include strengthening how Thumbtack sets and evaluates performance expectations; evolving career, talent, and succession frameworks; building leadership and organizational capabilities for the company’s next stage; and establishing a clear measurement system for the impact of these investments.<br /></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and own Thumbtack’s multi-year Talent and Organizational Development strategy, integrating performance management, career architecture, talent and succession planning, leadership development, and change into a focused roadmap with measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve how Thumbtack defines, enables, and assesses performance strengthening goal setting, expectations, feedback, calibration, and accountability so high performance is clear, consistent, and differentiated.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and evolve the company’s career architecture, including role and level frameworks, capability expectations, and career paths that give employees clarity and support consistent talent decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead talent planning and succession practices that help leaders assess talent, identify critical capability and bench gaps, accelerate high-potential employees, and make deliberate decisions about the organization’s future needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design scalable development experiences that close meaningful capability gaps, strengthen manager effectiveness, and prepare senior leaders for greater complexity and scope.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply an AI-first approach across the portfolio, building workflows that improve insight, personalization, and scale while helping managers and leaders develop the capabilities needed to lead in an AI-first company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish an integrated measurement framework for Talent and Organizational Development, using business, talent, and program data to evaluate impact and determine what to scale, change, or stop.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience across talent management, organizational development, learning and development, or related disciplines, including 4+ years leading and developing people</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in talent management—including performance, career architecture, talent planning, and succession—along with demonstrated strength in leadership development, organizational effectiveness, and change management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of personally designing and implementing scalable talent and organizational solutions, with clear evidence of the performance, capability, or business outcomes they produced</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Credibility with senior leaders and the ability to lead through ambiguity, influence without formal authority, and turn complex or sensitive issues into decisions and action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An AI-first approach to work, including hands-on experience building multi-step workflows and sound judgment about the use of AI in sensitive people processes and decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A player-coach orientation and analytical mindset: comfortable moving between strategy and detailed execution, grounding solutions in adult-learning and talent-management practices, and using data to improve what you build<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $270,000 - $330,000.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $243,000 - $297,000.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $230,000 - $281,000.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PEOPLE TEAM\n\nThe People team builds the systems, programs, and culture that let a virtual-first, AI-first company move fast without losing its edge. Organizational Development sits at the center of that work — designing how Thumbtack develops leaders, grows careers, structures teams, and navigates change. We’re a small, senior team with an unusually wide surface area: our programs reach every employee, and our partners are the executives running the business.\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe’re seeking a Director of Talent & Organizational Development to raise both the floor and the bar for performance and capability across Thumbtack, building the talent systems, leadership practices, and developmental plan to enable our talent to scale ahead of the business. Reporting to the Head of People, you’ll set the multi-year direction for an integrated portfolio spanning performance management, career architecture, talent and succession planning, leadership development, organizational design, and enterprise change.\n\nThis is a hands-on leadership role. You’ll lead a small team of experienced practitioners while partnering directly with senior leaders and HRBPs on Thumbtack’s highest-priority talent and organizational challenges. You’ll move comfortably between company-wide strategy and detailed execution: advising leaders, designing frameworks and operating rhythms, building development experiences, and ensuring the work translates into stronger performance, deeper talent density, and clearer paths for growth.\n\nYour initial priorities will include strengthening how Thumbtack sets and evaluates performance expectations; evolving career, talent, and succession frameworks; building leadership and organizational capabilities for the company’s next stage; and establishing a clear measurement system for the impact of these investments.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Set and own Thumbtack’s multi-year Talent and Organizational Development strategy, integrating performance management, career architecture, talent and succession planning, leadership development, and change into a focused roadmap with measurable outcomes.\n\n - Evolve how Thumbtack defines, enables, and assesses performance strengthening goal setting, expectations, feedback, calibration, and accountability so high performance is clear, consistent, and differentiated.\n\n - Maintain and evolve the company’s career architecture, including role and level frameworks, capability expectations, and career paths that give employees clarity and support consistent talent decisions.\n\n - Lead talent planning and succession practices that help leaders assess talent, identify critical capability and bench gaps, accelerate high-potential employees, and make deliberate decisions about the organization’s future needs.\n\n - Design scalable development experiences that close meaningful capability gaps, strengthen manager effectiveness, and prepare senior leaders for greater complexity and scope.\n\n - Apply an AI-first approach across the portfolio, building workflows that improve insight, personalization, and scale while helping managers and leaders develop the capabilities needed to lead in an AI-first company.\n\n - Establish an integrated measurement framework for Talent and Organizational Development, using business, talent, and program data to evaluate impact and determine what to scale, change, or stop.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 10+ years of experience across talent management, organizational development, learning and development, or related disciplines, including 4+ years leading and developing people\n\n - Deep expertise in talent management—including performance, career architecture, talent planning, and succession—along with demonstrated strength in leadership development, organizational effectiveness, and change management\n\n - A track record of personally designing and implementing scalable talent and organizational solutions, with clear evidence of the performance, capability, or business outcomes they produced\n\n - Credibility with senior leaders and the ability to lead through ambiguity, influence without formal authority, and turn complex or sensitive issues into decisions and action\n\n - An AI-first approach to work, including hands-on experience building multi-step workflows and sound judgment about the use of AI in sensitive people processes and decisions\n\n - A player-coach orientation and analytical mindset: comfortable moving between strategy and detailed execution, grounding solutions in adult-learning and talent-management practices, and using data to improve what you build\n   \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected salary range for the role is currently $270,000 - $330,000.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected salary range for the role is currently $243,000 - $297,000.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected salary range for this role is currently $230,000 - $281,000.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"602052fe-52e0-4c37-9ca6-2c10776b3f50","title":"Manager, Partner Operations","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:12:37.632+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/602052fe-52e0-4c37-9ca6-2c10776b3f50","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/602052fe-52e0-4c37-9ca6-2c10776b3f50/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Commercial Strategy Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Commercial Strategy team sits within the Business Development &amp; Commercial Programs org and is responsible for helping take ideas from 0 to 1 by leading strategic initiatives and bets, and partnering cross functionally with other teams to test, experiment, and implement new strategies. The Partner Operations sub-team is the engine behind Thumbtack's partnerships business. We build the scalable systems, processes, and infrastructure that turn partner opportunities into operational reality. Beyond running the day-to-day, we lead high-priority strategic initiatives and early-stage pilots that don't fit neatly into existing lanes, coordinate cross-functionally to align workflows and ownership for new capabilities, and drive the transition from pilot to scalable operations. When we do our job well, partners grow, capabilities expand, and revenue grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Manager, Partner Operations, you will lead a portfolio of strategic programs that help grow and scale Thumbtack’s partnerships business. Reporting to the Senior Manager of Partnership Operations, you’ll manage a globally distributed team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines while working across the organization to turn high-potential opportunities into durable business capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will operate at the intersection of strategy, program leadership, and operations. Your work may include building and scaling new growth programs, developing go-to-market strategies, improving business performance and economics, strengthening partner-facing capabilities, and evolving the systems and processes that support our partnerships. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-impact player-coach role for a versatile operator who can set direction, lead complex execution, and deliver measurable outcomes. You will bring structure to ambiguous opportunities, move fluidly between strategy and execution, and align teams across functions to take programs from concept through launch and scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead a portfolio of strategic programs</strong>: Lead and own high-impact initiatives that accelerate the growth and scalability of Thumbtack’s partnerships business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and scale new business capabilities</strong>: Take emerging opportunities from concept through launch and scale, establishing the operating processes, systems, and cross-functional model required for reliable execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own measurable business outcomes</strong>: Define success measures, monitor performance, identify limiting factors, and make clear recommendations that improve growth, efficiency, operational performance, and program economics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead complex programs end to end</strong>: Serve as the central hub across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Marketing, Commercial Operations, Commercial Strategy, Legal, and external partners to translate strategy into coordinated execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shape strategy through analytical insight</strong>: Use data, customer and partner insights, and structured problem-solving to evaluate opportunities, make tradeoffs, and influence investment decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strengthen the Partner Operations foundation</strong>: Improve the tools, systems, processes, and operating models that enable partnerships to launch and scale reliably.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead a globally distributed team</strong>: Set a clear vision and priorities while managing and developing a team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines to become increasingly independent owners.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in strategy and operations, business operations, program management, general management, management consulting, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of people-management experience, with a demonstrated ability to set direction, develop talent, and lead a team of operators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience translating ambiguous business opportunities into clear strategies, operating plans, and measurable results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of leading complex initiatives from concept through execution, including stepping toward problems and taking accountability when results fall short.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong business judgment and analytical rigor, with the ability to assess performance, understand economics, evaluate tradeoffs, and determine where to invest.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, influential communication skills, with the ability to create a compelling vision, distill complexity, align diverse stakeholders, and influence without authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An owner mentality, strong learning agility, a bias for action, and a low-ego approach to leadership and collaboration.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable)<strong> </strong>range<strong> </strong>for the role is currently $153,000.00 - $198,000.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range<strong> </strong>for the role is currently $137,700.00 - $178,200.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range<strong> </strong>for the role is currently $130,100.00 - $168,300.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE COMMERCIAL STRATEGY TEAM\n\nThe Commercial Strategy team sits within the Business Development & Commercial Programs org and is responsible for helping take ideas from 0 to 1 by leading strategic initiatives and bets, and partnering cross functionally with other teams to test, experiment, and implement new strategies. The Partner Operations sub-team is the engine behind Thumbtack's partnerships business. We build the scalable systems, processes, and infrastructure that turn partner opportunities into operational reality. Beyond running the day-to-day, we lead high-priority strategic initiatives and early-stage pilots that don't fit neatly into existing lanes, coordinate cross-functionally to align workflows and ownership for new capabilities, and drive the transition from pilot to scalable operations. When we do our job well, partners grow, capabilities expand, and revenue grows.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Manager, Partner Operations, you will lead a portfolio of strategic programs that help grow and scale Thumbtack’s partnerships business. Reporting to the Senior Manager of Partnership Operations, you’ll manage a globally distributed team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines while working across the organization to turn high-potential opportunities into durable business capabilities.\n\nYou will operate at the intersection of strategy, program leadership, and operations. Your work may include building and scaling new growth programs, developing go-to-market strategies, improving business performance and economics, strengthening partner-facing capabilities, and evolving the systems and processes that support our partnerships. \n\nThis is a high-impact player-coach role for a versatile operator who can set direction, lead complex execution, and deliver measurable outcomes. You will bring structure to ambiguous opportunities, move fluidly between strategy and execution, and align teams across functions to take programs from concept through launch and scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead a portfolio of strategic programs: Lead and own high-impact initiatives that accelerate the growth and scalability of Thumbtack’s partnerships business.\n\n - Build and scale new business capabilities: Take emerging opportunities from concept through launch and scale, establishing the operating processes, systems, and cross-functional model required for reliable execution.\n\n - Own measurable business outcomes: Define success measures, monitor performance, identify limiting factors, and make clear recommendations that improve growth, efficiency, operational performance, and program economics.\n\n - Lead complex programs end to end: Serve as the central hub across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Marketing, Commercial Operations, Commercial Strategy, Legal, and external partners to translate strategy into coordinated execution.\n\n - Shape strategy through analytical insight: Use data, customer and partner insights, and structured problem-solving to evaluate opportunities, make tradeoffs, and influence investment decisions.\n\n - Strengthen the Partner Operations foundation: Improve the tools, systems, processes, and operating models that enable partnerships to launch and scale reliably.\n\n - Lead a globally distributed team: Set a clear vision and priorities while managing and developing a team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines to become increasingly independent owners.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 5+ years of experience in strategy and operations, business operations, program management, general management, management consulting, or a related field.\n\n - 2+ years of people-management experience, with a demonstrated ability to set direction, develop talent, and lead a team of operators.\n\n - Experience translating ambiguous business opportunities into clear strategies, operating plans, and measurable results.\n\n - A track record of leading complex initiatives from concept through execution, including stepping toward problems and taking accountability when results fall short.\n\n - Strong business judgment and analytical rigor, with the ability to assess performance, understand economics, evaluate tradeoffs, and determine where to invest.\n\n - Clear, influential communication skills, with the ability to create a compelling vision, distill complexity, align diverse stakeholders, and influence without authority.\n\n - An owner mentality, strong learning agility, a bias for action, and a low-ego approach to leadership and collaboration.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $153,000.00 - $198,000.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $137,700.00 - $178,200.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $130,100.00 - $168,300.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"499fc892-28ad-489d-83eb-e1d1d9842305","title":"Manager, Partner Operations","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:12:33.550+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/499fc892-28ad-489d-83eb-e1d1d9842305","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/499fc892-28ad-489d-83eb-e1d1d9842305/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Commercial Strategy Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Commercial Strategy team sits within the Business Development &amp; Commercial Programs org and is responsible for helping take ideas from 0 to 1 by leading strategic initiatives and bets, and partnering cross functionally with other teams to test, experiment, and implement new strategies. The Partner Operations sub-team is the engine behind Thumbtack's partnerships business. We build the scalable systems, processes, and infrastructure that turn partner opportunities into operational reality. Beyond running the day-to-day, we lead high-priority strategic initiatives and early-stage pilots that don't fit neatly into existing lanes, coordinate cross-functionally to align workflows and ownership for new capabilities, and drive the transition from pilot to scalable operations. When we do our job well, partners grow, capabilities expand, and revenue grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Manager, Partner Operations, you will lead a portfolio of strategic programs that help grow and scale Thumbtack’s partnerships business. Reporting to the Senior Manager of Partnership Operations, you’ll manage a globally distributed team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines while working across the organization to turn high-potential opportunities into durable business capabilities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will operate at the intersection of strategy, program leadership, and operations. Your work may include building and scaling new growth programs, developing go-to-market strategies, improving business performance and economics, strengthening partner-facing capabilities, and evolving the systems and processes that support our partnerships. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-impact player-coach role for a versatile operator who can set direction, lead complex execution, and deliver measurable outcomes. You will bring structure to ambiguous opportunities, move fluidly between strategy and execution, and align teams across functions to take programs from concept through launch and scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead a portfolio of strategic programs</strong>: Lead and own high-impact initiatives that accelerate the growth and scalability of Thumbtack’s partnerships business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and scale new business capabilities</strong>: Take emerging opportunities from concept through launch and scale, establishing the operating processes, systems, and cross-functional model required for reliable execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own measurable business outcomes</strong>: Define success measures, monitor performance, identify limiting factors, and make clear recommendations that improve growth, efficiency, operational performance, and program economics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead complex programs end to end</strong>: Serve as the central hub across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Marketing, Commercial Operations, Commercial Strategy, Legal, and external partners to translate strategy into coordinated execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shape strategy through analytical insight</strong>: Use data, customer and partner insights, and structured problem-solving to evaluate opportunities, make tradeoffs, and influence investment decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strengthen the Partner Operations foundation</strong>: Improve the tools, systems, processes, and operating models that enable partnerships to launch and scale reliably.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead a globally distributed team</strong>: Set a clear vision and priorities while managing and developing a team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines to become increasingly independent owners.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in strategy and operations, business operations, program management, general management, management consulting, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of people-management experience, with a demonstrated ability to set direction, develop talent, and lead a team of operators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience translating ambiguous business opportunities into clear strategies, operating plans, and measurable results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of leading complex initiatives from concept through execution, including stepping toward problems and taking accountability when results fall short.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong business judgment and analytical rigor, with the ability to assess performance, understand economics, evaluate tradeoffs, and determine where to invest.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, influential communication skills, with the ability to create a compelling vision, distill complexity, align diverse stakeholders, and influence without authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An owner mentality, strong learning agility, a bias for action, and a low-ego approach to leadership and collaboration.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range<strong> </strong>for the role is currently $120,700.00 - $156,200.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE COMMERCIAL STRATEGY TEAM\n\nThe Commercial Strategy team sits within the Business Development & Commercial Programs org and is responsible for helping take ideas from 0 to 1 by leading strategic initiatives and bets, and partnering cross functionally with other teams to test, experiment, and implement new strategies. The Partner Operations sub-team is the engine behind Thumbtack's partnerships business. We build the scalable systems, processes, and infrastructure that turn partner opportunities into operational reality. Beyond running the day-to-day, we lead high-priority strategic initiatives and early-stage pilots that don't fit neatly into existing lanes, coordinate cross-functionally to align workflows and ownership for new capabilities, and drive the transition from pilot to scalable operations. When we do our job well, partners grow, capabilities expand, and revenue grows.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Manager, Partner Operations, you will lead a portfolio of strategic programs that help grow and scale Thumbtack’s partnerships business. Reporting to the Senior Manager of Partnership Operations, you’ll manage a globally distributed team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines while working across the organization to turn high-potential opportunities into durable business capabilities.\n\nYou will operate at the intersection of strategy, program leadership, and operations. Your work may include building and scaling new growth programs, developing go-to-market strategies, improving business performance and economics, strengthening partner-facing capabilities, and evolving the systems and processes that support our partnerships. \n\nThis is a high-impact player-coach role for a versatile operator who can set direction, lead complex execution, and deliver measurable outcomes. You will bring structure to ambiguous opportunities, move fluidly between strategy and execution, and align teams across functions to take programs from concept through launch and scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead a portfolio of strategic programs: Lead and own high-impact initiatives that accelerate the growth and scalability of Thumbtack’s partnerships business.\n\n - Build and scale new business capabilities: Take emerging opportunities from concept through launch and scale, establishing the operating processes, systems, and cross-functional model required for reliable execution.\n\n - Own measurable business outcomes: Define success measures, monitor performance, identify limiting factors, and make clear recommendations that improve growth, efficiency, operational performance, and program economics.\n\n - Lead complex programs end to end: Serve as the central hub across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Marketing, Commercial Operations, Commercial Strategy, Legal, and external partners to translate strategy into coordinated execution.\n\n - Shape strategy through analytical insight: Use data, customer and partner insights, and structured problem-solving to evaluate opportunities, make tradeoffs, and influence investment decisions.\n\n - Strengthen the Partner Operations foundation: Improve the tools, systems, processes, and operating models that enable partnerships to launch and scale reliably.\n\n - Lead a globally distributed team: Set a clear vision and priorities while managing and developing a team of three to four people across the U.S. and the Philippines to become increasingly independent owners.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 5+ years of experience in strategy and operations, business operations, program management, general management, management consulting, or a related field.\n\n - 2+ years of people-management experience, with a demonstrated ability to set direction, develop talent, and lead a team of operators.\n\n - Experience translating ambiguous business opportunities into clear strategies, operating plans, and measurable results.\n\n - A track record of leading complex initiatives from concept through execution, including stepping toward problems and taking accountability when results fall short.\n\n - Strong business judgment and analytical rigor, with the ability to assess performance, understand economics, evaluate tradeoffs, and determine where to invest.\n\n - Clear, influential communication skills, with the ability to create a compelling vision, distill complexity, align diverse stakeholders, and influence without authority.\n\n - An owner mentality, strong learning agility, a bias for action, and a low-ego approach to leadership and collaboration.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $120,700.00 - $156,200.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"323602c6-082f-4c92-953d-642eccb0ed7f","title":"Product Manager, Pro Integrations & Foundations","department":"Product Management","team":"Product Management","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T21:59:29.248+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/323602c6-082f-4c92-953d-642eccb0ed7f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/323602c6-082f-4c92-953d-642eccb0ed7f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Pro Activation &amp; Success Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack's Pro Activation &amp; Success pillar helps local service businesses discover Thumbtack, get started, find success, and grow with us over time. We build products and experiences that help more pros thrive, partnering closely with marketing, partnerships, and sales across the full pro journey. We're a highly collaborative, data-driven team united by a simple goal: helping pros build stronger businesses.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack was originally built to serve individual professionals and small businesses. Now, larger and more sophisticated businesses represent one of our biggest opportunities for growth — and serving them well requires us to rethink what Thumbtack can offer. In this role, you'll shape how we win with this segment, from connecting Thumbtack with the tools pros use to run their businesses to creating the foundational experiences they need to succeed at scale. You'll work closely with our partnerships and business development teams to turn integrations into meaningful growth, identify and scale new growth levers tailored to this segment, and bring differentiated products to market.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for unlocking growth among larger, more sophisticated pros, with accountability for customer and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a deep understanding of how these pros operate, using research and data to identify unmet needs, product gaps, and new opportunities for growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the strategy for our APIs, data integrations, and partner offerings, working directly with partnerships, business development, and external partners to create value for pros and open new growth channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead new products and capabilities from early discovery through launch and adoption, helping complex businesses succeed on a product originally designed for smaller businesses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with engineering to make thoughtful tradeoffs between near-term opportunities and durable technical foundations that can support future products and partnerships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring engineering, design, data science, marketing, sales, and partnerships together around clear priorities and lead execution across organizational boundaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define success, test the highest-potential ideas, and use what you learn to scale the experiences and growth levers that deliver meaningful results.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of product management experience, with a track record of owning complex product areas and delivering meaningful customer and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience turning ambiguous, early stage opportunities into clear product strategies and taking new products from discovery through launch and adoption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical fluency and experience owning technically complex products, with the ability to partner with engineering on APIs, data, integrations, and system tradeoffs while keeping customer value at the center.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent product judgment and customer empathy, with the ability to understand complex business workflows and turn them into simple, intuitive experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical thinking and business acumen, including the ability to uncover growth opportunities, define success, and balance near-term impact with long-term investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An AI-first mindset: curiosity, adaptability, and enthusiasm for using agentic AI workflows throughout product development, paired with sound judgment about where AI adds value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to influence and lead across engineering, design, data science, commercial teams, and external stakeholders, using clear communication to navigate different incentives and build alignment.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $200,600.00 - $259,600.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $170,900.00 - $221,100.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PRO ACTIVATION & SUCCESS TEAM\n\nThumbtack's Pro Activation & Success pillar helps local service businesses discover Thumbtack, get started, find success, and grow with us over time. We build products and experiences that help more pros thrive, partnering closely with marketing, partnerships, and sales across the full pro journey. We're a highly collaborative, data-driven team united by a simple goal: helping pros build stronger businesses.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThumbtack was originally built to serve individual professionals and small businesses. Now, larger and more sophisticated businesses represent one of our biggest opportunities for growth — and serving them well requires us to rethink what Thumbtack can offer. In this role, you'll shape how we win with this segment, from connecting Thumbtack with the tools pros use to run their businesses to creating the foundational experiences they need to succeed at scale. You'll work closely with our partnerships and business development teams to turn integrations into meaningful growth, identify and scale new growth levers tailored to this segment, and bring differentiated products to market.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for unlocking growth among larger, more sophisticated pros, with accountability for customer and business outcomes.\n\n - Develop a deep understanding of how these pros operate, using research and data to identify unmet needs, product gaps, and new opportunities for growth.\n\n - Set the strategy for our APIs, data integrations, and partner offerings, working directly with partnerships, business development, and external partners to create value for pros and open new growth channels.\n\n - Lead new products and capabilities from early discovery through launch and adoption, helping complex businesses succeed on a product originally designed for smaller businesses.\n\n - Partner with engineering to make thoughtful tradeoffs between near-term opportunities and durable technical foundations that can support future products and partnerships.\n\n - Bring engineering, design, data science, marketing, sales, and partnerships together around clear priorities and lead execution across organizational boundaries.\n\n - Define success, test the highest-potential ideas, and use what you learn to scale the experiences and growth levers that deliver meaningful results.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 5+ years of product management experience, with a track record of owning complex product areas and delivering meaningful customer and business outcomes.\n\n - Experience turning ambiguous, early stage opportunities into clear product strategies and taking new products from discovery through launch and adoption.\n\n - Strong technical fluency and experience owning technically complex products, with the ability to partner with engineering on APIs, data, integrations, and system tradeoffs while keeping customer value at the center.\n\n - Excellent product judgment and customer empathy, with the ability to understand complex business workflows and turn them into simple, intuitive experiences.\n\n - Strong analytical thinking and business acumen, including the ability to uncover growth opportunities, define success, and balance near-term impact with long-term investments.\n\n - An AI-first mindset: curiosity, adaptability, and enthusiasm for using agentic AI workflows throughout product development, paired with sound judgment about where AI adds value.\n\n - Proven ability to influence and lead across engineering, design, data science, commercial teams, and external stakeholders, using clear communication to navigate different incentives and build alignment.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $200,600.00 - $259,600.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $180,200.00 - $233,200.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $170,900.00 - $221,100.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"245a9552-23a1-439e-83c5-fd840961dcec","title":"Product Manager, Pro Integrations & Foundations ","department":"Product Management","team":"Product Management","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T21:59:33.662+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/245a9552-23a1-439e-83c5-fd840961dcec","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/245a9552-23a1-439e-83c5-fd840961dcec/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Pro Activation &amp; Success Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack's Pro Activation &amp; Success pillar helps local service businesses discover Thumbtack, get started, find success, and grow with us over time. We build products and experiences that help more pros thrive, partnering closely with marketing, partnerships, and sales across the full pro journey. We're a highly collaborative, data-driven team united by a simple goal: helping pros build stronger businesses.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack was originally built to serve individual professionals and small businesses. Now, larger and more sophisticated businesses represent one of our biggest opportunities for growth — and serving them well requires us to rethink what Thumbtack can offer. In this role, you'll shape how we win with this segment, from connecting Thumbtack with the tools pros use to run their businesses to creating the foundational experiences they need to succeed at scale. You'll work closely with our partnerships and business development teams to turn integrations into meaningful growth, identify and scale new growth levers tailored to this segment, and bring differentiated products to market.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for unlocking growth among larger, more sophisticated pros, with accountability for customer and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a deep understanding of how these pros operate, using research and data to identify unmet needs, product gaps, and new opportunities for growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the strategy for our APIs, data integrations, and partner offerings, working directly with partnerships, business development, and external partners to create value for pros and open new growth channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead new products and capabilities from early discovery through launch and adoption, helping complex businesses succeed on a product originally designed for smaller businesses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with engineering to make thoughtful tradeoffs between near-term opportunities and durable technical foundations that can support future products and partnerships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring engineering, design, data science, marketing, sales, and partnerships together around clear priorities and lead execution across organizational boundaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define success, test the highest-potential ideas, and use what you learn to scale the experiences and growth levers that deliver meaningful results.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of product management experience, with a track record of owning complex product areas and delivering meaningful customer and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience turning ambiguous, early stage opportunities into clear product strategies and taking new products from discovery through launch and adoption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical fluency and experience owning technically complex products, with the ability to partner with engineering on APIs, data, integrations, and system tradeoffs while keeping customer value at the center.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent product judgment and customer empathy, with the ability to understand complex business workflows and turn them into simple, intuitive experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical thinking and business acumen, including the ability to uncover growth opportunities, define success, and balance near-term impact with long-term investments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An AI-first mindset: curiosity, adaptability, and enthusiasm for using agentic AI workflows throughout product development, paired with sound judgment about where AI adds value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to influence and lead across engineering, design, data science, commercial teams, and external stakeholders, using clear communication to navigate different incentives and build alignment.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $164,100.00 - $212,300.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE PRO ACTIVATION & SUCCESS TEAM\n\nThumbtack's Pro Activation & Success pillar helps local service businesses discover Thumbtack, get started, find success, and grow with us over time. We build products and experiences that help more pros thrive, partnering closely with marketing, partnerships, and sales across the full pro journey. We're a highly collaborative, data-driven team united by a simple goal: helping pros build stronger businesses.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThumbtack was originally built to serve individual professionals and small businesses. Now, larger and more sophisticated businesses represent one of our biggest opportunities for growth — and serving them well requires us to rethink what Thumbtack can offer. In this role, you'll shape how we win with this segment, from connecting Thumbtack with the tools pros use to run their businesses to creating the foundational experiences they need to succeed at scale. You'll work closely with our partnerships and business development teams to turn integrations into meaningful growth, identify and scale new growth levers tailored to this segment, and bring differentiated products to market.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for unlocking growth among larger, more sophisticated pros, with accountability for customer and business outcomes.\n\n - Develop a deep understanding of how these pros operate, using research and data to identify unmet needs, product gaps, and new opportunities for growth.\n\n - Set the strategy for our APIs, data integrations, and partner offerings, working directly with partnerships, business development, and external partners to create value for pros and open new growth channels.\n\n - Lead new products and capabilities from early discovery through launch and adoption, helping complex businesses succeed on a product originally designed for smaller businesses.\n\n - Partner with engineering to make thoughtful tradeoffs between near-term opportunities and durable technical foundations that can support future products and partnerships.\n\n - Bring engineering, design, data science, marketing, sales, and partnerships together around clear priorities and lead execution across organizational boundaries.\n\n - Define success, test the highest-potential ideas, and use what you learn to scale the experiences and growth levers that deliver meaningful results.\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 5+ years of product management experience, with a track record of owning complex product areas and delivering meaningful customer and business outcomes.\n\n - Experience turning ambiguous, early stage opportunities into clear product strategies and taking new products from discovery through launch and adoption.\n\n - Strong technical fluency and experience owning technically complex products, with the ability to partner with engineering on APIs, data, integrations, and system tradeoffs while keeping customer value at the center.\n\n - Excellent product judgment and customer empathy, with the ability to understand complex business workflows and turn them into simple, intuitive experiences.\n\n - Strong analytical thinking and business acumen, including the ability to uncover growth opportunities, define success, and balance near-term impact with long-term investments.\n\n - An AI-first mindset: curiosity, adaptability, and enthusiasm for using agentic AI workflows throughout product development, paired with sound judgment about where AI adds value.\n\n - Proven ability to influence and lead across engineering, design, data science, commercial teams, and external stakeholders, using clear communication to navigate different incentives and build alignment.\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $164,100.00 - $212,300.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bcb16bb9-aef4-4bd7-8e52-a5b707b08d20","title":"Director, Product Design","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T15:38:31.042+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/bcb16bb9-aef4-4bd7-8e52-a5b707b08d20","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/bcb16bb9-aef4-4bd7-8e52-a5b707b08d20/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Design Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a tight-knit team of product designers, researchers, and content designers working closely with engineers and product managers to research, explore, and iterate on well-crafted user experiences that are innovative, engaging, and delightful. We collaborate regularly through design critiques, work sessions, and presentations to inspire and influence the direction of the product and company as a whole.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thumbtack, we're building the most trusted way for people to care for their homes. Delivering on that promise means meeting homeowners at every doorway into our product — from the partners who bring them to Thumbtack to the experiences that keep them coming back. Our Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen teams sit at the front of that mission: Demand Partnerships builds the strategic relationships — retail and OEM platforms like Lowe's, GenAI platforms like OpenAI and Gemini, and new verticals like real estate and property management — that create new entry points into Thumbtack, while Demand Gen owns the acquisition, lifecycle, and experience-led growth work that turns demand into lasting engagement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Director of Product Design to lead design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar. This is a senior leadership role responsible for setting vision, elevating craft, and driving strategy across multiple teams spanning partner-facing and homeowner-facing experiences. You'll build strong cross-functional partnerships with Business Development, Marketing, and Engineering leadership, and lead a high-performing design organization to deliver impactful, user-centered experiences at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and scale Product Design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar, overseeing multiple teams and designers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and drive a clear, compelling vision and north star that guides product and experience decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor and develop the skills, talents, and careers of the designers on your team, coaching them to success and impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Engineering, Research, and Data leaders (as well as cross-functional partners in Business Development and Marketing) to shape strategy and drive business impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure consistent delivery of high-quality, user-centered design solutions across teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish effective team processes, operating models, and org design to scale design impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion user-centered thinking and integrate research and data into decision-making</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience managing product designers, including senior-level talent and/or managers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of driving product vision and strategy across complex, cross-functional environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Craft and Systems Thinking: a high bar for visual, interaction, and systems thinking across experiences, and ability to raise quality through teams rather than individual contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional cross-functional leadership and influence at senior and executive levels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and scaling high-performing design teams and inclusive team cultures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep commitment to user-centered design, with strong partnership with Research and Data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading product design for growth and/or demand-generation experiences, with a track record of improving acquisition, conversion, activation, and/or retention through experimentation, data, and user insight</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $293,300.00 - $379,500.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $264,400.00 - $342,100.00.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $249,100.00 - $322,300.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE DESIGN TEAM\n\nWe're a tight-knit team of product designers, researchers, and content designers working closely with engineers and product managers to research, explore, and iterate on well-crafted user experiences that are innovative, engaging, and delightful. We collaborate regularly through design critiques, work sessions, and presentations to inspire and influence the direction of the product and company as a whole.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAt Thumbtack, we're building the most trusted way for people to care for their homes. Delivering on that promise means meeting homeowners at every doorway into our product — from the partners who bring them to Thumbtack to the experiences that keep them coming back. Our Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen teams sit at the front of that mission: Demand Partnerships builds the strategic relationships — retail and OEM platforms like Lowe's, GenAI platforms like OpenAI and Gemini, and new verticals like real estate and property management — that create new entry points into Thumbtack, while Demand Gen owns the acquisition, lifecycle, and experience-led growth work that turns demand into lasting engagement.\n\nWe're looking for a Director of Product Design to lead design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar. This is a senior leadership role responsible for setting vision, elevating craft, and driving strategy across multiple teams spanning partner-facing and homeowner-facing experiences. You'll build strong cross-functional partnerships with Business Development, Marketing, and Engineering leadership, and lead a high-performing design organization to deliver impactful, user-centered experiences at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead and scale Product Design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar, overseeing multiple teams and designers\n\n - Define and drive a clear, compelling vision and north star that guides product and experience decisions\n\n - Mentor and develop the skills, talents, and careers of the designers on your team, coaching them to success and impact\n\n - Partner with Product, Engineering, Research, and Data leaders (as well as cross-functional partners in Business Development and Marketing) to shape strategy and drive business impact\n\n - Ensure consistent delivery of high-quality, user-centered design solutions across teams\n\n - Establish effective team processes, operating models, and org design to scale design impact\n\n - Champion user-centered thinking and integrate research and data into decision-making\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 10+ years of experience managing product designers, including senior-level talent and/or managers\n\n - Proven track record of driving product vision and strategy across complex, cross-functional environments\n\n - Craft and Systems Thinking: a high bar for visual, interaction, and systems thinking across experiences, and ability to raise quality through teams rather than individual contribution\n\n - Exceptional cross-functional leadership and influence at senior and executive levels\n\n - Experience building and scaling high-performing design teams and inclusive team cultures\n\n - Deep commitment to user-centered design, with strong partnership with Research and Data\n\n - Experience leading product design for growth and/or demand-generation experiences, with a track record of improving acquisition, conversion, activation, and/or retention through experimentation, data, and user insight\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in San Francisco / Bay Area, San Jose, New York City, or Seattle metros, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $293,300.00 - $379,500.00.\n\n - For candidates living in Austin, TX or Washington DC metros or in California, Massachusetts, New Jersey, or Washington states, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for the role is currently $264,400.00 - $342,100.00.\n\n - For candidates living in all other US locations, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $249,100.00 - $322,300.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"197d5a24-4e1e-4e86-b153-93edb78e3f7e","title":"Director, Product Design","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote, Ontario","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote, British Columbia","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"British Columbia","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Victoria"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T15:38:37.860+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Ontario","addressCountry":"Canada","addressLocality":"Toronto"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/197d5a24-4e1e-4e86-b153-93edb78e3f7e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thumbtack/197d5a24-4e1e-4e86-b153-93edb78e3f7e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Thumbtack helps millions of people confidently care for their homes.</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.</p><h2><strong>About the Design Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a tight-knit team of product designers, researchers, and content designers working closely with engineers and product managers to research, explore, and iterate on well-crafted user experiences that are innovative, engaging, and delightful. We collaborate regularly through design critiques, work sessions, and presentations to inspire and influence the direction of the product and company as a whole.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thumbtack, we're building the most trusted way for people to care for their homes. Delivering on that promise means meeting homeowners at every doorway into our product — from the partners who bring them to Thumbtack to the experiences that keep them coming back. Our Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen teams sit at the front of that mission: Demand Partnerships builds the strategic relationships — retail and OEM platforms like Lowe's, GenAI platforms like OpenAI and Gemini, and new verticals like real estate and property management — that create new entry points into Thumbtack, while Demand Gen owns the acquisition, lifecycle, and experience-led growth work that turns demand into lasting engagement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Director of Product Design to lead design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar. This is a senior leadership role responsible for setting vision, elevating craft, and driving strategy across multiple teams spanning partner-facing and homeowner-facing experiences. You'll build strong cross-functional partnerships with Business Development, Marketing, and Engineering leadership, and lead a high-performing design organization to deliver impactful, user-centered experiences at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and scale Product Design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar, overseeing multiple teams and designers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and drive a clear, compelling vision and north star that guides product and experience decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor and develop the skills, talents, and careers of the designers on your team, coaching them to success and impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Engineering, Research, and Data leaders (as well as cross-functional partners in Business Development and Marketing) to shape strategy and drive business impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure consistent delivery of high-quality, user-centered design solutions across teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish effective team processes, operating models, and org design to scale design impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion user-centered thinking and integrate research and data into decision-making</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>In order to be successful, you must bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience managing product designers, including senior-level talent and/or managers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of driving product vision and strategy across complex, cross-functional environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Craft and Systems Thinking: a high bar for visual, interaction, and systems thinking across experiences, and ability to raise quality through teams rather than individual contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional cross-functional leadership and influence at senior and executive levels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and scaling high-performing design teams and inclusive team cultures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep commitment to user-centered design, with strong partnership with Research and Data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading product design for growth and/or demand-generation experiences, with a track record of improving acquisition, conversion, activation, and/or retention through experimentation, data, and user insight</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Expected salary ranges</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $226,100.00 - $292,600.00.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:recruitingops@thumbtack.com\"><u>recruitingops@thumbtack.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy\"><u>Job Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams\"><u>Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes.</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"THUMBTACK HELPS MILLIONS OF PEOPLE CONFIDENTLY CARE FOR THEIR HOMES.\n\nThumbtack is the one app you need to take care of and improve your home — from personalized guidance to AI tools and a best-in-class hiring experience. Every day in every county of the U.S., people turn to Thumbtack to complete urgent repairs, seasonal maintenance and bigger improvements. We help homeowners know which projects to do, when to do them and who to hire from our growing community of 300,000 local service businesses. If making an impact inspires you, join us. Imagine what we’ll build together.\n\n\nABOUT THE DESIGN TEAM\n\nWe're a tight-knit team of product designers, researchers, and content designers working closely with engineers and product managers to research, explore, and iterate on well-crafted user experiences that are innovative, engaging, and delightful. We collaborate regularly through design critiques, work sessions, and presentations to inspire and influence the direction of the product and company as a whole.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAt Thumbtack, we're building the most trusted way for people to care for their homes. Delivering on that promise means meeting homeowners at every doorway into our product — from the partners who bring them to Thumbtack to the experiences that keep them coming back. Our Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen teams sit at the front of that mission: Demand Partnerships builds the strategic relationships — retail and OEM platforms like Lowe's, GenAI platforms like OpenAI and Gemini, and new verticals like real estate and property management — that create new entry points into Thumbtack, while Demand Gen owns the acquisition, lifecycle, and experience-led growth work that turns demand into lasting engagement.\n\nWe're looking for a Director of Product Design to lead design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar. This is a senior leadership role responsible for setting vision, elevating craft, and driving strategy across multiple teams spanning partner-facing and homeowner-facing experiences. You'll build strong cross-functional partnerships with Business Development, Marketing, and Engineering leadership, and lead a high-performing design organization to deliver impactful, user-centered experiences at scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead and scale Product Design across the Demand Partnerships and Demand Gen pillar, overseeing multiple teams and designers\n\n - Define and drive a clear, compelling vision and north star that guides product and experience decisions\n\n - Mentor and develop the skills, talents, and careers of the designers on your team, coaching them to success and impact\n\n - Partner with Product, Engineering, Research, and Data leaders (as well as cross-functional partners in Business Development and Marketing) to shape strategy and drive business impact\n\n - Ensure consistent delivery of high-quality, user-centered design solutions across teams\n\n - Establish effective team processes, operating models, and org design to scale design impact\n\n - Champion user-centered thinking and integrate research and data into decision-making\n\n \n\n\nIN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL, YOU MUST BRING\n\n - 10+ years of experience managing product designers, including senior-level talent and/or managers\n\n - Proven track record of driving product vision and strategy across complex, cross-functional environments\n\n - Craft and Systems Thinking: a high bar for visual, interaction, and systems thinking across experiences, and ability to raise quality through teams rather than individual contribution\n\n - Exceptional cross-functional leadership and influence at senior and executive levels\n\n - Experience building and scaling high-performing design teams and inclusive team cultures\n\n - Deep commitment to user-centered design, with strong partnership with Research and Data\n\n - Experience leading product design for growth and/or demand-generation experiences, with a track record of improving acquisition, conversion, activation, and/or retention through experimentation, data, and user insight\n\n \n\n\nEXPECTED SALARY RANGES\n\n - For candidates living in Ontario and British Columbia, the expected total cash compensation (base salary + variable pay, if applicable) range for this role is currently $226,100.00 - $292,600.00.\n\nActual offered salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as calibrated job level, qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role.\n\nThumbtack embraces diversity. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, provincial, state, or local law. We also will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable law.\n\nThumbtack is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you would like to request a reasonable accommodation for a medical condition or disability during any part of the application process, please contact: recruitingops@thumbtack.com.\n\nFor information about how Thumbtack collects, uses, and shares personal information about job applicants, please see our Job Applicant Privacy Policy https://www.thumbtack.com/job-applicant-privacy-policy.\n\nWe put as much craftsmanship into candidate safety as we do into the hiring experience itself. While scammers may try to impersonate our team, we’ll never ask you for money, banking info, or SSNs during hiring. Check out our blueprint on how to spot the fakes. https://careers.thumbtack.com/recruiting-scams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}